	file.0000000000000001.title: "&6Starwright"
	quest.0079A5D0AEA5DD0B.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The foundries ask for you by name now.\"&r"
		"Pay &660 Contract Seals&r to rise to Specialist."
		"Opens the &eSpecialist shelf&r and two Grand Contracts: &bThe Great Foundry&r and &bCity of Brass&r."
	]
	quest.0079A5D0AEA5DD0B.quest_subtitle: "60 Contract Seals"
	quest.0079A5D0AEA5DD0B.title: "Rank III: Specialist"
	quest.00829F5A41A0FA59.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a Farmer's Delight &6Knife&r. The &6Flint Knife&r is just flint and a stick."
		"A knife harvests &6Straw&r from grass, wheat and rice, and guarantees the bonus drops from animals, like &6Ham&r from pigs."
		"It's also the main tool for the &bCutting Board&r, coming up next."
	]
	quest.00829F5A41A0FA59.quest_subtitle: "A knife for the kitchen"
	quest.00829F5A41A0FA59.title: "Hunt and Gather"
	quest.00D4171060A2AC27.quest_desc: [
		"The Lunar Program opens orders from the Moon and Earth orbit, plus a bulk fuel order."
		"Landing on Mars (&bOne Giant Leap&r) adds the Ares Mining Consortium's Mars orders. Starting the Inner Worlds (&bDurasteel&r) adds the Sunward Expedition's."
		"&eTip:&r most of these goods come home by rocket, so leave room in the hold."
	]
	quest.00D4171060A2AC27.quest_subtitle: "Opens with the Lunar Program"
	quest.00D4171060A2AC27.title: "Tier V: Planetary Orders"
	quest.00F91DF4149279D4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Space Suit Insulation Unit&r: insulation, a Module Base, iron sheets and HDPE."
		"&6Heat-Resistive Unit&r: &6Heat Insulation&r (a Martian Steel Sheet, insulation and Blaze Powder), a Module Base, iron sheets and HDPE."
		"Together they carry you through acid clouds and scorching days."
		"&7Their in-game names may show as raw item keys.&r"
	]
	quest.00F91DF4149279D4.quest_subtitle: "Acid clouds and scorching days"
	quest.00F91DF4149279D4.title: "Insulated"
	quest.012819CB13A544DA.quest_desc: [
		"Copper is the fluid metal. &6Fluid Pipes&r (a copper ingot and a copper sheet) carry liquids, and a &6Mechanical Pump&r (a cogwheel and a pipe) pushes them along while it turns."
		"&6Fluid Tanks&r (copper sheets and a barrel) merge into bigger tanks. A &6Spout&r (copper casing and dried kelp) fills items placed under it."
		"&eTip:&r a pump moves fluid the way its arrow points; use a wrench on it to flip it."
	]
	quest.012819CB13A544DA.quest_subtitle: "Pipes, pumps and tanks"
	quest.012819CB13A544DA.title: "Under Pressure"
	quest.013F5A8F4C1B379D.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The forges run hot and hungry. Send charcoal.\"&r"
		"64 &6Charcoal&r. Smelt logs in a furnace: one log makes one charcoal."
		"&eTip:&r feed the furnace a little of its own output. One charcoal smelts eight logs."
	]
	quest.013F5A8F4C1B379D.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Ironvale Foundry"
	quest.013F5A8F4C1B379D.title: "Charcoal Burn"
	quest.016B8D963E4A5024.quest_desc: [
		"&7Landfall was about surviving. Main Street is about living here.&r"
		""
		"Four short streets branch off this square: &bbuilding&r up top, the &bbank&r to the right, the &bstudio&r down and to the right, and the &bfishing pier&r below."
		"The server runs on &6Numismatics&r coins: Spur 1, Bevel 8, Sprocket 16, Cog 64, Crown 512 and Sun 4096 spurs."
		"Coins come from quests and the Guild’s repeatable contracts. The admin exchange only buys goods that can't be placed, so duplicated ship blocks can't mint money."
		"Spend them in friends' shops, on train fares and at the server's shops."
	]
	quest.016B8D963E4A5024.quest_subtitle: "Homes, shops, studios and the pier"
	quest.016B8D963E4A5024.title: "Town Charter"
	quest.0170694929EAA683.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Bank Terminal&r (a precision mechanism, an industrial iron block and an electron tube) opens your own account or any account you're trusted with."
		"Check balances, switch between accounts and set up &bSub Accounts&r: limited access for chosen players or for automation."
		"Bind an &6Authorized Card&r to a sub-account in the terminal. Put it in a Vendor or Depositor and the takings go straight into that sub-account."
	]
	quest.0170694929EAA683.quest_subtitle: "Balances, sub-accounts and cards"
	quest.0170694929EAA683.title: "Bank Terminal"
	quest.018DDBC98C0721F2.quest_desc: [
		"HV wire carries the most FE the farthest. An &6HV Wire Coil&r is &6Steel Wire&r and &6Aluminium Wire&r on a stick; aluminium comes from &6Bauxite Ore&r."
		"Hang it from &6HV Wire Relays&r. At each end, step it down with an &6HV Transformer&r, then a regular &6Transformer&r for LV machines."
		"The HV Transformer needs an &6Electronic Component&r from the Workbench, plus HV and MV connectors. MV connectors use &6Electrum&r, alloyed from gold and silver in a &bKiln&r."
		"&eGoal:&r run a line between two friends' bases and share the power."
	]
	quest.018DDBC98C0721F2.quest_subtitle: "A line between two bases"
	quest.018DDBC98C0721F2.title: "High Voltage"
	quest.02567E8A5ED9A6F6.quest_desc: [
		"&7Megaproject.&r Build the server a proper spaceport."
		"Two &6Rocket Stations&r to assemble rockets and set their destinations, an &6Auto-Landing Station&r that sets rockets down safely, and two &6Rocket Waypoints&r to mark the landing pads."
		"Right-click a waypoint with a &6Space Atlas&r to add its pad to the atlas."
		"All three are mechanical-crafted. The Auto-Landing Station is built from a third Rocket Station, and waypoints need tungsten from Mercury."
		"&eBonus:&r a CC: Tweaked monitor makes a fine departures board."
	]
	quest.02567E8A5ED9A6F6.quest_subtitle: "Megaproject: a shared launch site"
	quest.02567E8A5ED9A6F6.title: "Spaceport"
	quest.02847F02F1054AD7.quest_desc: [
		"After landing on both Venus and Mercury, visit &bVenus Orbit&r and &bMercury Orbit&r: room for stations above the inner worlds."
		"Bring building blocks: there is nothing to stand on up there."
	]
	quest.02847F02F1054AD7.quest_subtitle: "Orbit the inner worlds"
	quest.02847F02F1054AD7.title: "Station Keeping"
	quest.02ED2ECEFEC2B2A1.quest_desc: [
		"Better Archeology hides seven fossils (wolf, sheep, ocelot, chicken, creeper, villager and guardian), each as a skull and a body."
		"Brush them out of &6Fossiliferous Dirt&r and suspicious blocks at its dig sites, ruins and graves. Iron, diamond and netherite brushes work faster."
		"Craft each skull and body into the full fossil, then build the town a museum."
		"&7Read their tooltips: some fossils change how mobs act near them.&r"
	]
	quest.02ED2ECEFEC2B2A1.quest_subtitle: "Every fossil part found"
	quest.02ED2ECEFEC2B2A1.title: "Paleontologist's Pride"
	quest.032B3828F3F9D59E.quest_desc: [
		"Build the &bWither&r: four &6Soul Sand&r (or soul soil) in a T, topped with three &6Wither Skeleton Skulls&r. The last skull brings it to life."
		"&cIt explodes when it spawns and smashes blocks as it fights.&r Summon it far from anything you love, ideally deep underground."
		"Wither skeletons in Nether fortresses drop the skulls, rarely. Looting helps."
		"It drops a &6Nether Star&r."
	]
	quest.032B3828F3F9D59E.quest_subtitle: "Summon and slay the Wither"
	quest.032B3828F3F9D59E.title: "Withered Away"
	quest.032D224D95D62407.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blast Bricks&r are made from &6Nether Bricks&r, a &6Magma Block&r and &6Bricks&r, so bring Nether supplies home."
		"Build 27 of them into a 3x3x3 cube and hit the centre of one side with the hammer to form the &bCrude Blast Furnace&r."
		"It burns &6Coal Coke&r or charcoal. Coke lasts four times as long."
	]
	quest.032D224D95D62407.quest_subtitle: "The Crude Blast Furnace"
	quest.032D224D95D62407.title: "Really Hot Topic"
	quest.046D64C94361BD1B.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Mechanical Saw&r (an iron sheet, andesite casing and an iron ingot) facing upward cuts whatever is dropped on it or carried past on a belt."
		"Logs become stripped logs and then planks, so a saw keeps your casing line fed without an axe."
		"&cIt hurts. Don't walk over a running saw.&r"
	]
	quest.046D64C94361BD1B.quest_subtitle: "The Mechanical Saw"
	quest.046D64C94361BD1B.title: "Workshop's Most Feared"
	quest.047CCA38F679C4DE.quest_desc: [
		"Create: Marketplace lists every shop on one &bGlobal Market&r board. Right-click your Vendor with a &6Registration Book&r (a book and a cogwheel) to name the shop and publish its offer."
		"Anyone can open the market with its keybind, sort and filter the listings, star favorites and press &bNavigate&r to drop a Xaero waypoint at the shop."
		"&7Price fairly. Your customers know where you live.&r"
	]
	quest.047CCA38F679C4DE.quest_subtitle: "Every shop on one board"
	quest.047CCA38F679C4DE.title: "On the Market"
	quest.04A518B6EF5644B0.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Pie day at the bakery, and our ovens are already full. Can you help?\"&r"
		"3 &6Apple Pies&r and 3 &6Sweet Berry Cheesecakes&r, Farmer's Delight style."
		"Both start from a &6Pie Crust&r (wheat and milk). Craft it with apples, wheat and sugar for a pie, or with sweet berries and more milk for a cheesecake."
		"&eTip:&r a Milk Bucket and four glass bottles make four &6Milk Bottles&r, and either one counts as milk here."
	]
	quest.04A518B6EF5644B0.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Hearthstone Bakery"
	quest.04A518B6EF5644B0.title: "Pie Day"
	quest.04C84E761131DC6D.quest_desc: [
		"Nameless Trinkets are another family of Curios charms from structure chests."
		"Right-click an &bAmethyst Block&r with a trinket you don't want to break it into an &6Unknown Fragment&r."
		"Fragments craft into a &6Mysterious Trinket&r. Use it for a random trinket, with a chance of unlocking an extra trinket slot."
		"Get an Unknown Fragment."
	]
	quest.04C84E761131DC6D.quest_subtitle: "Reroll the trinkets you don't want"
	quest.04C84E761131DC6D.title: "Lucky Charms"
	quest.054DF2C40282112C.quest_desc: [
		"&bYUNG's Better End Island&r rebuilds the central island and its dragon fight."
		"Destroy the &bEnd Crystals&r first, since they heal the dragon. Bring a good bow, blocks to climb with, and slow falling or a water bucket."
		"The dragon is one of the three keys to &bPinnacle&r, with the Ender Guardian and a Mars landing."
		"&eRespawn:&r four End Crystals placed around the exit portal summon it again, so every team can take its turn."
		"&7This also opens the weekly dragon bounty.&r"
	]
	quest.054DF2C40282112C.quest_subtitle: "Slay the Ender Dragon"
	quest.054DF2C40282112C.title: "Free the End"
	quest.056B0AA20A15766B.quest_desc: [
		"Make an &6Iron Pickaxe&r. Iron is the start of almost everything."
		"&6Copper&r and Create's &6Zinc&r are worth mining now too; the Andesite Age needs both."
		"&eTip:&r &bEMI Ores&r shows the heights where every ore spawns."
	]
	quest.056B0AA20A15766B.quest_subtitle: "Isn't it iron pick?"
	quest.056B0AA20A15766B.title: "Iron Age"
	quest.056EDD1A63482DC5.quest_desc: [
		"Process &6Uranium Ore&r into ingots, then enrich the ingots into &6Yellow Cake Uranium&r."
		"Oxidize yellow cake into uranium oxide, add &6Hydrofluoric Acid&r (sulfuric acid and fluorite) in a &bChemical Infuser&r for &6Uranium Hexafluoride&r, then spin it in an &bIsotopic Centrifuge&r for &6Fissile Fuel&r."
		"&cRadiation:&r wear a full &6Hazmat Suit&r around radioactive chemicals, and never break a tank or pipe that holds them."
	]
	quest.056EDD1A63482DC5.quest_subtitle: "The uranium chain"
	quest.056EDD1A63482DC5.title: "Look, Don't Eat"
	quest.05D53CAA0E5AB79C.quest_desc: [
		"Mars grows its own plants. Gather &6Martian Strawberries&r on Mars, and revive &6Dormant Martian Seeds&r in a sequenced assembly to get Mars sprout, palm and tulip seeds."
		"Martian crops grow in &bMars Farmland&r and feed a colony."
		"&eTip:&r a &bMechanical Mixer&r blends Martian Strawberries with vanilla ice cream into strawberry ice cream."
	]
	quest.05D53CAA0E5AB79C.quest_subtitle: "Strawberries on Mars"
	quest.05D53CAA0E5AB79C.title: "Red Garden"
	quest.05F01351A2C3CDDB.quest_desc: [
		"My Nether's Delight brings the Nether into the kitchen: hoglin loins, striderloaf, ghast dishes and fiery spices."
		"&6Hot Wings&r cook in a cooking pot from raw chicken, an onion and a hot spice: &6Blaze Powder&r, a &6Bullet Pepper&r, or &6Pepper Powder&r from cutting a pepper on a cutting board."
		"&eTip:&r Piglins sometimes barter Bullet Peppers."
		"Cook four Hot Wings."
	]
	quest.05F01351A2C3CDDB.quest_subtitle: "Cooking with fire"
	quest.05F01351A2C3CDDB.title: "Nether Cuisine"
	quest.0651F48D2BF568BC.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our history column needs old faces for old places.\"&r"
		"Step (or dig) into a set of &bTrail Ruins&r, half-buried in taiga and jungle, and bring 2 &6Aged Photographs&r."
		"Age a print by crafting it with &6Brown Dye&r and a &6Brush&r."
		"&eTip:&r while you're there, brush the &bSuspicious Gravel&r: trail ruins hide pottery sherds and armour trims."
	]
	quest.0651F48D2BF568BC.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from The Gazette"
	quest.0651F48D2BF568BC.title: "Then and Now"
	quest.0667A3F283FCEF87.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every hunter in the Lodge has a story. Only a few have this one.\"&r"
		""
		"The Lodge's signature order: bring down its five great beasts, in any order. Kills count from the moment this order opens."
		"&bThe Ender Dragon&r, &bThe Leviathan&r, &bThe Harbinger&r and &bScylla&r, as on this board."
		"And &bIgnis&r, the Lodge's oldest grudge. An &6Eye of Flame&r finds its &bBurning Arena&r in the Nether, and the arena's two Ignited Revenants drop the &6Burning Ashes&r that summon it at the &bAltar of Fire&r."
		"Finish all five and your team's names go up over the Lodge's hearth."
	]
	quest.0667A3F283FCEF87.quest_subtitle: "Five great beasts, one ledger"
	quest.0667A3F283FCEF87.title: "Legend of the Lodge"
	quest.06683ECDAF2DE46C.quest_desc: [
		"The &bSlicer&r (a cogwheel, an andesite casing and a turntable) runs cutting-board recipes on rotation. Right-click it with a knife or other tool and feed it from a depot, belt or basin below."
		"Its &bSprinkler&r goes under a fluid pipe and sprays whatever it gets: water works like rain on the farmland below, and &6Liquid Fertilizer&r (organic compost or tree fertilizer mixed with water) fertilizes crops."
		"A &bSpout&r filling Organic Compost with Liquid Fertilizer makes Rich Soil on the spot."
		"Create: Central Kitchen teaches Create to cook: Blaze Burners heat cooking pots, Mechanical Arms serve feasts and pies, Deployers with knives cut, and pipes and Spouts run kegs. Ponder shows each setup."
	]
	quest.06683ECDAF2DE46C.quest_subtitle: "Create takes over the kitchen"
	quest.06683ECDAF2DE46C.title: "Slice \\& Dice"
	quest.077E9AF5C20E460E.quest_desc: [
		"A Mekanism fusion reactor burns deuterium-tritium fuel, ignited by a laser fired through a &6Hohlraum&r."
		"The &6Fusion Reactor Controller&r needs &6Fusion Reactor Frames&r (polonium, ultimate alloy and steel casing). The &6Laser Focus Matrix&r is reactor glass and redstone blocks."
		"It's a big build: Mekanism: Ponders walks you through it."
	]
	quest.077E9AF5C20E460E.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism fusion"
	quest.077E9AF5C20E460E.title: "Star in a Jar"
	quest.0788893B808656F0.quest_desc: [
		"Fly a full starship round trip: Overworld to Mars and back, with an &6Interplanetary Navigator&r aboard."
		"Climb to the trigger altitude, make the jump, land, then jump home the same way."
		"Tick the box when your ship is home."
		"&7Your flagship is now a starship.&r"
	]
	quest.0788893B808656F0.quest_subtitle: "Mars and back by airship"
	quest.0788893B808656F0.title: "Starship"
	quest.07B285EFCFB51911.quest_desc: [
		"&7The planets are walked and the reactor hums. The world keeps turning.&r"
		""
		"Starwright is built to run for years. From here the goals are long ones: collections to finish, megaprojects to build together, and contracts that pay out day after day."
		"Each season the world border grows: a freshly pregenerated ring of land opens past the old edge, ready to explore."
		"&eTip:&r none of this is a race. Pick a project, recruit a friend or two, and chip away at it."
	]
	quest.07B285EFCFB51911.quest_subtitle: "Starwright keeps going"
	quest.07B285EFCFB51911.title: "The Long Game"
	quest.07F271C36B7EC801.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Bring the Guild one thing from every world you have walked, and we will charter the stars in your name.\"&r"
		""
		"A one-time showpiece: four &6Lunar Sapphire Crystals&r from the Moon, four &6Blocks of Martian Steel&r from Mars, eight &6Venus Plumes&r from Venus and four &6Blocks of Tungsten&r from Mercury."
		"A crystal is three Polished Lunar Sapphire with two iron ingots and two redstone. Venus Plumes are found on the Venusian plains and wastes."
		"This order only checks your inventory, so nothing is used up."
	]
	quest.07F271C36B7EC801.quest_subtitle: "Signature order: one from every world"
	quest.07F271C36B7EC801.title: "Charter of the Stars"
	quest.0809C4438D205B11.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The dragon is back. Again.\"&r"
		"Respawn the &bEnder Dragon&r with four &6End Crystals&r (glass, an eye of ender and a ghast tear) set on the exit portal, one on each side, then win the fight once more."
		"Destroy the crystals on the pillars first: they heal it."
		"&eTip:&r YUNG's Better End Island rebuilt the arena, so scout it before you place the last crystal."
	]
	quest.0809C4438D205B11.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.0809C4438D205B11.title: "Bounty: The Ender Dragon"
	quest.0816921BC687EC64.quest_desc: [
		"Build &6Crushing Wheels&r on your Mechanical Crafters (andesite alloy, planks and stone). Place a pair with a one-block gap between them and power them so they spin into each other."
		"Drop raw ore in from above to get &6Crushed Ore&r, usually with a &6Nugget of Experience&r as well. The &bMillstone&r can't crush raw ore."
		"Wash crushed ore with an &bEncased Fan&r blowing through water for nuggets plus a bonus, like redstone from iron. Ore blocks mined with Silk Touch crush into almost two each."
		"&eTip:&r save the experience nuggets. Enchantment Industry turns them into liquid XP."
	]
	quest.0816921BC687EC64.quest_subtitle: "More from every ore"
	quest.0816921BC687EC64.title: "Wheels of Destruction"
	quest.08177422F8DCAA62.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Engineer's Hammer&r (iron, sticks and string) forms every Immersive Engineering multiblock: build the structure, then hit the right block with it."
		"The &6Engineer's Manual&r (a book and a lever) shows every layout and recipe. Keep it close."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r FTB Ultimine is off for the Engineer's Hammer, the Create Wrench and the Mekanism Configurator, so they can't wipe out a row of machines by accident."
	]
	quest.08177422F8DCAA62.quest_subtitle: "Immersive Engineering begins"
	quest.08177422F8DCAA62.title: "HAMMAH!"
	quest.0893C89892611494.quest_desc: [
		"Climb the &bLich Tower&r to face the &6Twilight Lich&r. Break the shields circling it before you can hurt it."
		"Its loot includes magic &6Scepters&r and its trophy."
		"Beating it lifts the curses on the &bSwamp&r and the &bDark Forest&r, and counts toward &bWorld Tier Frontier&r."
	]
	quest.0893C89892611494.quest_subtitle: "Atop the Lich Tower"
	quest.0893C89892611494.title: "The Lich"
	quest.08D14EBD917343BE.quest_desc: [
		"When you die, &bCorpse&r keeps your items in a corpse at that spot. It's an entity, not a block, so it's safe on ships and contraptions."
		"Open it to take everything back. Curios items go straight back into their slots."
		"Corpse also keeps a &bdeath history&r with the place of every death (its key is in Controls), and &b/back&r takes you to where you last died, unless that was on a planet."
		"&eTip:&r Comforts &6Sleeping Bags&r and &6Hammocks&r let you rest on long trips without moving your spawn."
	]
	quest.08D14EBD917343BE.quest_subtitle: "Corpses, not item piles"
	quest.08D14EBD917343BE.title: "When You Fall"
	quest.0914EC6B44B08D06.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Untreated sleepers rot in a season. Ours won't.\"&r"
		"64 &6Treated Wood Planks&r. A &bCoke Oven&r leaves &6Creosote Oil&r behind as it bakes coal. A bucket of it surrounded by eight planks crafts eight treated planks, and a Create &bSpout&r treats one plank per 125 mB."
		"&eTip:&r the oven won't push creosote out by itself, so pump it into a tank."
	]
	quest.0914EC6B44B08D06.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Northline Railways"
	quest.0914EC6B44B08D06.title: "Treated Timber"
	quest.092FFC2628E76BD3.quest_desc: [
		"Three Twilight materials make strong gear early on."
		"&6Ironwood:&r craft &6Liveroot&r, raw iron and a gold nugget into Raw Ironwood, then smelt it."
		"&6Steeleaf&r and &6Armor Shards&r come from the forest's creatures and chests. Shards craft into a cluster that smelts into &6Knightmetal&r."
		"&eTip:&r EMI Loot shows where each one drops."
	]
	quest.092FFC2628E76BD3.quest_subtitle: "Ironwood, Steeleaf, Knightmetal"
	quest.092FFC2628E76BD3.title: "Forest Metals"
	quest.09483D3217845161.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Mechanical Mixer&r (andesite casing, a whisk and a cogwheel) over a &6Basin&r mixes: andesite and nuggets into alloy in bulk, flour and water into dough."
		"A &6Mechanical Press&r over a basin &bcompacts&r: two flint, gravel and a little lava into andesite, nine snow blocks into ice, or seeds into plant oil."
		"&7Some recipes need heat from a Blaze Burner under the basin. That comes with the Brass Age.&r"
	]
	quest.09483D3217845161.quest_subtitle: "The basin does the work"
	quest.09483D3217845161.title: "Mixing It Up"
	quest.0948C24073235F87.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hot Air Envelopes&r (white wool and a stick, by hand or with a Deployer) build the balloon. They must enclose an airtight space."
		"A &6Hot Air Burner&r below the balloon fills it from the top down."
		"&eTip:&r coloured envelopes give a fleet its livery, and splashing (a fan through water) washes them white again."
	]
	quest.0948C24073235F87.quest_subtitle: "Hot air lifts"
	quest.0948C24073235F87.title: "Head in the Clouds"
	quest.0975295FEE24016D.quest_desc: [
		"Mix sugar cane, bamboo or saplings with water in a &bMechanical Mixer&r for &6Pulp&r, then press it into &6Cardboard&r."
		"A &6Packager&r (cardboard block, iron and redstone) sits against an inventory. A redstone signal packs the contents into a package, and a package fed back in is unpacked."
		"Put a sign on the packager and every package it makes carries the sign's text as its address."
		"&eTip:&r Create: Additional Logistics adds the &6Package Editor&r, which rewrites addresses by rule, and the &6Package Accelerator&r, which speeds up a packager at the cost of stress."
	]
	quest.0975295FEE24016D.quest_subtitle: "Cardboard boxes with an address"
	quest.0975295FEE24016D.title: "Post Production"
	quest.0A31CAD327306032.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Bulk order: every Propeller Bearing in the fleet wants more sails.\"&r"
		"1,024 &6Windmill Sails&r. Each craft of wool, two sticks and Andesite Alloy makes two."
		"Propeller Bearings spin their sails as one big propeller, and more sails push harder."
		"&eTip:&r a Mechanical Crafter or Molecular Assembler line can run this all week. Send the output into a &bTask Screen&r."
	]
	quest.0A31CAD327306032.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Skyward Freight"
	quest.0A31CAD327306032.title: "A Thousand Sails"
	quest.0A83231FB2A877F2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Steel Casing&r is the frame of nearly every Mekanism machine, so plan to make a lot of it."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r its recipe is changed to need Create &6Precision Mechanisms&r and IE &6Steel&r. Check EMI for the exact layout."
		"Almost Unified keeps one steel, so the infuser's steel dust smelts into the same IE steel ingot."
	]
	quest.0A83231FB2A877F2.quest_subtitle: "Steel Casing"
	quest.0A83231FB2A877F2.title: "The Perfect Foundation"
	quest.0B113AA2F053AA7F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Explorer's Compass&r is a compass with cobwebs and cracked stone bricks. Its recipe opens with the Explorer's Licence."
		"Pick a structure from its list and it points to the nearest one it can find."
		"&cLandmarks are off the list.&r When Dungeons Arise sites and other landmarks are blacklisted, so finding them is still a real search. Watch the skyline."
	]
	quest.0B113AA2F053AA7F.quest_subtitle: "Point the way to a structure"
	quest.0B113AA2F053AA7F.title: "Seeker's Compass"
	quest.0BFDEBE829D5B60C.quest_desc: [
		"Rockets burn &6biofuel&r, &6hydrogen&r, &6liquid hydrogen&r, &6liquid hydrocarbons&r or &6methane&r, held in Fluid Tanks on the rocket. &cDiesel, gasoline and biodiesel only run engines;&r they will not lift a rocket."
		"The first fuel is &6Biofuel&r: three dried kelp and a bone meal in a heated basin under a &bMechanical Press&r. Crafts \\& Additions bioethanol burns too, and Mekanism hydrogen condensed into a liquid in a &bRotary Condensentrator&r carries twice the energy."
		"Each trip’s cost depends on gravity and distance. The station shows what you need."
		"&eTip:&r carry spare fuel. The rocket is your only way home."
	]
	quest.0BFDEBE829D5B60C.quest_subtitle: "Biofuel, hydrogen or better"
	quest.0BFDEBE829D5B60C.title: "Fuel the Bird"
	quest.0BFDF7280E76E789.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Grappling Hook&r latches onto a block and pulls you to it: up cliffs, across ravines and out of dungeon shafts."
		"Make an &6Iron Hook&r from iron ingots and nuggets, then add a &6Chain&r and a &6Stick&r."
		"Golden and diamond hooks craft the same way and reach further. A smithing table upgrades a diamond hook to netherite, the longest of all."
	]
	quest.0BFDF7280E76E789.quest_subtitle: "A grappling hook for the vertical"
	quest.0BFDF7280E76E789.title: "Hook, Line and Cliff"
	quest.0C0B479418473217.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The copper halls fascinate our curators. Bring us keys and rods.\"&r"
		"Step into a &bTrial Chamber&r and bring 3 &6Trial Keys&r and 4 &6Breeze Rods&r."
		"Beat a &bTrial Spawner&r's waves and it ejects a reward for each player who fought: often a Trial Key, otherwise Wind Charges. Breezes drop breeze rods."
		"&eTip:&r spawners wake again after a cooldown, so one chamber can fill this order day after day."
	]
	quest.0C0B479418473217.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Lantern Museum"
	quest.0C0B479418473217.title: "Keys to the Vaults"
	quest.0C4CB939F4FE0DF1.quest_desc: [
		"&7The ship's stores won't last forever. Time to find food that grows.&r"
		""
		"Wild crops dot the Overworld. Farmer's Delight's &6Wild Cabbages&r grow on beaches, &6Wild Onions&r in temperate lands, &6Wild Tomatoes&r in hot, dry biomes and &6Wild Rice&r in wet ones."
		"Farm \\& Charm adds wild &6lettuce, barley, oats, corn, strawberries&r and more across plains, forests, rivers and savannas."
		"Break them for seeds and produce, then bring home a Farmer's Delight &6Cabbage Seed&r, &6Tomato Seed&r, &6Onion&r or &6Rice&r."
		"&eTip:&r Farm \\& Charm has its own tomatoes and onions. They work in recipes that take any onion or tomato, but this quest wants the Farmer's Delight ones. The tooltip names the mod."
	]
	quest.0C4CB939F4FE0DF1.quest_subtitle: "Forage first, farm later"
	quest.0C4CB939F4FE0DF1.title: "Crops of the Wild"
	quest.0C5DF95C9B19EF84.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"New carriages need casing, and the yard wants spare sheet.\"&r"
		"16 &6Train Casing&r and 16 &6Sturdy Sheets&r. Crush &6Obsidian&r into powder, then sequence it: a &bSpout&r adds 500 mB of lava and a &bMechanical Press&r flattens it twice. A sturdy sheet used on placed &6Brass Casing&r makes Train Casing."
		"&eTip:&r crushing wheels often hand the obsidian back, so one block gives several powders."
	]
	quest.0C5DF95C9B19EF84.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Northline Railways"
	quest.0C5DF95C9B19EF84.title: "Rolling Stock"
	quest.0C8CE18F174D5B41.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Crafters&r are made from an &6Electron Tube&r, &6Brass Casing&r and a &6Crafting Table&r. Together they craft recipes bigger than 3x3."
		"Place them in a grid shaped like the recipe and turn their arrows with a &bWrench&r so everything flows into one last crafter. Then give them rotation."
		"Put one ingredient in each crafter. Crafting starts when every slot is filled, or right away on a redstone pulse."
		"They build &6Crushing Wheels&r, the Crafts \\& Additions &6Alternator&r, &6Waystones&r and the &6Contraption Claim Block&r, and much later, rocket parts."
	]
	quest.0C8CE18F174D5B41.quest_subtitle: "Recipes too big for a table"
	quest.0C8CE18F174D5B41.title: "Automated Assembly"
	quest.0CC701FE1F1A9938.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Girders for a hundred buildings. Steel, and lots of it.\"&r"
		"1,024 &6Steel Ingots&r."
		"A bank of &bImproved Blast Furnaces&r with Create feeding them iron and coke keeps up; Mekanism's steel route works too once it is running."
		"&eTip:&r one Task Screen at the end of the smelting line is enough."
	]
	quest.0CC701FE1F1A9938.quest_subtitle: "Monthly Grand Contract from Ironvale Foundry"
	quest.0CC701FE1F1A9938.title: "The Great Foundry"
	quest.0CD907845D35EE39.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Vendor&r (brass casing, an electron tube and framed glass) runs a shop while you're away. Sneak and use it to set the item, the price in coins and the mode: sell to customers or buy from them."
		"Fill its stock slots to sell; in buy mode, give it coins to pay customers with. Put a &6Bank Card&r in it and payments go straight into that account."
		"Let friends manage the shop by putting their &6ID Card&r in its trust list."
		"&eTip:&r Andesite and Brass &bDepositors&r take coins for a redstone pulse, which makes train fares and toll gates easy."
	]
	quest.0CD907845D35EE39.quest_subtitle: "A shop that runs itself"
	quest.0CD907845D35EE39.title: "Open for Business"
	quest.0D8B5522DBF8A010.quest_desc: [
		"&bSpice of Life&r rewards a varied diet: eating new foods earns permanent extra hearts: one at each of eight milestones, from 10 to 220 different foods."
		"The milestones are spread over the whole food tree, so the last hearts come from the fancy dishes much later."
		"The &6Food Book&r (a book and a carrot) lists the foods you've tasted and the ones you haven't tried yet."
	]
	quest.0D8B5522DBF8A010.quest_subtitle: "Variety is the spice of life"
	quest.0D8B5522DBF8A010.title: "Food Journal"
	quest.0D99523D75AB4CD4.quest_desc: [
		"&bCC: Tweaked&r computers run Lua programs that you write in-game. Craft a &6Computer&r from stone, redstone and a glass pane, place it and right-click it to open the terminal."
		""
		"Type &bhelp&r to look around, &blua&r to try code live, and &bedit startup.lua&r to write a program that runs every time the computer boots."
		"HTTP is on with the default rules (no local or private addresses), so &bwget&r and &bpastebin&r can fetch scripts from the web."
		""
		"&7Every quest in this chapter is optional: small projects that put a computer on top of each age."
	]
	quest.0D99523D75AB4CD4.quest_subtitle: "Your first Lua computer"
	quest.0D99523D75AB4CD4.title: "Hello, World"
	quest.0DFC7FE67EB48BB0.quest_desc: [
		"Use the &6Orb of Prophecy&r on the portal frame in the ruins to open the &bStarlight Portal&r."
		"&bEternal Starlight&r is a starlit dimension with its own biomes, creatures, metals and bosses."
		"&eTip:&r more Orbs can be crafted from &6Blue Starlight Crystal Shards&r and glass, so spares are easy once you're through."
		"&7The two Starlight boss quests after this one are optional.&r"
	]
	quest.0DFC7FE67EB48BB0.quest_subtitle: "Through the Starlight Portal"
	quest.0DFC7FE67EB48BB0.title: "Sky of a Million Stars"
	quest.0E1CA585142324C7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Salvaging Table&r breaks unwanted affix gear into rarity materials: Mysterious Scrap Metal, Timeworn Fabric, Luminous Crystal Shards, Arcane Sands and Godforged Pearls."
		"Its recipe needs &6Gem Dust&r. Your first dust comes from dropping any Apotheosis gem on the ground and letting a falling &banvil&r land on it. After that, salvage spare gems for dust."
		"Plain vanilla tools and armor salvage back into some of their materials too."
	]
	quest.0E1CA585142324C7.quest_subtitle: "Scrap it for parts"
	quest.0E1CA585142324C7.title: "Salvage Yard"
	quest.0E740526C9A4DBB2.quest_desc: [
		"An &6Ender Modem&r (eight gold around an Eye of Ender) has no range limit and works across dimensions, so every base can join one rednet network."
		""
		"Craft an &6Advanced Pocket Computer&r (gold, a golden apple and a glass pane), then place an Ender Modem directly above it in the crafting grid to fit it."
		"Now you can check the reactor, dispatch trains and call the cargo ship from anywhere. Base computers only answer while their chunks are loaded."
		"&7Hint: rednet.broadcast() from the pocket, rednet.receive() at each base."
	]
	quest.0E740526C9A4DBB2.quest_subtitle: "Every base, one network, in your pocket"
	quest.0E740526C9A4DBB2.title: "Control Room"
	quest.0E842E49E98E9D39.quest_desc: [
		"The &bNether Gauntlet&r sleeps in a big arena low in the Nether, among the lava."
		"Break the &6Ancient Carved Blackstone&r in the middle of the arena to wake it."
		"It drops a &6Blazing Eye&r and some &6Ancient Debris&r."
	]
	quest.0E842E49E98E9D39.quest_subtitle: "BoMD's Nether Gauntlet"
	quest.0E842E49E98E9D39.title: "Through the Gauntlet"
	quest.0F6D6C242DA5E5F2.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"A full house this afternoon. Two pots on, please.\"&r"
		"8 &6Rooibos Tea&r and 8 &6Strawberry Tea&r."
		"Rooibos grows wild in savannas; plant its leaves to farm it. Brew a leaf with a glass bottle in a HerbalBrews &bTea Kettle&r set on a stove and topped up with water."
		"Strawberry Tea is Farm \\& Charm's: two strawberries and a water bottle in its &bCooking Pot&r over heat, served into a glass bottle."
		"&eTip:&r rooibos needs only the stove's heat, unlike green tea and coffee."
	]
	quest.0F6D6C242DA5E5F2.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Lantern Row Tea House"
	quest.0F6D6C242DA5E5F2.title: "Afternoon Tea"
	quest.0FDC134C3C72D50A.quest_desc: [
		"Daily orders farther afield: the Twilight Forest, the Nether, Trial Chambers and trail ruins."
		"Each pays &6100 XP&r, &61 sprocket&r and &62 Contract Seals&r."
		"The Twilight and Nether orders also wait on &bInto the Twilight&r and &bReturn to the Nether&r."
	]
	quest.0FDC134C3C72D50A.quest_subtitle: "Opens with Andesite Works"
	quest.0FDC134C3C72D50A.title: "Tier II Orders"
	quest.1052E90BE14BA51D.quest_desc: [
		"&6LV Wire Connectors&r (copper and terracotta) mount on machines and posts. Right-click one with an &6LV Wire Coil&r, then another, to string a wire."
		"LV wire moves FE between Alternators, batteries and machines. Make copper wire from a copper plate with &6Wire Cutters&r, or on the Rolling Mill."
		"IE's &6Kinetic Dynamo&r makes FE from IE windmills and water wheels. It doesn't take Create rotation."
		"&eTip:&r Wire Cutters also take a wire down again."
	]
	quest.1052E90BE14BA51D.quest_subtitle: "Low voltage, high hopes"
	quest.1052E90BE14BA51D.title: "Birds on a Wire"
	quest.105B45CFB4ED747F.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"A line to every corner of the map, and we need the track yesterday.\"&r"
		"1,024 &6Train Track&r, 32 &6Train Casings&r and 32 &6Train Signals&r."
		"Track comes out of a &bsequenced assembly&r line from sleepers, so it automates well."
		"&eTip:&r point the line's output at a &6Task Screen&r and let it run between visits."
	]
	quest.105B45CFB4ED747F.quest_subtitle: "Monthly Grand Contract from Northline Railways"
	quest.105B45CFB4ED747F.title: "The Great Railway"
	quest.1066B9786FAF123B.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every navigator we build eats sapphire. Polish us thirty-two.\"&r"
		"Lunar Sapphire geodes on the Moon grow clusters on budding blocks, like amethyst. &cClusters only drop with Silk Touch;&r the geode's Lunar Sapphire Blocks drop normally."
		"Crush clusters or blocks into &6Lunar Sapphire Shards&r with &bCrushing Wheels&r, then polish each shard with Sand Paper, by hand or with a &bDeployer&r."
		"&eTip:&r Moon Sand Paper (moon sand and paper) polishes just as well."
	]
	quest.1066B9786FAF123B.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Lunar Survey Corps"
	quest.1066B9786FAF123B.title: "Polished Moonlight"
	quest.1096AB9C2C9FA20D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Deployer&r (Andesite Casing, a &6Brass Hand&r and an &6Electron Tube&r) is a mechanical player hand. Give it rotation and it uses whatever it holds on the block in front of it."
		"It places blocks, uses tools, attacks mobs, and applies items to things passing on a belt or sitting on a depot."
		"A row of deployers runs &bsequenced assembly&r, each one adding a part as the item goes by. That is how Precision Mechanisms are built."
		"&eTip:&r right-click a deployer with an item to hand it over. A wrench switches it between using and punching."
	]
	quest.1096AB9C2C9FA20D.quest_subtitle: "A hand that never tires"
	quest.1096AB9C2C9FA20D.title: "Artificial Intelligence"
	quest.11239812938F0BB8.quest_desc: [
		"&bDungeons and Taverns&r fills the mid-range ring with taverns, crypts, ruins and manors."
		"The &6Illager Manor&r is a grand house held by illagers, with loot to match. Find one and step inside."
		"&eTip:&r tavern &bcartographers&r sell maps to sites like this one, so stop in for a drink first."
	]
	quest.11239812938F0BB8.quest_subtitle: "An illager estate"
	quest.11239812938F0BB8.title: "Mind Your Manors"
	quest.119B7444DDC566D3.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Bulk order: we're stockpiling fuel for the Mars run.\"&r"
		"64,000 mB of &6Liquid Hydrocarbons&r, which pack more energy per bucket than hydrogen or biofuel."
		"A &bsuperheated&r Mixer makes it from three Sodium Catalysts, carbon gas and water; a heated Mixer makes it from carbon gas and sodium."
		"A &6Sodium Catalyst&r is Salt filled with lava by a &bSpout&r; crush basalt or Mars gravel for salt. Compact three coal over heat for carbon gas."
		"&eTip:&r a Task Screen at the end of the mixer line fills this on its own."
	]
	quest.119B7444DDC566D3.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Ares Mining Consortium"
	quest.119B7444DDC566D3.title: "Fuel Depot for the Mars Run"
	quest.11A5BA7CB88A398C.quest_desc: [
		"One random pick from the &6Explorer's Cache&r: trail food, torches, ender pearls, empty maps, a name tag, a spyglass, leads, a sleeping bag, a saddle or XP bottles, among others."
		"&7A lucky dip for the road.&r"
	]
	quest.11A5BA7CB88A398C.quest_subtitle: "5 seals"
	quest.11A5BA7CB88A398C.title: "Explorer's Cache"
	quest.11CE60A5DA48E7CF.quest_desc: [
		"Both inner worlds walked, the suit space-rated, antimatter in hand."
		"Bring home four &6Blocks of Tungsten&r and an &6Antimatter Pellet&r to prove it."
		"&eNext:&r Ascension, where the world keeps going."
	]
	quest.11CE60A5DA48E7CF.quest_subtitle: "The inner worlds walked"
	quest.11CE60A5DA48E7CF.title: "Sunward"
	quest.1245D093CCCCF2E7.quest_desc: [
		"&7The ground is getting crowded. Look up.&r"
		""
		"The Immersive Aircraft &6Biplane&r is a &6Hull&r, an &6Engine&r and a &6Propeller&r."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r those parts need Create components. Check EMI for the exact recipes."
		"The engine burns furnace fuel such as coal or charcoal."
		"The server allows flight and &6Too Fast&r stops speed kicks, so open the throttle."
	]
	quest.1245D093CCCCF2E7.quest_subtitle: "A biplane built on Create parts"
	quest.1245D093CCCCF2E7.title: "Take to the Skies"
	quest.1354CCEEEE48250F.quest_desc: [
		"&7A forest where it is always dusk, full of bosses and their treasures.&r"
		""
		"Dig a &b2x2 pool of water&r set into grass, ring it with flowers or other small plants, and toss a &6Diamond&r into the water. Lightning opens the portal."
		"Each boss unlocks the next part of the forest. Skip ahead and the land pushes back with curses and barriers."
		"&cBarriers check each player's own progress,&r so a friend who missed a boss fight may still be locked out."
		"Step through the portal to finish this quest."
	]
	quest.1354CCEEEE48250F.quest_subtitle: "A pool, some flowers, a diamond"
	quest.1354CCEEEE48250F.title: "Into the Twilight"
	quest.13E231C9A89E1E78.quest_desc: [
		"Press seeds into &6Plant Oil&r with a &bMechanical Press&r over a &bBasin&r."
		"Ferment crops with bone meal into &6Ethanol&r in a basin topped with a &6Basin Lid&r, or in a &bBulk Fermenter&r. EMI lists what ferments."
		"Mix plant oil and ethanol in a &bMechanical Mixer&r for &6Biodiesel&r. IE's Squeezer, Fermenter and Refinery make the same fluids in this pack."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r the Bulk Fermenter is ground-only and can't go on a ship. Aboard, use a Basin and Basin Lid, or bring fuel by pipe, package or train."
	]
	quest.13E231C9A89E1E78.quest_subtitle: "Biodiesel from the farm"
	quest.13E231C9A89E1E78.title: "Grow Your Own Fuel"
	quest.13ED776A943E2067.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Backpack&r is a chest, leather and string."
		"Tier it up in the crafting grid with copper, then iron, gold and a diamond. Netherite goes on at a smithing table."
		"Upgrades start from an &6Upgrade Base&r (iron, leather and string): magnet, feeding, refill, crafting, tanks and more. EMI shows each recipe."
		"A backpack sits in your Curios &bback slot&r. In Starwright that slot holds two items, so a backpack and (later) Icarus wings fit together."
	]
	quest.13ED776A943E2067.quest_subtitle: "Room for the road"
	quest.13ED776A943E2067.title: "Pack a Bag"
	quest.145AC34DB89305B1.quest_desc: [
		"Titanium ore only exists on other worlds, but Create can make the metal here."
		"Crush &6Obsidian&r into &6Powdered Obsidian&r and turn it into &6Sturdy Sheets&r, as you did for trains. A &bsequenced assembly&r then turns each sheet into a &6Titanium Ingot&r. EMI shows every step."
		"A &bMechanical Press&r flattens ingots into &6Titanium Sheets&r. Rockets eat both."
		"&eTip:&r automate this line now. You'll mine titanium on the Moon, but first you have to get there."
	]
	quest.145AC34DB89305B1.quest_subtitle: "Space metal, made at home"
	quest.145AC34DB89305B1.title: "Titanium from Obsidian"
	quest.14BEDB8DABEBFAC8.quest_desc: [
		"Set the atlas to the &bMoon&r, fuel up, suit up and launch. Then step out onto the surface."
		"&cWaystones, /home and /tpa can't reach planets.&r The rocket is your way there and your way home."
		"&eTip:&r pack spare air, food, a pickaxe and blocks for a landing pad."
	]
	quest.14BEDB8DABEBFAC8.quest_subtitle: "Boots on the Moon"
	quest.14BEDB8DABEBFAC8.title: "One Small Step"
	quest.14F79BB6FEB7BC1E.quest_desc: [
		"An &6Encased Fan&r (andesite casing, a propeller and a shaft) blows items through whatever is in front of it."
		"Through water it &bwashes&r, through fire it &bsmokes&r food, through lava it &bblasts&r (smelts), and through soul fire it &bhaunts&r."
		"Washing turns gravel into flint and iron nuggets, sand into clay, and red sand into gold nuggets."
		"&eTip:&r aim the fan along a belt, or at items lying on the ground."
	]
	quest.14F79BB6FEB7BC1E.quest_subtitle: "Wash, smoke, blast"
	quest.14F79BB6FEB7BC1E.title: "Processing by Particle"
	quest.150236B5BB135CFA.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"We pay for every brute that never reaches our walls.\"&r"
		"Kill a &bPiglin Brute&r and 20 &bZombified Piglins&r. Brutes never respawn in bastions, so the steady source is a &bGateway&r."
		"Craft a Gate Pearl for the &6Gateway of the Hellish Fortress&r (rotten flesh, a wither skeleton skull, gold blocks, an eye of ender and blaze rods) and use it on open ground. Its last wave is a brute called the &cButcher&r."
		"Clearing it pays fortress loot and a &6Wither Skeleton spawner&r."
		"&cA failed gate explodes and starts fires,&r so open it well away from your base."
	]
	quest.150236B5BB135CFA.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from Bastion Watch"
	quest.150236B5BB135CFA.title: "The Butcher's Gate"
	quest.163E51F6BD4F7ED6.quest_desc: [
		"Mutant monsters spawn rarely wherever their ordinary cousins do, in any dimension."
		"A downed &bMutant Zombie&r gets back up unless you set it on fire. The &bMutant Creeper&r leaps and explodes, so keep your distance."
		"Spoils include the &6Hulk Hammer&r and bones for &6Mutant Skeleton armour&r."
	]
	quest.163E51F6BD4F7ED6.quest_subtitle: "Zombie, skeleton and creeper"
	quest.163E51F6BD4F7ED6.title: "Mutant Hunter"
	quest.1648B6A532E716E7.quest_desc: [
		"Everyday stock for a new contractor: trail food, ender pearls, a horse kit and the odd lucky cache."
		"&7Higher shelves open as your team buys Contractor Ranks in the Guild Hall.&r"
	]
	quest.1648B6A532E716E7.quest_subtitle: "Open to every contractor"
	quest.1648B6A532E716E7.title: "Registered Shelf"
	quest.1659B281D9981361.quest_desc: [
		"Trade with a tavern &bCartographer&r for a &6quest map&r. It points the way to another Dungeons and Taverns site."
		"It's a built-in quest loop: each map leads somewhere worth clearing."
	]
	quest.1659B281D9981361.quest_subtitle: "Optional: a map to the next site"
	quest.1659B281D9981361.title: "Call for Adventure"
	quest.167A0F6F177C7011.quest_desc: [
		"One random pick: steel, osmium, tin, lead, enriched carbon, fluorite, certus quartz, silicon, HDPE sheets, diamonds or obsidian."
		"Opens once your team brings its &6Reactor Online&r."
	]
	quest.167A0F6F177C7011.quest_subtitle: "10 seals"
	quest.167A0F6F177C7011.title: "Reactor Crate"
	quest.16B59EF14DC1521E.quest_desc: [
		"&bEcliptic Seasons&r runs a year of 24 solar terms with regional weather."
		"Here it's set to the &bEcology&r level: winter snow is only visual, and no crop is slowed by the season, so farms grow all year."
		"Craft a &6Calendar&r (paper, a book and a feather) to see the current term."
	]
	quest.16B59EF14DC1521E.quest_subtitle: "Twenty-four solar terms"
	quest.16B59EF14DC1521E.title: "Turn of the Seasons"
	quest.1759A8DF4D620881.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Another serpent has nested in a courtyard. The Rangers want it gone.\"&r"
		"Kill a &bNaga&r. Each &bNaga Courtyard&r holds only one, so every bounty means &cfinding a fresh courtyard&r."
		"Courtyards are common landmarks in the forest, and a &6Magic Map&r marks them."
		"&eTip:&r make it ram something hard to stun it, then strike."
	]
	quest.1759A8DF4D620881.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from the Twilight Rangers"
	quest.1759A8DF4D620881.title: "Courtyard Serpent"
	quest.17B639D64199C626.quest_desc: [
		"Build a &bFluid Tank&r, put fuelled &bBlaze Burners&r under it and pump in water with a &bMechanical Pump&r. Now it is a &bboiler&r."
		"Place a &6Steam Engine&r (Golden Sheet, Copper Block and Andesite Alloy) on the tank's side, then right-click the engine with a &6Shaft&r to take the power off."
		"More heat, more water and a bigger tank raise the boiler level, and higher levels run more engines. A superheated burner counts as two."
		"&eTip:&r look at the tank wearing &6Engineer's Goggles&r to see what is holding the boiler back."
	]
	quest.17B639D64199C626.quest_subtitle: "Boilers and steam engines"
	quest.17B639D64199C626.title: "The Powerhouse"
	quest.17D61E13C3150BBC.quest_desc: [
		"&bAncient Cities&r lie in the &bDeep Dark&r, far below the surface. Their chests are rich, and Lootr gives each player their own."
		"&cDon't wake the Warden yet.&r Crouch to move quietly past &bsculk sensors&r and &bshriekers&r. Every shriek raises the warning level, and the fourth brings the Warden."
		"Deeper and Darker adds a &6Warden Carapace&r to some Ancient City chests."
		"&7Opens at World Tier Ascent.&r"
	]
	quest.17D61E13C3150BBC.quest_subtitle: "Find an Ancient City"
	quest.17D61E13C3150BBC.title: "A Metropolis of Restless Souls"
	quest.17E09617317FB62C.quest_desc: [
		"Charge &6Certus Quartz Crystals&r in the &bCharger&r. A Crafts \\& Additions &bTesla Coil&r also charges them on a depot or belt below it."
		"Throw a &6Charged Certus Quartz Crystal&r, &6Redstone&r and &6Nether Quartz&r into water together and they become two &6Fluix Crystals&r."
		"&eTip:&r a &bMechanical Mixer&r over a &bBasin&r with water mixes the same recipe in bulk, no heat needed."
	]
	quest.17E09617317FB62C.quest_subtitle: "Charge, splash, fluix"
	quest.17E09617317FB62C.title: "Unnatural"
	quest.181CEE5D2365AA30.quest_desc: [
		"Every Twilight boss drops a &6Trophy&r."
		"Find the &bTrophy Pedestal&r in the ruins of the Dark Forest and set a boss trophy on it."
		"&7Spare trophies make fine mantelpieces back home.&r"
	]
	quest.181CEE5D2365AA30.quest_subtitle: "Put a trophy on display"
	quest.181CEE5D2365AA30.title: "Trophied Champion"
	quest.18480AC22EFD3172.quest_desc: [
		"Find a planet in the night sky, keep &6Paper&r on you and hold use with the &6Telescope&r until you get an &6Astronomical Reading&r."
		"Readings of different planets, and readings from different days, are worth more science than repeats of the same one."
		"&eTip:&r take a reading every night you can. Variety fills the atlas faster."
	]
	quest.18480AC22EFD3172.quest_subtitle: "Your first page of science"
	quest.18480AC22EFD3172.title: "Astronomical Reading"
	quest.1851057F2197CD5B.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Diesel Engine&r turns liquid fuel into strong rotation. Pipe in diesel, gasoline, biodiesel, ethanol or plant oil to start it; a redstone signal stops it."
		"&6Modular Diesel Engines&r stack into one long engine, and every block you add raises its output."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r the Huge Diesel Engine is disabled. Regular and modular engines are fine."
		"&eTip:&r engines also take upgrades. Their Ponder scene shows how."
	]
	quest.1851057F2197CD5B.quest_subtitle: "Fuel into rotation"
	quest.1851057F2197CD5B.title: "Diesel Power"
	quest.18CCDEC4E0BFF5A7.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"We're wiring a new exchange floor. Engineering processors, please.\"&r"
		"16 &6Engineering Processors&r. In an &bInscriber&r, print a &6Diamond&r with the Engineering Press and &6Silicon&r with the Silicon Press, then press both prints together with &6Redstone&r."
		"&eTip:&r ExtendedAE's &bCircuit Slicer&r cuts prints from whole blocks and speeds up a processor line."
	]
	quest.18CCDEC4E0BFF5A7.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Lattice Data Exchange"
	quest.18CCDEC4E0BFF5A7.title: "Processor Order"
	quest.190AD6D34C19EEB9.quest_desc: [
		"YUNG's Better Dungeons rebuilds the old monster room and digs spider caves, catacombs and undead fortresses underground. Better Mineshafts redoes the mineshafts, too."
		"Find an upgraded monster room."
		"Lootr gives every player their own loot, so clear it together and everyone still gets a full chest."
	]
	quest.190AD6D34C19EEB9.quest_subtitle: "YUNG's dungeons"
	quest.190AD6D34C19EEB9.title: "Quite the Renovation"
	quest.191EA4C1D0B2B6E8.quest_desc: [
		"The Guild's vault: the Silence trim, the Everlasting Upgrade and Nether Stars."
		"&7Opens when your team holds the Legend rank. Patron of the Guild waits beyond it.&r"
	]
	quest.191EA4C1D0B2B6E8.quest_subtitle: "Opens at Legend rank"
	quest.191EA4C1D0B2B6E8.title: "Legend Shelf"
	quest.196C6B302EA46CE5.quest_desc: [
		"A growing workshop soon needs more stress capacity than a few water wheels give."
		"Build &6Windmill Sails&r (andesite alloy, sticks and wool) onto a &6Windmill Bearing&r (wooden slabs, stone and a shaft), then right-click the bearing to start it. Its Ponder shows the layout."
		"More sails mean more stress capacity, and a windmill works anywhere."
	]
	quest.196C6B302EA46CE5.quest_subtitle: "More power for a bigger shop"
	quest.196C6B302EA46CE5.title: "A Mild Breeze"
	quest.198F41CE91FCF066.quest_desc: [
		"Build a &6Photo Analyzer&r from a &6Lightroom&r, iron, redstone and a diamond."
		"Give it a printed photo of the night sky. It studies the shot and files the object in your cosmic catalogue."
		"The first study of each object pays out, so every new star is worth a night outside."
		"&7Filling the whole catalogue is a long-term goal in Ascension.&r"
	]
	quest.198F41CE91FCF066.quest_subtitle: "Name what you photographed"
	quest.198F41CE91FCF066.title: "First Light"
	quest.19D89804B0757533.quest_desc: [
		"One random pick of Create stock: zinc, andesite casings, iron or copper sheets, cogwheels, shafts, belts or pipes, or quartz, gold or redstone."
		"Opens once your team finishes &6Andesite Works&r."
	]
	quest.19D89804B0757533.quest_subtitle: "6 seals"
	quest.19D89804B0757533.title: "Workshop Crate"
	quest.19EF7D59B3336FA7.quest_desc: [
		"Keep feeding readings into the atlas until it shows the &bMoon&r as unlocked."
		"Then assemble a &6Targeting Computer&r: a &bsequenced assembly&r that starts from an &6Iron Sheet&r. EMI lists the steps."
		"Tick the box once the Moon is charted and the computer is built."
		"&eNext:&r Liftoff turns these parts into a rocket."
	]
	quest.19EF7D59B3336FA7.quest_subtitle: "The first destination"
	quest.19EF7D59B3336FA7.title: "Chart the Moon"
	quest.19FEF02447A6E938.quest_desc: [
		"&7The reactor hums. Time to give the base a brain.&r"
		""
		"Applied Energistics 2 starts at a &bmeteorite&r: a sphere of &6Sky Stone&r that usually leaves a big crater. Its core holds a &6Mysterious Cube&r, packed in certus quartz and &6Budding Certus&r."
		"&eTip:&r a vanilla compass charged in an AE2 &bCharger&r (iron and copper) becomes a &6Meteorite Compass&r that points to the nearest cube. Power the Charger with FE, or turn a &6Wooden Crank&r on top of it."
		"Find a meteorite and step inside it."
	]
	quest.19FEF02447A6E938.quest_subtitle: "Something fell from the sky"
	quest.19FEF02447A6E938.title: "Meteorite Hunter"
	quest.1A0CC986F03607AB.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Electrolytic Separator&r splits water into &6Hydrogen&r and &6Oxygen&r with FE. Pump water in and pipe each gas out with &bPressurized Tubes&r."
		"Oxygen feeds the Purification Chamber. Hydrogen burns in a &6Gas-Burning Generator&r and fuels the Mekanism &6Jetpack&r, whose recipe needs an airship part."
		"&eLater:&r rockets can burn hydrogen too. Store spare gas in &6Chemical Tanks&r."
	]
	quest.1A0CC986F03607AB.quest_subtitle: "Hydrogen and oxygen"
	quest.1A0CC986F03607AB.title: "Split the Water"
	quest.1A88A382BC351AD3.quest_desc: [
		"Beat a &bTrial Spawner&r's waves and it spits out loot, sometimes a &6Trial Key&r."
		"Use the key on a &bVault&r for a roll of its loot. Each player can unlock each vault once, so everyone in the party gets a turn."
		"&eTip:&r enter with Bad Omen and the chamber turns ominous: harder waves, &6Ominous Trial Keys&r and richer &bOminous Vaults&r."
	]
	quest.1A88A382BC351AD3.quest_subtitle: "Trial Keys open Vaults"
	quest.1A88A382BC351AD3.title: "Under Lock and Key"
	quest.1A91F95133FA0CAE.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Masters sign other people's contracts.\"&r"
		"Pay &6250 Contract Seals&r to rise to Master Contractor."
		"Opens the &eMaster shelf&r and two Grand Contracts: &bSkyport Construction&r and the &bLunar Supply Run&r."
	]
	quest.1A91F95133FA0CAE.quest_subtitle: "250 Contract Seals"
	quest.1A91F95133FA0CAE.title: "Rank V: Master"
	quest.1AB8BD3331AD7015.quest_desc: [
		"&6Chain Conveyors&r (large cogwheel and andesite casing) link when you right-click two of them with chains. The chain carries packages and passes rotation along."
		"Right-click a conveyor with a &6Frogport&r (item vault, slimeball, andesite alloy), place it nearby and give it an address. It catches packages bearing its address and throws the rest onto the chain, where they find their own frog."
		"A frogport also loads and unloads the inventory or packager right below it."
		"&eTip:&r right-click frogports with a &6Clipboard&r to collect their addresses for autocomplete."
	]
	quest.1AB8BD3331AD7015.quest_subtitle: "Chain conveyors and frogports"
	quest.1AB8BD3331AD7015.title: "Hungry Hoppers"
	quest.1AF5AB0F6B758878.quest_desc: [
		"You met the Ender Guardian and the Netherite Monstrosity on the boss ladder. Now finish the set: Ignis, the Harbinger, the Leviathan, the Ancient Remnant, Maledictus, Scylla and the rest of L_Ender's Cataclysm."
		"Most guard dungeons of their own, and each one is a full team fight."
		"&eTip:&r every lair has a craftable Eye (Flame, Abyss, Mech, Storm, Desert, Curse, Void, Monstrous). Throw it like an Eye of Ender to find the way."
		"&7Lootr gives every player their own share of the dungeon chests.&r"
	]
	quest.1AF5AB0F6B758878.quest_subtitle: "Every Cataclysm boss"
	quest.1AF5AB0F6B758878.title: "The Cataclysmfarer"
	quest.1B1F7BD6F68993DC.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Mega Torch&r (a torch, a diamond, a gold block and logs) stops hostile monsters from spawning naturally in a big radius, so a town stays safe without a torch on every block."
		"Its cousins: the &6Dread Lamp&r keeps passive mobs like bats and squid from spawning, and the &6Feral Flare Lantern&r places invisible lights in dark spaces."
		"&7It won't stop mobs that wander in from outside.&r"
	]
	quest.1B1F7BD6F68993DC.quest_subtitle: "Spawn-proofing in style"
	quest.1B1F7BD6F68993DC.title: "Safe Streets"
	quest.1B6A1B9663FA93E3.quest_desc: [
		"&bTrial Chambers&r are copper and tuff halls buried underground, full of &bTrial Spawners&r that send waves of mobs at you."
		"&6Not Enough Trials&r reworks them with five new chamber designs, secret puzzle rooms and a wider mix of mobs."
		"Find one and step inside."
		"&eTip:&r Breezes knock arrows aside, so bring a good melee weapon."
	]
	quest.1B6A1B9663FA93E3.quest_subtitle: "Step into a Trial Chamber"
	quest.1B6A1B9663FA93E3.title: "Trial by Copper"
	quest.1BFEC3A05A10FC08.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"A dragon's skeleton, lying out in the void? The fossil hall must have a cast.\"&r"
		"Survey a &bDragon Skeleton&r in Nullscape's &bShadowlands&r and bring 16 &6Bone Blocks&r for the cast."
		"&7Please leave the skeleton standing and bring bone blocks from home. Each is nine bone meal.&r"
		"&eTip:&r a Create &bMillstone&r grinds bones, and even calcite, into bone meal."
	]
	quest.1BFEC3A05A10FC08.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Lantern Museum"
	quest.1BFEC3A05A10FC08.title: "Bones in the Void"
	quest.1CB00059C89A2672.quest_desc: [
		"&7The fleet owns the sky. Now look past it.&r"
		""
		"Craft a &6Telescope&r from an &6Amethyst Shard&r, &6Brass Ingots&r and a &6Stick&r."
		"At night, look at a planet with &6Paper&r in your inventory and hold use to take an &6Astronomical Reading&r."
		"This chapter splits in two: Northstar star maps on the left, Exposure: Space astrophotography on the right. Both lead to the Moon."
	]
	quest.1CB00059C89A2672.quest_subtitle: "A brass telescope and a dark night"
	quest.1CB00059C89A2672.title: "Eyes on the Sky"
	quest.1CB6A34F0AC0D6BF.quest_desc: [
		"Six templates from far places: &6Tide&r, &6Ward&r, &6Eye&r, &6Snout&r, &6Rib&r and &6Spire&r."
		"Opens once your team reaches the End. Copy each one before you use it."
	]
	quest.1CB6A34F0AC0D6BF.quest_subtitle: "18 seals"
	quest.1CB6A34F0AC0D6BF.title: "Far Realms Trim Set"
	quest.1CB7155B35A28F76.quest_desc: [
		"Throw one to get out of a pit or across a gap in a hurry."
		"Pearls also go into &6Warp Stones&r, and into &6Waystones&r once you reach the Brass Age."
	]
	quest.1CB7155B35A28F76.quest_subtitle: "2 seals"
	quest.1CB7155B35A28F76.title: "Ender Pearls x4"
	quest.1CC943104AF7B074.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The new mill needs a chimney, and chimneys need bricks.\"&r"
		"32 blocks of &6Bricks&r. Dig clay from riverbeds and swamps, smelt the &6Clay Balls&r into bricks and craft four bricks into each block."
		"&eTip:&r once Create is running, an &bEncased Fan&r washing sand through water turns up clay balls too."
	]
	quest.1CC943104AF7B074.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Andesite Mill \\& Co."
	quest.1CC943104AF7B074.title: "Kiln Bricks"
	quest.1CCDFC8372E2F8CA.quest_desc: [
		"&7Fifty containers opened and Stage 3 power humming at home. The team has earned some trust.&r"
		""
		"Open &650 Lootr containers&r. Your team must also have made its &bFirst Spark&r in Steel \\& Sparks."
		"The reward unlocks the &6Explorer's Compass&r recipe for your whole team."
		""
		"&eYou also receive an &6Explorer's Licence&e. Keep it: it goes into the &bExplorer's Compass&e recipe and comes back after crafting."
	]
	quest.1CCDFC8372E2F8CA.quest_subtitle: "Fifty containers and a spark"
	quest.1CCDFC8372E2F8CA.title: "Explorer's Licence"
	quest.1CDF18F85B5D60ED.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Rocket Station&r is mechanical-crafted from Circuits, a Targeting Computer, a Hardened Precision Mechanism, titanium and an &6Iron Cogwheel&r (a shaft and an Industrial Iron Block)."
		"&6Rocket Controls&r are a Circuit, an Industrial Iron Block, a lever and titanium."
		"Build the rocket on the station: the controls, seats, thrusters, the computer rack, &bFluid Tanks&r of fuel and metal blocks for heat shielding. Then assemble it."
		"The station shows fuel, thrusters, shielding and the destination from your &6Space Atlas&r."
	]
	quest.1CDF18F85B5D60ED.quest_subtitle: "The launch pad and its brain"
	quest.1CDF18F85B5D60ED.title: "Rocket Station"
	quest.1CF95111046C91F1.quest_desc: [
		"The bounties reach past the Overworld: the &bTwilight Rangers&r post culls in the Twilight Forest, and &bBastion Watch&r in the Nether. Each one waits until you can get there."
		"The first &bweekly boss bounties&r appear too: mutants once your team reaches World Tier Frontier, and the Naga."
		"&7Tier III opens with Steel Backbone.&r"
	]
	quest.1CF95111046C91F1.quest_subtitle: "The Twilight Forest and the Nether"
	quest.1CF95111046C91F1.title: "Tier II Bounties"
	quest.1D0E63255B7BA2BE.quest_desc: [
		"&7The last contract is one you write yourself.&r"
		""
		"Run regular freight between a colony on another planet and your town's market street, by starship (an Aeronautics ship with a &6Dimensional Drive&r) or by rocket."
		"A &6Shipping Schedule&r (a Create Schedule and a Compass) flies a ship between &6Ship Docks&r on its own. The ship needs an &bAdvanced Contraption Controller&r on a &bShip Control Module&r, and a &6Diagnostic Tablet&r links controllers to docks."
		"&cShip Control Modules count against your chunk-loading budget, and a ship needs a Contraption Claim Block to be protected.&r"
		"&7Gadgets \\& Gizmos marks the autopilot experimental: ride along on the first runs.&r"
		"Carry the schedule and tick the box once the first cargo reaches market."
	]
	quest.1D0E63255B7BA2BE.quest_subtitle: "Goods between worlds"
	quest.1D0E63255B7BA2BE.title: "Interplanetary Trade Route"
	quest.1E03E0C081BB0675.quest_desc: [
		"Mekanism machines run on FE. A &6Heat Generator&r burns fuel or soaks up heat from lava beside it. &6Solar&r and &6Wind Generators&r make a little power for free."
		"Store it in an &6Energy Cube&r and move it with &bUniversal Cables&r."
		"&eTip:&r your Crafts \\& Additions alternators and IE generators make the same FE, so wire them in too."
	]
	quest.1E03E0C081BB0675.quest_subtitle: "Power for the new machines"
	quest.1E03E0C081BB0675.title: "Your First Generator"
	quest.1E072015D22E5C21.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The citadel's guardian is back at its post.\"&r"
		"Kill the &bEnder Guardian&r in its &bRuined Citadel&r out on the End's outer islands. An &6Eye of Void&r leads there."
		"After each defeat it leaves a &bBoss Respawner&r; use another Eye of Void on it to call the Guardian back."
		"Its prize is the &6Gauntlet of Guard&r."
	]
	quest.1E072015D22E5C21.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.1E072015D22E5C21.title: "Bounty: Ender Guardian"
	quest.1E4B339054DA0DD9.quest_desc: [
		"&7Every fleet needs a flagship.&r"
		""
		"Build a big ship that works as a mobile base: an on-board &6Waystone&r (Waystones: Sable keeps it working in flight), a &6Digital Miner&r rig and its own &6Ship Dock&r."
		"Mekanism machines work aboard ships, so a flying Digital Miner can mine wherever you park."
		"Bring the parts, then tick the box once your flagship is in the air."
		"&eNext:&r the Moon program in &dLiftoff&r."
	]
	quest.1E4B339054DA0DD9.quest_subtitle: "A mobile base in the clouds"
	quest.1E4B339054DA0DD9.title: "The Flagship"
	quest.1E5089866A6EF1C8.quest_desc: [
		"The Create &6Jetpack&r is built on a &bMechanical Crafter&r grid from a &6Copper Backtank&r, a &6Precision Mechanism&r, &6Brass Sheets&r, a chute, a shaft and an &6Elytra&r."
		"It flies on the backtank's stored air and has a hover mode, which makes it a superb building tool. It takes the chest slot."
		"&7The Elytra means the End, so this one waits for Summit.&r"
	]
	quest.1E5089866A6EF1C8.quest_subtitle: "A builder's best friend"
	quest.1E5089866A6EF1C8.title: "Brass Jetpack"
	quest.1EB808F562C9F757.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Mars is a long burn, and our freighters want cold fuel.\"&r"
		"16,000 mB of &6Liquid Hydrogen&r. An &bElectrolysis Machine&r (built with Martian steel) splits water into hydrogen gas and oxygen."
		"An &bIce Box&r condenses the gas once it is colder than -253 °C. Orbit sits at -270 °C, so an Ice Box at an orbital station does the job."
		"&eTip:&r hand it in from tanks in the quest screen, or pipe it into a Task Screen."
	]
	quest.1EB808F562C9F757.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Ares Mining Consortium"
	quest.1EB808F562C9F757.title: "Cold Fuel for the Long Burn"
	quest.1ED7B179A5B1DB1C.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The rot spreads if nobody cuts it back. Cut it back.\"&r"
		"Kill 20 &bRotwalkers&r and 8 &bRotbelchers&r in the &bUndergarden&r. Rotspawn roam almost every biome down there, and every kind drops &6Utheric Shards&r."
		"&eTip:&r Utherium weapons deal 1.5x damage to Rotspawn, and a &6Shard Torch&r (a shard on a stick) hurts any that come close."
	]
	quest.1ED7B179A5B1DB1C.quest_subtitle: "Daily bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.1ED7B179A5B1DB1C.title: "Rotspawn Purge"
	quest.200DFAD481F7305A.quest_desc: [
		"&bLootr&r gives every player their own copy of every structure container, so nobody arrives at a dungeon somebody else has already emptied."
		"Leave loot chests standing. Breaking one (Lootr makes you sneak to do it) takes its loot away from everyone who hasn't opened it yet, and Carry On refuses to lift them."
		"Open any loot chest out in the world."
	]
	quest.200DFAD481F7305A.quest_subtitle: "Your own copy of every chest"
	quest.200DFAD481F7305A.title: "Loot for Everyone"
	quest.20A3284402EE0A77.quest_desc: [
		"An outpost stops when nobody is nearby, unless something keeps its chunks loaded."
		"Craft an &6Empty Andesite Chunk Loader&r (andesite casing, a shaft, glass and a Respawn Anchor), then right-click a &6Ghast&r with it to capture one."
		"Place it at the outpost and give it rotation. While it turns, it keeps the area loaded."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r loaders count against your team's force-load budget. Keep to about two active loaders per player."
	]
	quest.20A3284402EE0A77.quest_subtitle: "A ghast that minds the outpost"
	quest.20A3284402EE0A77.title: "Keep It Turning"
	quest.20B3B3B925B8C12E.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Seeds older than the oldest ruins. The Museum's glasshouse wants more.\"&r"
		"Bring 3 &6Torchflower Seeds&r and 3 &6Pitcher Pods&r. Only a &bSniffer&r digs them up, snuffling through grass, dirt and moss."
		"&6Sniffer Eggs&r turn up when you brush the &bSuspicious Sand&r of warm ocean ruins."
		"&eTip:&r one sniffer keeps digging all day, and two will breed when fed torchflower seeds."
	]
	quest.20B3B3B925B8C12E.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Lantern Museum"
	quest.20B3B3B925B8C12E.title: "Ancient Seeds"
	quest.20F9911AC0D65706.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Turtle&r is a computer that moves: surround a Computer with iron ingots, with a chest under it."
		"Craft it next to a &6Diamond Pickaxe&r for a mining turtle; diamond axes, hoes, shovels and swords give it other jobs."
		""
		"Turtles burn fuel to move. Put coal in a turtle's inventory and run &brefuel all&r."
		"Then try &bexcavate 8&r to dig an 8x8 shaft down to bedrock, or &btunnel 32&r for a long mining corridor."
		"&eTurtles stop when their chunk unloads, so stay near them or keep them inside your force-load budget."
	]
	quest.20F9911AC0D65706.quest_subtitle: "Small robots that dig, chop and build"
	quest.20F9911AC0D65706.title: "Turtle Power"
	quest.2115159DB0AED51D.quest_desc: [
		"Each &6MekaSuit&r piece is netherite armor plus &6Polonium Pellets&r, &6Ultimate Control Circuits&r, a &6Basic Induction Cell&r and &6HDPE Sheets&r."
		"Polonium comes from fission waste in a &bSolar Neutron Activator&r; a &bChemical Crystallizer&r turns it into pellets."
		"The &bModification Station&r installs units into the suit. The next three quests make the space-rated ones."
	]
	quest.2115159DB0AED51D.quest_subtitle: "The full MekaSuit"
	quest.2115159DB0AED51D.title: "Mekanist"
	quest.21D70DCE353B7B26.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"All the founders at one table, and every kitchen in the colony cooking for them.\"&r"
		""
		"Set the finest table the colony has seen: a &6Honey Glazed Ham&r and a &6Stuffed Pumpkin&r from Farmer's Delight, two &6Lasagne&r from Candlelight and a &6Grandma's Strawberry Cake&r from Farm \\& Charm."
		"To drink: a &6Jellie Wine&r, blended in a Fermentation Barrel from Apple, Chenet and Bolvar Wine with white grapejuice, and a &6Dark Brew&r, three whiskeys blended in a &bNetherite Brewingstation&r."
		"Nothing is handed in. Once the quest completes, set the feast out and serve the crew."
		"&7A one-time order. It opens once your team has finished Master Chef.&r"
	]
	quest.21D70DCE353B7B26.quest_subtitle: "Signature order: a feast for the colony"
	quest.21D70DCE353B7B26.title: "The Founders' Feast"
	quest.21E573E827F2FA7F.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Survey crews head out at dawn. Pack them something that travels.\"&r"
		"8 &6Hamburgers&r and 8 &6Mutton Wraps&r."
		"Both are crafted from bread, an onion and a leafy green such as a &6Cabbage Leaf&r (a cabbage cut on the Cutting Board). Burgers add a &6Beef Patty&r and a tomato; wraps add &6Cooked Mutton&r."
		"A Beef Patty is &6Minced Beef&r (raw beef on the Cutting Board), cooked in a furnace, smoker or campfire."
		"&eTip:&r keep a few cows and sheep penned near the kitchen."
	]
	quest.21E573E827F2FA7F.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from The Mess Hall"
	quest.21E573E827F2FA7F.title: "Packed Lunches"
	quest.2214B9E23C1A8376.quest_desc: [
		"Apothic Enchanting reworks the table. The shelves around it set three stats: &bEterna&r (the highest level), &bQuanta&r (randomness, for better or worse) and &bArcana&r (rarer enchantments, and more of them)."
		"A &6Hellshelf&r (a bookshelf, nether bricks and a blaze rod) adds Quanta, and a &6Seashelf&r (a bookshelf, prismarine bricks and a pufferfish) adds Arcana. Both let Eterna climb to 45."
		"Your World Tier caps the Eterna you can use: 30 at Haven, 45 at Frontier, 60 at Ascent, 75 at Summit and 100 at Pinnacle."
		"Collect one of each shelf."
	]
	quest.2214B9E23C1A8376.quest_subtitle: "Shelves past level 30"
	quest.2214B9E23C1A8376.title: "The Chaos of Hell"
	quest.224DAF15F5B6E180.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The night shift runs on green tea and milky coffee.\"&r"
		"8 &6Green Tea&r and 8 &6Milk Coffee&r, brewed in a &bTea Kettle&r on a stove."
		"Tea: shear flowers for &6Tea Blossoms&r and plant them. Pack nine &6Green Tea Leaves&r into a block, place it to dry, then break it for &6Dried Green Tea&r and brew that with a glass bottle."
		"Coffee: plant &6Coffee Beans&r from Wild Coffee in jungles. Brew beans with a glass bottle into Coffee, then that Coffee with a Milk Bucket into Milk Coffee."
		"&eTip:&r both need more heat than a stove gives, so put &6Blaze Powder&r in the kettle's heat slot."
	]
	quest.224DAF15F5B6E180.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Lantern Row Tea House"
	quest.224DAF15F5B6E180.title: "Tea and Coffee"
	quest.2251BA941260153A.quest_desc: [
		"Opens with &6Andesite Works&r. Andesite Mill \\& Co. and the Voltaic Grid Authority want alloy and gearing straight away."
		"The Brassworks Union's orders also need the Brass Age's &6Complex Curiosities&r, and Northline Railways' need &6Rails \\& Parcels&r."
	]
	quest.2251BA941260153A.quest_subtitle: "The Create workshop, reset daily"
	quest.2251BA941260153A.title: "Tier II Orders"
	quest.2289DEA90B0AD2DB.quest_desc: [
		"Waystones are built with Create. First make a &6Warp Stone&r from an amethyst shard, an emerald and an ender pearl."
		"Then assemble the &6Waystone&r on a &bMechanical Crafter&r grid with &6Andesite Casing&r, &6Stone Bricks&r and an &6Ender Pearl&r. EMI shows the layout."
		"Activate the waystones you find in villages too. Each player can warp to any waystone they have activated."
		"Warps cost a few coins from your bank (&e/fares&r), and &cno waystone reaches a planet&r. The rocket is the only way up."
	]
	quest.2289DEA90B0AD2DB.quest_subtitle: "Fast travel, the Create way"
	quest.2289DEA90B0AD2DB.title: "Waystone Network"
	quest.228A7D399ED94C0B.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The stations go up before the rails do, and they need light.\"&r"
		"64 &6Glass Panes&r and 8 &6Lanterns&r. Smelt sand into glass and craft six glass into sixteen panes. A lantern is a torch ringed by eight iron nuggets."
		"&eTip:&r leave a few furnaces of sand running while you gather the iron."
	]
	quest.228A7D399ED94C0B.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Northline Railways"
	quest.228A7D399ED94C0B.title: "Station Windows"
	quest.229A003A0EC96ABB.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our Twilight sheets are mostly blank, and nobody has charted an Enchanted Forest.\"&r"
		"Find an &bEnchanted Forest&r in the Twilight Forest and bring 3 &6Magic Maps&r."
		"A &6Magic Map Focus&r is a raven feather, torchberries and glowstone dust; craft it with paper into a &6Blank Magic Map&r. Use one in the Twilight Forest to draw the land around you."
		"&eTip:&r a magic map shades each biome in its own colour, which makes rare ones like the Enchanted Forest easier to spot."
	]
	quest.229A003A0EC96ABB.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Cartographers' Society"
	quest.229A003A0EC96ABB.title: "The Twilight Atlas"
	quest.22FC6032D71B4000.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Sigil of Socketing&r (amethyst, gem-fused slate, gem dust and gunpowder) adds one more socket to an item. Gem-Fused Slate is deepslate and gem dust."
		"Set a gem at a &bSmithing Table&r: the item on the left, the gem on the right."
		"Choose carefully. A &6Sigil of Withdrawal&r pulls gems back out, but it takes out all of them at once."
	]
	quest.22FC6032D71B4000.quest_subtitle: "Gems into gear"
	quest.22FC6032D71B4000.title: "Socket to Me"
	quest.2361A61E6E64BA21.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Enrichment Chamber&r turns each ore block into two dusts. Smelt them for twice the ingots."
		"It also enriches coal, redstone and diamonds for the infuser."
		"&eTip:&r the ore multipliers count ore blocks, so mine with Silk Touch for the full bonus. Keep this machine: every later ore stage still ends here, cleaning dirty dust."
	]
	quest.2361A61E6E64BA21.quest_subtitle: "Ore doubling"
	quest.2361A61E6E64BA21.title: "Getting More From Less"
	quest.237289BFD9DA0B5E.quest_desc: [
		"The &bNetherite Monstrosity&r guards the &bSoul Forge&r in the Nether."
		"Craft an &6Eye of Monstrous&r (an Eye of Ender, netherite scrap, blackstone and a lava bucket) and follow it there."
		"It's one of the two keys to Ascent, with the Twilight Hydra."
		"Its loot includes the &6Infernal Forge&r and a &6Monstrous Horn&r."
	]
	quest.237289BFD9DA0B5E.quest_subtitle: "Cataclysm's Netherite Monstrosity"
	quest.237289BFD9DA0B5E.title: "The Nether's Warmachine"
	quest.237615FBCB9FD54B.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Venus burns whatever isn't shielded. Send the best heat shield there is.\"&r"
		"64 &6Tungsten Plating&r. Mine Mercury's tungsten ore for Raw Tungsten and smelt it; four &6Tungsten Ingots&r craft four plating, or a stonecutter makes one per ingot."
		"Tungsten blocks are the strongest heat shielding a Rocket Station counts on a rocket."
		"&eTip:&r with Silk Touch, Crushing Wheels get about 1.75 crushed tungsten from each ore block."
	]
	quest.237615FBCB9FD54B.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Sunward Expedition"
	quest.237615FBCB9FD54B.title: "Heat Shields for Sunward"
	quest.23FD36E8AF599689.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Simple Reforging Table&r (an enchanting table, gem dust, iron and smooth stone) rerolls an item's affixes for &6Sigils of Rebirth&r and rarity materials. Sigils of Rebirth are gem dust and gem-fused slate."
		"Its tooltip shows the highest rarity it can handle. For the top rarities, upgrade it into the full &6Reforging Table&r with netherite and Arcane Sands."
		"&eMuch later:&r Create: Enchantment Industry's &bAffix Augmentor&r strengthens affixes on a belt or depot, fed with Apotheotic Essence. It needs a nether star."
	]
	quest.23FD36E8AF599689.quest_subtitle: "Roll the dice again"
	quest.23FD36E8AF599689.title: "Reforged"
	quest.2403ACB5E5A291AE.quest_desc: [
		"Tier I is &bdaily culls&r in the Overworld for The Wardens' Lodge: zombies and skeletons, spiders, and drowned."
		"Each pays a bevel and a Contract Seal, and comes back a day after you claim it."
		"&7Tier II opens with Andesite Works.&r"
	]
	quest.2403ACB5E5A291AE.quest_subtitle: "Daily culls around the colony"
	quest.2403ACB5E5A291AE.title: "Tier I Bounties"
	quest.244DC1B951D3979C.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Someone always builds one. Better you, and far from us.\"&r"
		"Summon the &bWither&r with three &6Wither Skeleton Skulls&r on four &6Soul Sand&r or &6Soul Soil&r in a T, then kill it."
		"Skulls drop from wither skeletons in Nether fortresses, and the &bGateway of the Sunlit Ascent&r pays out three."
		"&cIt explodes when it spawns and smashes blocks as it fights.&r Summon it in a sealed arena, deep underground."
	]
	quest.244DC1B951D3979C.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from Bastion Watch"
	quest.244DC1B951D3979C.title: "Bounty: The Wither"
	quest.2490160F38DFC50B.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"We're building the colony's biggest crafting CPU, and it has to think faster.\"&r"
		"16 &6Crafting Co-Processing Units&r. Each is a &6Crafting Unit&r (iron, two Fluix ME Glass Cables, a Logic and a Calculation Processor) crafted together with an &6Engineering Processor&r."
		"&eTip:&r encode the patterns once and let your own network autocraft the whole order."
	]
	quest.2490160F38DFC50B.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Lattice Data Exchange"
	quest.2490160F38DFC50B.title: "Thinking Machines"
	quest.249D5B555943A2BB.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every client on the board chipped in for one commission: an engine big enough to run the colony.\"&r"
		""
		"Show the Guild the best of every line you run: 16 &6Hardened Precision Mechanisms&r from Create, 16 &6Heavy Engineering Blocks&r from IE, 16 &6Ultimate Control Circuits&r from Mekanism and a &6256k ME Storage Component&r from AE2."
		"Then start it up with 64,000 mB of &6Diesel&r and 100,000,000 FE. &cThe power can only go in through a Task Screen,&r up to 100,000 FE per tick."
		"&7The parts stay yours. The fuel and the power go into the first run.&r"
		"&eTip:&r a second Task Screen set to the diesel task lets your distillation tower pipe it straight in."
	]
	quest.249D5B555943A2BB.quest_subtitle: "The Industry Board's signature order"
	quest.249D5B555943A2BB.title: "The World Engine"
	quest.24A1B52680B9E815.quest_desc: [
		"Five armour trim templates from overworld landmarks: &6Coast&r, &6Dune&r, &6Wild&r, &6Sentry&r and &6Vex&r."
		"A template is used up when applied, so copy it first: 7 diamonds and its base block in a crafting grid make two."
	]
	quest.24A1B52680B9E815.quest_subtitle: "12 seals"
	quest.24A1B52680B9E815.title: "Wayfarer Trim Set"
	quest.24BC4B4A05AE0008.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Ironvale's armour shop wants plate that turns a blade.\"&r"
		"32 &6Reinforced Alloy&r. In a &bMetallurgic Infuser&r, infuse &6Copper&r with redstone into &6Infused Alloy&r, then infuse that with diamond."
		"&eTip:&r an &bEnrichment Chamber&r turns each diamond into an &6Enriched Diamond&r, worth eight times as much infusion as diamond dust."
	]
	quest.24BC4B4A05AE0008.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Ironvale Foundry"
	quest.24BC4B4A05AE0008.title: "Alloy Shipment"
	quest.24E2166031700F05.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Nothing in our cabinets glows like the Twilight does. Bring samples.\"&r"
		"In the &bTwilight Forest&r, collect 4 &6Fireflies&r, 8 &6Mushgloom&r and 8 &6Liveroot&r."
		"Fireflies cling to the trunks of canopy and mangrove trees. Mushgloom grows in the Mushroom and Firefly Forests. &bLiveroots&r tangle among the roots of Twilight trees underground; break them for liveroot."
		"&eTip:&r a Magic Map shows where the Mushroom Forests lie."
	]
	quest.24E2166031700F05.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Field Survey Office"
	quest.24E2166031700F05.title: "Twilight Specimens"
	quest.24EF7760AF7B6858.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a placed &6Stripped Log&r or &6Stripped Wood&r block with a &6Brass Ingot&r to turn it into &6Brass Casing&r."
		"Brass casing goes into Mechanical Crafters and Arms, Display Links, Rotation Speed Controllers and train casing."
		"&eTip:&r once you have Deployers, one holding a brass ingot can case logs on a belt for you."
	]
	quest.24EF7760AF7B6858.quest_subtitle: "A shell for smarter machines"
	quest.24EF7760AF7B6858.title: "The Brass Age"
	quest.24F5372D0F836191.quest_desc: [
		"The &bLunar Monstrosity&r is rooted in the &bCursed Garden&r, a thorny maze full of trapped souls."
		"Its hide shrugs off most weapons until it's scorched. Set it alight with Fire Aspect or Flame arrows, then strike while it burns."
		"It mostly stays put, but now and then it burrows underground to chase you."
		"Prizes include the &6Moonring Bow&r and the &6Crescent Pendant&r."
	]
	quest.24F5372D0F836191.quest_subtitle: "Burn the Lunar Monstrosity"
	quest.24F5372D0F836191.title: "Through the Thorns"
	quest.24F9D48F115E9CA5.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Eight mechanisms for the clockmakers, and they count every tooth.\"&r"
		"8 &6Precision Mechanisms&r. Send &6Golden Sheets&r through &bsequenced assembly&r: three &bDeployers&r add a &6Cogwheel&r, a &6Large Cogwheel&r and an &6Iron Nugget&r, five times round."
		"&eTip:&r a looped belt runs unattended. Sort out the occasional scrap."
	]
	quest.24F9D48F115E9CA5.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Brassworks Union"
	quest.24F9D48F115E9CA5.title: "Precision Parts"
	quest.252AA32A5CC59CC3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ancient Debris&r hides deep in the Nether, usually sealed inside the rock. It shrugs off explosions, so TNT can clear the rock around it without destroying it."
		"Smelt or blast it into &6Netherite Scrap&r. Four scrap and four &6Gold Ingots&r make a &6Netherite Ingot&r."
		"Upgrading gear also takes a &6Netherite Upgrade&r smithing template. Bastion remnants hide them."
		"&eTip:&r keep some scrap. Cataclysm's &6Eye of Monstrous&r needs it, and that eye leads to the Netherite Monstrosity, one of the keys to Ascent."
	]
	quest.252AA32A5CC59CC3.quest_subtitle: "Ancient debris and netherite"
	quest.252AA32A5CC59CC3.title: "Hidden in the Depths"
	quest.25C9E4F087ADA27D.quest_desc: [
		"&7Build the engine. Chart the horizon. Leave the planet.&r"
		""
		"Starwright climbs from a Create workshop to steel and power grids, an airship fleet and ME networks, then on to rockets bound for the Moon, Mars, Venus and Mercury. Exploring feeds the factory, and the factory takes you farther."
		"Everyone gets this &6Quest Book&r on first join. Progress is shared by your FTB team: start one with &b/ftbteams party create <name>&r and bring friends in with &b/ftbteams party invite <player>&r."
		"New chapters open as your team climbs. Optional quests are side trips: skip them and nothing locks."
		"&eTip:&r each stop around this one takes a minute, and together they save a lot of wiki reading."
	]
	quest.25C9E4F087ADA27D.quest_subtitle: "How this book works"
	quest.25C9E4F087ADA27D.title: "Welcome Aboard"
	quest.25E76EF21A45D327.quest_desc: [
		"Your first airship opens Skyward Freight's weekly orders: propellers, balloon gear, docking hardware, autopilot parts and sails, all built with Create Aeronautics and its add-ons."
		"The Levitite Blend order also waits on the End."
	]
	quest.25E76EF21A45D327.quest_subtitle: "Opens with your first airship"
	quest.25E76EF21A45D327.title: "Tier IV: Airship Freight"
	quest.2679597805F377BD.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every new hull needs a balloon. Send us complete kits.\"&r"
		"Eight &6Hot Air Burners&r (iron sheets, a block of coal, redstone and andesite alloy) and 256 &6Hot Air Envelopes&r."
		"Envelopes are white wool and sticks: four per craft, or three per wool when a &bDeployer&r holding sticks works a belt of white wool."
		"&eTip:&r a sheep farm feeding that Deployer line keeps this order cheap."
	]
	quest.2679597805F377BD.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Skyward Freight"
	quest.2679597805F377BD.title: "Hot Air, Wholesale"
	quest.26B1653D874386E1.quest_desc: [
		"Hold right-click to read one, then pick any waystone you have activated. A scroll warp is free."
		"Opens once your team makes a &6Precision Mechanism&r. &cNo scroll reaches the planets.&r"
	]
	quest.26B1653D874386E1.quest_subtitle: "4 seals"
	quest.26B1653D874386E1.title: "Warp Scrolls x4"
	quest.26E7210222FAF558.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The night shift wants the fields clear by sunrise.\"&r"
		"Kill 30 &bZombies&r and 20 &bSkeletons&r. They spawn in the dark: outdoors at night, in caves and in any unlit corner."
		"Plains and forests are the best hunting grounds. In snow, desert, jungle and swamp most of them spawn as local cousins (husks, strays and the like) that don't count."
		"&eTip:&r a zombie or skeleton spawner from a dungeon makes a handy kill room."
	]
	quest.26E7210222FAF558.quest_subtitle: "Daily bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.26E7210222FAF558.title: "Night Watch"
	quest.26E7366D671605C4.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Nobody has printed a photo from inside an Ancient City. Be the first. Quietly.\"&r"
		"Step into an &bAncient City&r in the Deep Dark and bring 3 &6Photographs&r."
		"&cMind the shriekers:&r crouch past sculk sensors. Each shriek raises the warning level, and the fourth brings the Warden."
		"&eTip:&r a &6Redstone Lamp&r fitted to the camera works as a flash in the dark."
	]
	quest.26E7366D671605C4.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from The Gazette"
	quest.26E7366D671605C4.title: "Hush, Please"
	quest.27582B55ED899B3F.quest_desc: [
		"An &6Advanced Computer&r adds colour and mouse support. Craft one with gold in place of stone, or ring an existing Computer with seven gold ingots to upgrade it and keep its files."
		""
		"&6Advanced Monitors&r placed side by side merge into one colour touchscreen, up to 8 blocks wide and 6 tall."
		"Place one next to the computer and run &bmonitor right <program>&r (name the side it is on) to show any program on it."
		"&eTapping an advanced monitor fires a monitor_touch event, which is all you need for on-screen buttons."
	]
	quest.27582B55ED899B3F.quest_subtitle: "Advanced computers and touchscreens"
	quest.27582B55ED899B3F.title: "Full Color"
	quest.27828259E5172036.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Chemical Injection Chamber&r uses &6Hydrogen Chloride&r to turn each ore into four &6Shards&r. Purify the shards into clumps and carry on down the chain."
		"Make hydrogen chloride in a &bChemical Infuser&r from hydrogen and &6Chlorine&r. Chlorine comes from separating &6Brine&r, which a &bThermal Evaporation Plant&r makes from water."
		"&eTip:&r it needs &6Elite Control Circuits&r and &6Reinforced Alloy&r."
	]
	quest.27828259E5172036.quest_subtitle: "Ore quadrupling"
	quest.27828259E5172036.title: "Injecting... 1, 2, 3, 4"
	quest.2816D6DBA65B4B04.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our house red is the pride of Old Vine. Six bottles for the tasting room.\"&r"
		"6 bottles of &6Red Wine&r."
		"Drop red grapes into a &bGrapevine Pot&r, jump on them and collect the juice in empty &6Wine Bottles&r."
		"Pour the &6Red Grapejuice&r into a &bFermentation Barrel&r, then add sugar and an empty Wine Bottle for each wine. Each bottle takes about five minutes, so run a few barrels."
		"&7Keep some back: wine keeps improving in the cellar.&r"
	]
	quest.2816D6DBA65B4B04.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Old Vine Cellars"
	quest.2816D6DBA65B4B04.title: "House Red"
	quest.2995554DE66D07BF.quest_desc: [
		"The &6AE Stock Bridge&r links your Create stock network with ME. Create can order items stored in ME, and ME can request Create stock as if crafting it."
		"Bind it to your stock network with a right-click before placing it, then set its address to match the &6Frogport&r that serves it. Its Ponder shows the setup."
		"&cTeam rules:&r keep Stock Links, Stock Bridges and ME terminals inside your claim, 6+ blocks from the edge, and never share a Stock Link frequency with another team."
	]
	quest.2995554DE66D07BF.quest_subtitle: "Create stock, meet ME"
	quest.2995554DE66D07BF.title: "Bridge the Stock"
	quest.29E7EE6833277D17.quest_desc: [
		"Daily orders from the Undergarden, Eternal Starlight, the Enchanted Forest and the ocean monuments."
		"Each pays &6200 XP&r, &62 sprockets&r and &63 Contract Seals&r."
		"Some also wait on the quest that opens their world: &bReturn to the Nether&r, &bInto the Twilight&r or &bWorld Tier: Frontier&r."
	]
	quest.29E7EE6833277D17.quest_subtitle: "Opens with Steel Backbone"
	quest.29E7EE6833277D17.title: "Tier III Orders"
	quest.2A7CEB2EFEF83CBD.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"A new district, all gears and gleam.\"&r"
		"1,024 &6Brass Ingots&r, 256 &6Brass Casings&r and 128 &6Precision Mechanisms&r."
		"Brass is mixed from copper and zinc in a heated &bMechanical Mixer&r; precision mechanisms come off a &bsequenced assembly&r line."
	]
	quest.2A7CEB2EFEF83CBD.quest_subtitle: "Monthly Grand Contract from the Brassworks Union"
	quest.2A7CEB2EFEF83CBD.title: "City of Brass"
	quest.2AC99E788390D1FF.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Patrols in the Nether burn through food. Send something with a kick.\"&r"
		"8 &6Hot Wings&r and 8 &6Hotdogs&r."
		"Hot Wings cook in a &bCooking Pot&r from raw chicken, an onion and a hot spice: &6Blaze Powder&r, a &6Bullet Pepper&r or &6Pepper Powder&r."
		"Hoglins drop &6Hoglin Loin&r. Cut it into two &6Hoglin Sausages&r on a Cutting Board, roast them, then craft each with bread into a Hotdog."
		"&eTip:&r piglins sometimes barter Bullet Peppers."
	]
	quest.2AC99E788390D1FF.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from The Mess Hall"
	quest.2AC99E788390D1FF.title: "Nether Patrol Rations"
	quest.2AE6E6E8F866A445.quest_desc: [
		"Each press prints a circuit: &6Gold&r for Logic, &6Certus Quartz&r for Calculation, &6Diamond&r for Engineering and &6Silicon&r for Printed Silicon."
		"Then inscribe a printed circuit (top), &6Redstone&r (middle) and Printed Silicon (bottom) into a processor."
		"&6Silicon&r comes from smelting &6Certus Quartz Dust&r, and a Mekanism &bCrusher&r turns sand into silicon too."
		"&eTip:&r you'll want processors by the stack, so automate a few Inscribers early."
	]
	quest.2AE6E6E8F866A445.quest_subtitle: "Logic, Calculation, Engineering"
	quest.2AE6E6E8F866A445.title: "Silicon Dreams"
	quest.2AEE94EB40500B9D.quest_desc: [
		"Gems come in purities: Cracked, Chipped, Flawed, Normal, Flawless and Perfect. The better the purity, the stronger the bonus."
		"The &6Gem Cutting Table&r (gem dust, shears, planks and smooth stone) raises a gem one purity at a time, paid in Gem Dust and rarity materials. Each step costs more than the last."
		"&eLater:&r Create: Enchantment Industry's &bGem Cutter&r upgrades gems on a belt or depot, fed from a Crystal Essence tank two blocks below."
	]
	quest.2AEE94EB40500B9D.quest_subtitle: "Polish your gems"
	quest.2AEE94EB40500B9D.title: "Gem Cutting"
	quest.2AFA47F63C210C0B.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Something cursed stirs in the frozen prison.\"&r"
		"Kill &bMaledictus&r in a &bFrosted Prison&r on the snowy plains. An &6Eye of Curse&r points the way."
		"Summon it at the &bCursed Tombstone&r deep inside. The tombstone regains its power after a while, so the same prison serves again."
		"Its prize is &6Cursium&r, a netherite upgrade material."
	]
	quest.2AFA47F63C210C0B.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.2AFA47F63C210C0B.title: "Bounty: Maledictus"
	quest.2B7F22A4027E969F.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Kobolds in the caves, druids in the spooky woods. Thin them out.\"&r"
		"Kill 16 &bKobolds&r and 4 &bSkeleton Druids&r in the Twilight Forest."
		"Kobolds scurry through the caves under the forest. Skeleton Druids haunt the &bSpooky Forest&r, among a great many spiders."
		"&eTip:&r druids drop &6Torchberries&r, one of the parts of a Magic Map Focus."
	]
	quest.2B7F22A4027E969F.quest_subtitle: "Daily bounty from the Twilight Rangers"
	quest.2B7F22A4027E969F.title: "Twilight Patrol"
	quest.2B8A301809B39486.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a &6Blaze&r with an &6Empty Blaze Burner&r to catch it. Using it on a blaze &bspawner&r works too."
		"A &bBlaze Burner&r under a &bBasin&r heats it while you feed it furnace fuel such as logs or coal. A &6Blaze Cake&r superheats it for a while."
		"&eTip:&r catch several. Brass mixing, steam boilers and Enchantment Industry all want burners."
	]
	quest.2B8A301809B39486.quest_subtitle: "Catch a blaze"
	quest.2B8A301809B39486.title: "Sentient Fireplace"
	quest.2B9505C495C2C2EB.quest_desc: [
		"&7The flagship proved Create can fly. Now it has to leave the sky.&r"
		""
		"A &6Hardened Precision Mechanism&r is a Precision Mechanism sent through a second &bsequenced assembly&r. A &6Circuit&r starts as an &6Iron Sheet&r on another. EMI shows each step."
		"Nearly every rocket part needs one or the other, so automate both lines early."
		"&7Quest rewards never hand out rocket parts. Every one of them is built.&r"
	]
	quest.2B9505C495C2C2EB.quest_subtitle: "Space-grade parts"
	quest.2B9505C495C2C2EB.title: "Hardened Mechanisms"
	quest.2BAD0E214586DAB6.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our bone hall would be complete with a few bones that hum.\"&r"
		"In the &bOtherside&r, collect 8 &6Sculk Bones&r, 16 &6Soul Dust&r and 4 &6Resonarium&r."
		"&bShattered&r in the Deeplands and Echoing Forest drop sculk bones. &bSculk Snappers&r drop soul dust, and the small &bSludges&r of the Blooming Caverns drop resonarium."
		"&eTip:&r the Otherside portal stands at the centre of every Ancient City; Below and Beyond shows how to light it."
	]
	quest.2BAD0E214586DAB6.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Lantern Museum"
	quest.2BAD0E214586DAB6.title: "Echoes from Below"
	quest.2BE10259489E68C9.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The gentry want something stronger than ale. The good stuff.\"&r"
		"4 &6Highland Hearth Signature&r and 4 &6Lilitu Single Malt&r whiskeys."
		"Whiskey needs a &bCopper Brewingstation&r: upgrade a Wooden one at a Smithing Table with a Copper Ingot and a &6Sentry Armor Trim&r template from a pillager outpost."
		"Highland Hearth brews from Dried Wheat, Dried Oat and yeast; Lilitu from Dried Wheat, Dried Barley and yeast. Dry the grain in a &bSilo&r."
		"&eTip:&r sort out the kettle, oven, timer and whistle when they act up for a better brew."
	]
	quest.2BE10259489E68C9.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from The Copper Kettle"
	quest.2BE10259489E68C9.title: "Top-Shelf Whiskey"
	quest.2C092A9172F974F6.quest_desc: [
		"Hearty meals give &bNourishment&r: while it lasts, your food meter doesn't drop, except when saturation is healing you."
		"Some soups and stews give &bComfort&r instead, which keeps you regenerating however hungry you are."
		"Cook a meal that gives Nourishment (its tooltip says so) and eat it."
	]
	quest.2C092A9172F974F6.quest_subtitle: "A proper cooked meal"
	quest.2C092A9172F974F6.title: "Nourishing!"
	quest.2C564BCACEF58A15.quest_desc: [
		"Oil lies under some chunks. Right-click an &6Oil Scanner&r to see how much is under you, from &7No Oil&r to &7Bottomless Supply&r. Oil fields are worth a long trip."
		"A &bpumpjack&r brings it up: a &6Pumpjack Bearing&r, a body you build, a &6Pumpjack Head&r and a second bearing, all glued together and driven by a &6Pumpjack Crank&r."
		"Dig a hole under the head, run a straight vertical pipe down to bedrock and cap it with a &6Pumpjack Hole&r. Then fill a bucket with &6Crude Oil&r."
		"&eTip:&r the Ponder scenes walk you through the build."
	]
	quest.2C564BCACEF58A15.quest_subtitle: "Strike oil"
	quest.2C564BCACEF58A15.title: "Black Gold"
	quest.2C99A7C02E65B4E2.quest_desc: [
		"Have two &6Targeting Computers&r on hand and mechanical-craft a &6Computer Rack&r from &6Andesite Alloy&r and &6Iron Sheets&r."
		"Targeting Computers in a Computer Rack on the rocket plot a better trajectory and cut fuel use."
		"&eTip:&r the Rocket Station takes a Targeting Computer of its own, so keep that line running."
	]
	quest.2C99A7C02E65B4E2.quest_subtitle: "Plot a cheaper course"
	quest.2C99A7C02E65B4E2.title: "Targeting Computers"
	quest.2CC7B16639DF5B22.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"We're opening a new machine hall, and every machine starts with osmium.\"&r"
		"A bulk order: 1,024 &6Osmium Ingots&r. Point a &bDigital Miner&r at osmium ore and run it through your ore line: purifying, injecting or dissolving gives three, four or five ingots per ore."
		"&eTip:&r end the smelting line at a &6Task Screen&r set to this order and it fills while you're away."
	]
	quest.2CC7B16639DF5B22.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Meridian Chemworks"
	quest.2CC7B16639DF5B22.title: "Osmium by the Ton"
	quest.2D653C0B43D3222F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Space Suit Unit&r makes the MekaSuit a space suit."
		"Mechanical-craft it from &6Atomic Alloy&r, an &6Ultimate Control Circuit&r, &6Insulation&r, a sapphire (EMI shows which), a &6Module Base&r, iron sheets and HDPE."
		"&6Insulation&r: mix &6Crushed Wool&r (crush wool or carpet), crushed raw copper and crushed raw iron in a &bBasin&r."
		"&7Its in-game name may show as a raw item key.&r"
	]
	quest.2D653C0B43D3222F.quest_subtitle: "The MekaSuit goes to space"
	quest.2D653C0B43D3222F.title: "Space Suit Unit"
	quest.2DE5720A438B9370.quest_desc: [
		"You get one &b/home&r (set it with &b/sethome&r), &b/tpa&r to a friend, and &b/spawn&r. Home and tpa have a 10 minute cooldown and a 5 second warmup."
		"&b/back&r returns you to your last teleport or death spot (30-second cooldown). There is no &b/rtp&r."
		"&6Waystones&r arrive in the Brass Age. They're crafted through Create, and every warp costs a few coins from your bank (&e/fares&r)."
		"&cNothing teleports onto a planet.&r Waystones, homes and /tpa never reach them; a rocket, and later a starship, is the way there."
		"&7Much later, the Red Planet chapter lets Mekanism teleporters link worlds you've already reached.&r"
	]
	quest.2DE5720A438B9370.quest_subtitle: "How travel works here"
	quest.2DE5720A438B9370.title: "Roads, Not Shortcuts"
	quest.2E14823A24A1366F.quest_desc: [
		"Gadgets \\& Gizmos parts are peripherals: put a &6Thruster&r in &bComputer&r mode and Lua sets its throttle, switches it on or off and reads its fuel. Servo and Vector Bearings take exact angles."
		""
		"The &6Advanced Contraption Controller&r is a node-graph autopilot (mechanical crafting: Blackstone Alloy, a Computation Mechanism, a Sable Contraption Controller and andesite alloy)."
		"On a &6Ship Control Module&r it flies the whole ship as one vehicle, and a computer can set its graph variables and send it named events."
		"A &6Navigation Table&r loaded with a filled map supplies the heading."
		"&eClaim the ship with a Contraption Claim Block, then test new scripts at low throttle, well away from your base."
	]
	quest.2E14823A24A1366F.quest_subtitle: "A cargo ship with nobody at the wheel"
	quest.2E14823A24A1366F.title: "Ghost Pilot"
	quest.2E35CBB3ADC4D12B.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Three weddings and a birthday this week. We need cakes. Lots of cakes.\"&r"
		"6 &6Strawberry Cakes&r, 3 &6Chocolate Gateaux&r and 24 &6Strawberry Glazed Cookies&r."
		"Right-click a &bCaking Station&r with &6Cake Dough&r for a blank cake. Top it with &6Strawberry Jam&r for a Strawberry Cake or a &6Chocolate Truffle&r for a Gateau, then right-click the cake to pick it up."
		"For cookies, cut the blank cake with a knife, roll it flat with a &6Rolling Pin&r and top it with jam: four cookies a batch."
		"Jam and truffles cook in Farm \\& Charm's Cooking Pot; jam needs an empty &6Jar&r."
	]
	quest.2E35CBB3ADC4D12B.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Hearthstone Bakery"
	quest.2E35CBB3ADC4D12B.title: "Celebration Cakes"
	quest.2E6397F4E40952AF.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every airship in the fleet needs a full larder before it casts off.\"&r"
		"2,048 &6Bread&r and 1,024 &6Baked Potatoes&r: a job for a Create food line."
		"Mill wheat into &6Wheat Flour&r with a &bMillstone&r or Crushing Wheels, wash it into &6Dough&r with an &bEncased Fan&r blowing through water, then blow the dough through fire to bake it. The same smoking fan bakes potatoes."
		"&eTip:&r set a &6Task Screen&r to each task and run the line straight into them."
	]
	quest.2E6397F4E40952AF.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from The Mess Hall"
	quest.2E6397F4E40952AF.title: "Fleet Provisioning"
	quest.2E764568D34635FC.quest_desc: [
		"Dungeons and Taverns builds &btaverns&r out in the wilds: safe stops with traders and a bed for the night."
		"Find one and walk in."
		"&eTip:&r talk to the tavern's &bCartographer&r before you leave."
	]
	quest.2E764568D34635FC.quest_subtitle: "Taverns out in the wilds"
	quest.2E764568D34635FC.title: "Safe Haven"
	quest.2E824E54F39E8076.quest_desc: [
		"Weekly orders for long trips: the Otherside, the great landmarks and the Ancient Cities."
		"Each pays &6300 XP&r, &61 cog&r, &66 Contract Seals&r and an &6Explorer's Cache&r."
		"The Otherside order also waits on &bBelow the Bedrock&r."
		"&eTip:&r an airship turns a week's survey into an evening."
	]
	quest.2E824E54F39E8076.quest_subtitle: "Opens with Reactor Online"
	quest.2E824E54F39E8076.title: "Tier IV Orders"
	quest.2E8F408DD4B3A016.quest_desc: [
		"Silent Gear builds tools and armor from parts, and every material brings its own stats and traits."
		"Start crude: &6Crude Tool Parts&r (cobblestone, dirt and a stick), a &6Crude Knife&r and a &bStone Anvil&r (cobblestone and dirt). Use the knife on a log sitting on the anvil for six &6Template Boards&r."
		"Template boards and sticks make a &6Template&r for each part. Blueprint Paper (paper and blue dye) makes &6Blueprints&r that do the same job."
		"&cTest note:&r Silent Gear is still being tested on our server. If gear turns white or reads \"unknown material\", report it to the admins."
	]
	quest.2E8F408DD4B3A016.quest_subtitle: "Silent Gear, the crude way"
	quest.2E8F408DD4B3A016.title: "Those'll Do For Now"
	quest.2E90C13B32DC2F73.quest_desc: [
		"Under the stone lie &bmineral veins&r: mixed ores too sparse to mine by hand, but rich enough for an Excavator."
		"Place a &6Core Sample Drill&r on natural ground, give it FE and start it by hand. It drills a &6Core Sample&r that shows what the vein holds and how rich it is."
		"Place a sample while sneaking, then right-click it with a map to mark the vein. &6Structural Engineer&r villagers also sell &6Mineral Deposit Maps&r."
		"&eTip:&r a charged &6LV Accumulator&r makes a handy portable battery for the drill."
	]
	quest.2E90C13B32DC2F73.quest_subtitle: "Survey the deep veins"
	quest.2E90C13B32DC2F73.title: "X Marks the Spot"
	quest.2E983C9D0D7579C0.quest_desc: [
		"&7Bag packed, map open, crew on the line.&r"
		""
		"That's every stop on the primer. The &eLandfall&r chapter is already open: first nights, a proper kitchen and the ruins near spawn."
		"&eTip:&r come back here whenever a rule slips your mind."
	]
	quest.2E983C9D0D7579C0.quest_subtitle: "Primer complete"
	quest.2E983C9D0D7579C0.title: "Ready for Landfall"
	quest.2E9F2AFA3DF52370.quest_desc: [
		"One random pick: coal coke, treated wood, LV wire coils, iron mechanical components, hemp fiber, brass, precision mechanisms, sturdy sheets, copper spools, redstone or magma blocks."
		"Opens once your team finishes &6Steel Backbone&r."
	]
	quest.2E9F2AFA3DF52370.quest_subtitle: "8 seals"
	quest.2E9F2AFA3DF52370.title: "Foundry Crate"
	quest.2ED2715936DBA720.quest_desc: [
		"&7Steel in hand, it's time to take matter apart.&r"
		""
		"Mekanism adds &6Osmium&r, &6Tin&r, &6Lead&r, &6Uranium&r and &6Fluorite&r ores. Osmium matters most: nearly every Mekanism machine needs it."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r Mekanism owns lead and uranium. IE's lead and uranium veins are switched off, so mine Mekanism's ores instead."
		"Mine any Mekanism ore to begin."
		"&eTip:&r your Create crushing wheels handle these ores too, until Mekanism processing is running."
	]
	quest.2ED2715936DBA720.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism's raw materials"
	quest.2ED2715936DBA720.title: "First Steps"
	quest.2F22198244247CB3.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The Guild's charter now carries your seal.\"&r"
		"Pay &6500 Contract Seals&r to rise to Grandmaster."
		"Opens the &eGrandmaster shelf&r and the Grand Contract &bThe Colony Ship&r."
	]
	quest.2F22198244247CB3.quest_subtitle: "500 Contract Seals"
	quest.2F22198244247CB3.title: "Rank VI: Grandmaster"
	quest.2F3E1AE2AFE11B72.quest_desc: [
		"&7The last throne in the forest is made of ice.&r"
		""
		"Cross the &bGlacier&r to the &bAurora Palace&r and defeat the &6Snow Queen&r at its top."
		"With her gone, the Twilight Forest's boss ladder is complete."
		"&7The Highlands beyond are unfinished in this Twilight Forest version, so the expedition ends here.&r"
	]
	quest.2F3E1AE2AFE11B72.quest_subtitle: "The Snow Queen's palace"
	quest.2F3E1AE2AFE11B72.title: "Ultimate Showdown"
	quest.2FF250F3388474BC.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every road out of the colony runs past something with teeth.\"&r"
		""
		"Three clients post work here: &bThe Wardens' Lodge&r (monster hunters), &bBastion Watch&r (the Nether) and the &bTwilight Rangers&r."
		"&bDaily culls&r ask for a set number of kills and reset a day after you claim them. &bBoss bounties&r reset weekly and come in three grades: minor, major and apex."
		"Kills by anyone on your team count, but only while a bounty is open: kills made during its cooldown don't."
		"New tiers open as the team climbs the book. A locked bounty shows the quest it waits on."
	]
	quest.2FF250F3388474BC.quest_subtitle: "Monster culls and boss bounties"
	quest.2FF250F3388474BC.title: "The Bounty Board"
	quest.3057849BD4EAA1C4.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The Union signed a launch contract. We need mechanisms that survive liftoff.\"&r"
		"8 &6Hardened Precision Mechanisms&r. Send &6Precision Mechanisms&r through a second &bsequenced assembly&r: &bDeployers&r add a &6Titanium Nugget&r, an &6Iron Cogwheel&r and a &6Large Iron Cogwheel&r, five times round."
		"&eTip:&r an iron cogwheel is a shaft and a block of &6Industrial Iron&r. Some failed parts come back as iron cogwheels, so send those round again."
	]
	quest.3057849BD4EAA1C4.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Brassworks Union"
	quest.3057849BD4EAA1C4.title: "Space-Grade Gearing"
	quest.30B0881FABD5A8F6.quest_desc: [
		"Each &6Rocket Thruster&r is a Combustion Chamber, a Propeller and Titanium Sheets."
		"Heavier rockets and stronger gravity need more thrusters. The Rocket Station tells you how many your build needs."
		"&eTip:&r a small, light rocket gets away with fewer thrusters."
	]
	quest.30B0881FABD5A8F6.quest_subtitle: "More weight, more engines"
	quest.30B0881FABD5A8F6.title: "Thrusters"
	quest.30E8E6FF3E8F2032.quest_desc: [
		"Opens with &6Lunar Program&r: reactor pellets, space-grade mechanisms, crafting hardware and power by the tens of millions. Each order adds a roll of the &6Orbital Crate&r."
		"Lattice's order still needs &6The Network&r. Once every line runs, take on the &6World Engine&r."
	]
	quest.30E8E6FF3E8F2032.quest_subtitle: "Space-age industry, reset weekly"
	quest.30E8E6FF3E8F2032.title: "Tier V Orders"
	quest.30F0C2612F362B34.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"You've filled enough orders to be trusted with bigger ones.\"&r"
		"Pay &625 Contract Seals&r in Guild dues to rise to Journeyman."
		"Opens the &eJourneyman shelf&r at the Exchange and two monthly Grand Contracts: &bThe Great Railway&r and the &bHarvest Festival&r."
	]
	quest.30F0C2612F362B34.quest_subtitle: "25 Contract Seals"
	quest.30F0C2612F362B34.title: "Rank II: Journeyman"
	quest.312465333D785146.quest_desc: [
		"Daily orders you can fill on foot: meadow flowers, village maps, sniffer seeds and postcards."
		"Each pays &650 XP&r, &61 bevel&r and &61 Contract Seal&r, and comes back a day after it is claimed."
	]
	quest.312465333D785146.quest_subtitle: "Daily work close to home"
	quest.312465333D785146.title: "Tier I Orders"
	quest.315B81F97666ADEB.quest_desc: [
		"Fit a &6Distillation Controller&r to a &bFluid Tank&r at least three blocks tall to make a distillation tower."
		"Pump crude oil into the bottom level and heat the tower with a fuelled &bBlaze Burner&r. Every batch splits into &6Diesel&r and &6Gasoline&r."
		"Diesel Generators fuels are Starwright's standard engine fuel. Rockets need biofuel or hydrogen instead (see Liftoff)."
		"&eTip:&r the controller's Ponder scene shows where each fuel comes out."
	]
	quest.315B81F97666ADEB.quest_subtitle: "Crude in, fuel out"
	quest.315B81F97666ADEB.title: "Fractional Distillation"
	quest.3163F46F4CBA7A70.quest_desc: [
		"The other road to Frontier runs through the &bTwilight Forest&r."
		"Beat the &bNaga&r and the &bTwilight Lich&r in Twilight Expeditions, then tick this box to count them here."
		"&7Either road works. You only need one.&r"
	]
	quest.3163F46F4CBA7A70.quest_subtitle: "The Naga and the Lich"
	quest.3163F46F4CBA7A70.title: "Twilight Duo"
	quest.31A375AFB5FCFAED.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Your reactor's waste is our feedstock. Bring it to us in pellets.\"&r"
		"4 &6Plutonium Pellets&r and 4 &6Polonium Pellets&r. Spin &6Nuclear Waste&r into plutonium in an &bIsotopic Centrifuge&r, or turn it into polonium in a &bSolar Neutron Activator&r, which needs the sun."
		"A &bPressurized Reaction Chamber&r makes one pellet from 1,000 mB of either, water and &6Fluorite Dust&r. Each pellet costs 10,000 mB of waste."
		"&cRadiation:&r wear a full Hazmat Suit, and never break a tank or pipe that holds waste."
	]
	quest.31A375AFB5FCFAED.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Meridian Chemworks"
	quest.31A375AFB5FCFAED.title: "Reactor Byproducts"
	quest.31AC504774757F54.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Tonight's pairing dinner: our Noir with a proper Beef Wellington.\"&r"
		"4 &6Beef Wellingtons&r and 4 bottles of &6Noir Wine&r."
		"The Wellington bakes in the Farm \\& Charm &bStove&r from &6Lamb Ham&r (mutton through the Mincer), &6Dough&r and Candlelight's &6Mushroom Soup&r."
		"The soup cooks in a pot from mushrooms, butter, milk and a bottle of wine (any potion bottle works too), served into a bowl."
		"Noir Wine ferments in a &bFermentation Barrel&r from Red Grapejuice, sweet berries and an empty Wine Bottle."
	]
	quest.31AC504774757F54.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Old Vine Cellars"
	quest.31AC504774757F54.title: "Wine and Dine"
	quest.31CCD45298BB9D82.quest_desc: [
		"&7The workshop needs fire, and the fire lives below.&r"
		""
		"Build a &bNether Portal&r and step through. Starwright's &bAmplified Nether&r is 256 blocks tall, so bring building blocks, food and &6Fire Resistance&r potions."
		"&bYUNG's Better Nether Fortresses&r hold &bblaze spawners&r. Lootr gives every player their own chest loot, so nobody has to race."
		"Craft an &6Empty Blaze Burner&r from &6Iron Sheets&r and &6Netherrack&r, and carry home extra netherrack."
		"&eTip:&r keep this trip short. The deep Nether's bosses and netherite wait for Below and Beyond in Stage 3."
	]
	quest.31CCD45298BB9D82.quest_subtitle: "A short trip below"
	quest.31CCD45298BB9D82.title: "First Descent"
	quest.3297CB76AE5844EF.quest_desc: [
		"Select a track and place a &6Train Signal&r nearby. Signals split the line into segments, and a scheduled train won't enter a segment another train is using."
		"Scheduled trains never pass a signal from behind, so two-way track needs a second signal facing the other way. A wrench switches a signal to its brass mode, which keeps queued trains out of busy junctions."
		"Steam 'n' Rails adds &6Semaphores&r (on a fence or girder pole above a signal), couplers that join and split trains without disassembly, and track switches."
		"&cNote:&r snow layers and moss carpets can't case track here, because they can kick everyone off the server. Slab casings work fine."
	]
	quest.3297CB76AE5844EF.quest_subtitle: "Signals, semaphores and switches"
	quest.3297CB76AE5844EF.title: "Traffic Control"
	quest.32A8800E518D65E1.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"We're stringing lines to every homestead. Send wire.\"&r"
		"32 &6LV&r, 16 &6MV&r and 8 &6HV Wire Coils&r. Four wires around a stick craft four coils: copper for LV, electrum for MV, and steel with aluminium for HV."
		"Cut wire from plates with &6Wire Cutters&r or press ingots in a &bMetal Press&r with a wire mold. A &bRolling Mill&r also rolls copper plates into wire. Electrum is gold and silver alloyed in a &bKiln&r."
		"&eTip:&r the aluminium for HV wire comes from &6Bauxite Ore&r."
	]
	quest.32A8800E518D65E1.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Voltaic Grid Authority"
	quest.32A8800E518D65E1.title: "Wire for the Grid"
	quest.32AD0450CF4E8C54.quest_desc: [
		"&6Not Enough Trials&r also hides a rarer &bvertical trial chamber&r, built in tall layers instead of spread out."
		"Find one and step inside."
		"&eTip:&r it is a long fight, so pack spare food, blocks and a water bucket."
	]
	quest.32AD0450CF4E8C54.quest_subtitle: "The vertical trial chamber"
	quest.32AD0450CF4E8C54.title: "The Pit of 100 Trials"
	quest.330D20D3345F8BA2.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Construction Stick&r places a whole row or wall of the block you're facing, using blocks from your inventory. Iron and a stick make the Iron Stick; better metals reach farther."
		"Its keybinds lock placement to horizontal, vertical or one axis and open its options. Mistakes can be undone."
		"Smithing templates add upgrades: &bAngel&r places blocks in mid-air, and &bDestruction&r, &bReplacement&r and &bBattery&r do what they say."
		"Construction Sticks work on airships too."
		"Craft any Construction Stick."
	]
	quest.330D20D3345F8BA2.quest_subtitle: "Whole rows in one click"
	quest.330D20D3345F8BA2.title: "Sticky Situation"
	quest.331AD9EA11520B2E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Purification Chamber&r uses &6Oxygen&r to turn each ore into three &6Clumps&r."
		"Crush clumps into &6Dirty Dust&r with a &bCrusher&r, clean it in the Enrichment Chamber, then smelt: three ingots per ore."
		"Oxygen comes from your Electrolytic Separator; pipe it in with &bPressurized Tubes&r."
		"&eTip:&r it needs &6Advanced Control Circuits&r: a basic circuit plus Infused Alloy."
	]
	quest.331AD9EA11520B2E.quest_subtitle: "Ore tripling with oxygen"
	quest.331AD9EA11520B2E.title: "Continue Purifying"
	quest.33219DA310892441.quest_desc: [
		"The rarest armour trim of all, otherwise found only in Ancient City chests."
		"Copy it before you use it: 7 diamonds and &6Cobbled Deepslate&r in a crafting grid make two."
	]
	quest.33219DA310892441.quest_subtitle: "40 seals"
	quest.33219DA310892441.title: "Silence Trim Template"
	quest.33C383B7123DED6A.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Fruit that teleports you and shells that float. The End is a botanist's dream.\"&r"
		"In &bthe End&r, gather 32 &6Chorus Fruit&r, 4 &6Chorus Flowers&r and 4 &6Shulker Shells&r."
		"Chorus plants grow on the outer islands, and the flower at the tip of a branch drops itself when broken. &bShulkers&r guard the End cities."
		"&eTip:&r a chorus flower planted on end stone grows a whole new plant, and a shulker hit by another shulker's bullet can split in two."
	]
	quest.33C383B7123DED6A.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Field Survey Office"
	quest.33C383B7123DED6A.title: "Void Botany"
	quest.33DC2764E9A13B0B.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Physics Assembler&r (andesite casing, andesite alloy and a lever) turns a glued build into a &bSimulated Contraption&r."
		"Simulated Contraptions run on real &bSable&r physics: they have weight and momentum, and they can tip."
		"&eTip:&r practise with something small on the ground before you build up high."
	]
	quest.33DC2764E9A13B0B.quest_subtitle: "Real physics for your builds"
	quest.33DC2764E9A13B0B.title: "Applied Kinematics"
	quest.33EDD05571647127.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The new powder store needs walls that no blast, and no enderman, gets through.\"&r"
		"96 &6Concrete&r and 16 &6Leaded Concrete&r. Four sand, two gravel, two clay balls and a water bucket craft eight concrete. Add a &6Lead Plate&r, pressed from Mekanism's lead, to a block to lead it."
		"&eTip:&r Create makes the dry mix: a &bMillstone&r turns cobblestone into gravel, &bCrushing Wheels&r turn gravel into sand, and washing sand gives clay."
	]
	quest.33EDD05571647127.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Andesite Mill \\& Co."
	quest.33EDD05571647127.title: "Concrete Pour"
	quest.3402FD3EC68CC0E7.quest_desc: [
		"Eat a serving of every Brewin' and Chewin' meal."
		"Its &bKeg&r ferments drinks, cheeses, jerky, kimchi and pickles, and the &bCooking Pot&r handles its pastas, soups, pierogi and fondue."
		"Some brews only ferment in a warm or cold keg, so set heat or ice beside it."
		"&eTip:&r every new dish also counts toward your Spice of Life hearts."
	]
	quest.3402FD3EC68CC0E7.quest_subtitle: "Every Brewin' and Chewin' meal"
	quest.3402FD3EC68CC0E7.title: "Chef of the Ages"
	quest.34175E85BB4725CC.quest_desc: [
		"An &6Oxygen Sealer&r takes oxygen from behind and rotation from below, and fills an airtight room. &6Large Fans&r extend the volume."
		"Mechanical-craft it from an Oxygen Separator, a Circuit, a Fluid Tank, an &6Encased Fan&r, a shaft and titanium."
		"Build an airtight lunar base, feed the sealer from a Concentrator, and you can breathe inside."
	]
	quest.34175E85BB4725CC.quest_subtitle: "Air you can breathe indoors"
	quest.34175E85BB4725CC.title: "Seal the Base"
	quest.3472AA54D75D145C.quest_desc: [
		"Structure chests, barrels and chest minecarts are &bLootr&r containers. Every player gets their own copy of the loot, so nobody beats a friend to it."
		"&6Loot Integrations&r also stocks structure chests with modded gems, trinkets and materials."
		"&cCarry On can't lift loot chests.&r Loot them where they stand."
		"Open 10 Lootr containers."
	]
	quest.3472AA54D75D145C.quest_subtitle: "Ten containers, all your own"
	quest.3472AA54D75D145C.title: "Delightful Decade"
	quest.348139E23EE423A6.quest_desc: [
		"&7The Moon was the rehearsal.&r"
		""
		"Chart &bMars&r in your atlas, fit the &6Interplanetary Navigator&r, then fly there and set foot on Mars. Trips this long need the Navigator aboard."
		"&cDust storms and cold peaks:&r bring a full suit and spare air."
		"&7Landing on Mars also counts toward the Pinnacle world tier and opens more weekly contracts.&r"
	]
	quest.348139E23EE423A6.quest_subtitle: "Boots on red dust"
	quest.348139E23EE423A6.title: "One Giant Leap"
	quest.349467C10B1B5A1E.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our chef wants trophy fish for the window. Real monsters.\"&r"
		"2 &6Bigeye Tuna&r, 2 &6Willow Bream&r and 2 &6Blue Ice Pike&r, all epic catches on a Starcatcher rod."
		"Bigeye Tuna bite at night in temperate, lukewarm and cold oceans; Willow Bream at night in rivers that aren't frozen; Blue Ice Pike in the water of snowy plains, snowy taiga and other snowy or icy biomes."
		"&eTip:&r plan one long night: the tuna and the bream both bite only after dark."
	]
	quest.349467C10B1B5A1E.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Harbor Kitchens"
	quest.349467C10B1B5A1E.title: "Trophy Catch"
	quest.34E08A1392A73890.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Etching Table&r (a diamond, iron and planks) burns music from a URL onto a disc. Give it a &6Blank Music Disc&r and a &6Music Label&r (paper), then paste the link."
		"Blank discs come from smelting any music disc."
		"The &6Album Jukebox&r (a chest, a jukebox, a repeater and redstone) plays through a whole set of discs. The &6Boombox&r is a jukebox you can carry, and the &6Radio&r streams from a URL."
	]
	quest.34E08A1392A73890.quest_subtitle: "Your own music, on disc"
	quest.34E08A1392A73890.title: "Etched in Wax"
	quest.353FB8EEF951A241.quest_desc: [
		"The &bImproved Blast Furnace&r is built from &6Reinforced Blast Bricks&r. Iron and coal coke go in through the top; steel comes out the front and slag out the back."
		"Add up to two &6Blast Furnace Preheaters&r, one on each side. They use FE to blow in hot air and speed up the furnace."
		"&eTip:&r it outputs into belts and inventories by itself, so a steel line can run while you're away."
	]
	quest.353FB8EEF951A241.quest_subtitle: "Steel without babysitting"
	quest.353FB8EEF951A241.title: "Next Level Blasting"
	quest.359E83AFA74981DD.quest_desc: [
		"Craft &6Polished Rose Quartz&r above an &6Iron Sheet&r to make an &6Electron Tube&r."
		"Tubes go into Deployers, Mechanical Crafters, Brass Funnels and Tunnels, Smart Chutes and train signals."
		"&eTip:&r set up a small rose quartz line now. You'll want tubes by the dozen."
	]
	quest.359E83AFA74981DD.quest_subtitle: "A glowing spark on iron"
	quest.359E83AFA74981DD.title: "Electron Tubes"
	quest.35A037DCBBEFF3C5.quest_desc: [
		"Artifacts are odd, powerful trinkets: running shoes, a cloud in a bottle, a lucky scarf, an umbrella and dozens more."
		"They turn up in structure chests. Sometimes the chest bites back: that's a &cMimic&r, and it drops an artifact when it dies."
		"Wear them in your &bCurios&r slots, opened from your inventory."
		"Find any artifact."
	]
	quest.35A037DCBBEFF3C5.quest_subtitle: "Strange relics in old chests"
	quest.35A037DCBBEFF3C5.title: "Amateur Archaeologist"
	quest.35F2DD91D273EA29.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The fish market wants real ocean fish, not pond minnows.\"&r"
		"6 &6Sea Bass&r and 4 &6Redscaled Tuna&r, landed with a Starcatcher rod."
		"Fish from the surface. Sea Bass bite in any ocean during the day; Redscaled Tuna only at night, and only in temperate, lukewarm and cold oceans."
		"&eTip:&r a day at sea and the night after covers both. Hooks, bobbers and bait change the odds."
	]
	quest.35F2DD91D273EA29.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Harbor Kitchens"
	quest.35F2DD91D273EA29.title: "Ocean Catch"
	quest.363BCB9D40069845.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The coastal fleet is switching to farm fuel. Fill the tanker.\"&r"
		"A bulk order: 64,000 mB of &6Biodiesel&r. Press seeds into &6Plant Oil&r over a &bBasin&r, ferment crops with bone meal into &6Ethanol&r, and mix the two half and half in a &bMechanical Mixer&r."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r the &bBulk Fermenter&r is ground-only. It makes twice the ethanol of a basin with a &6Basin Lid&r."
		"&eTip:&r pipe the mixer's output straight into a &6Task Screen&r set to this order."
	]
	quest.363BCB9D40069845.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Bluewater Refinery"
	quest.363BCB9D40069845.title: "Biodiesel by the Tanker"
	quest.36A35AC3CBAF0A52.quest_desc: [
		"&7New ground, wide skies and a long first night ahead.&r"
		""
		"Tectonic, Terralith and Regions Unexplored shape this world: tall mountains, deep valleys and plenty of new biomes."
		"Punch a tree, make a &6Crafting Table&r and some tools, and pick a spot near water for your first base."
		"&eTip:&r rivers and coasts make good homes. Create's water wheels, coming in the Andesite Age, need moving water."
	]
	quest.36A35AC3CBAF0A52.quest_subtitle: "First hours on new ground"
	quest.36A35AC3CBAF0A52.title: "Landfall"
	quest.36B06ACDA228A8BC.quest_desc: [
		"The &bNight Lich&r haunts a tower in snowy lands."
		"Every 50 undead you kill (zombies, skeletons, husks, strays, drowned and their kin) drops a &6Soul Star&r. A Soul Star leads you to the nearest tower, and summoning the Lich takes four of them."
		"It drops &6Ancient Anima&r and several enchanted books."
	]
	quest.36B06ACDA228A8BC.quest_subtitle: "BoMD's Night Lich"
	quest.36B06ACDA228A8BC.title: "Night Vanquisher"
	quest.36F5D4190924FA08.quest_desc: [
		"Ender's Delight cooks the End: chorus pies and juice, shulker dishes, pearl pasta and stranger things."
		"&6Chorus Stew&r cooks in a cooking pot from chorus fruit and a chorus flower. It's served in a &6Shulker Bowl&r, crafted from a shulker shell."
		"Its &bEndstone Stove&r needs dragon's breath to craft."
		"Cook two Chorus Stews."
	]
	quest.36F5D4190924FA08.quest_subtitle: "Recipes from the outer islands"
	quest.36F5D4190924FA08.title: "Void Cuisine"
	quest.36FC3A39D74C0162.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Steering Wheel&r (andesite casing, a large cogwheel and a shaft) lets the pilot steer by hand."
		"A &6Gimbal Sensor&r (brass casing, a compass and a gyroscopic mechanism) knows which way is up, the start of keeping a ship level."
		"An &6Altitude Sensor&r and the &6Navigation Table&r help on long flights."
	]
	quest.36FC3A39D74C0162.quest_subtitle: "Steering and staying level"
	quest.36FC3A39D74C0162.title: "Steady As She Goes"
	quest.37EE2A6AF59CE27F.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Crops that have never seen the sun. We want to know how they do it.\"&r"
		"In the &bUndergarden&r, gather 4 &6Gloomgourds&r, 8 &6Droopfruit&r and 8 &6Underbeans&r."
		"Gloomgourds grow wild, like pumpkins. Droopfruit hangs from glowing &bdroopvines&r, and underbeans grow on low bushes; pick them when ripe."
		"&eTip:&r bring light and a bed. The Undergarden has no sky."
	]
	quest.37EE2A6AF59CE27F.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Field Survey Office"
	quest.37EE2A6AF59CE27F.title: "Undergarden Harvest"
	quest.385396B3B423388D.quest_desc: [
		"Mine titanium ore on the Moon for &6Raw Titanium&r and smelt it back home."
		"&6Lunar Sapphire&r grows in crystal clusters, a bit like amethyst. Crush clusters or blocks into &6Lunar Sapphire Shards&r, then polish the shards with &6Sandpaper&r."
		"&eTip:&r the Navigator at the end of this chapter needs that polished sapphire."
	]
	quest.385396B3B423388D.quest_subtitle: "Titanium and sapphire"
	quest.385396B3B423388D.title: "Lunar Haul"
	quest.38684D794DD2A3E9.quest_desc: [
		"Create: Mobile Packages. Put a &6Robo Bee&r (item vault, propellers, honeycomb) in a &6Robo Bee Port&r's bee slot, insert a package addressed to a friend's player name, and the bee flies it straight to them."
		"Ports pull packages from adjacent inventories, push arrivals into a chest when powered with redstone, and can send to another port whose address matches."
		"&eTip:&r in a hurry? Hold a package in your offhand and use a Robo Bee to send it yourself."
	]
	quest.38684D794DD2A3E9.quest_subtitle: "Robo-bees carry packages to players"
	quest.38684D794DD2A3E9.title: "Bee Mail"
	quest.38848A3BC1E4AB7D.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Anyone can sell iron. We pay for what only a starfarer brings home.\"&r"
		""
		"The Star Charter posts &bweekly&r orders for the fleet and the space program. Four clients use it: Skyward Freight (airship parts), the Lunar Survey Corps (the Moon and Earth orbit), the Ares Mining Consortium (Mars) and the Sunward Expedition (Venus and Mercury)."
		"Tier IV opens with your first airship and Tier V with the Lunar Program. Some orders also wait on a planet: open a locked one to see which quest it needs."
		"Every teammate claims their own XP and coins from each order; the &6Contract Seals&r and the roll of &6Space Rations&r are paid once per team. The octagon orders are bulk jobs sized for a &bTask Screen&r."
		"&cWaystones never reach the planets, and Mekanism teleporters only do after Interplanetary Network,&r so plan each haul around a rocket."
	]
	quest.38848A3BC1E4AB7D.quest_subtitle: "Freight for the skies and the planets"
	quest.38848A3BC1E4AB7D.title: "The Star Charter"
	quest.38932C82F971D1C9.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our reactor contractor needs advanced circuits by the weekend.\"&r"
		"16 &6Advanced Control Circuits&r. In a &bMetallurgic Infuser&r, redstone turns &6Osmium Ingots&r into &6Basic Control Circuits&r and &6Copper&r into &6Infused Alloy&r. A basic circuit between two infused alloys crafts an advanced one."
		"&eTip:&r the infuser can also upgrade a basic circuit straight to advanced with more redstone."
	]
	quest.38932C82F971D1C9.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Meridian Chemworks"
	quest.38932C82F971D1C9.title: "Circuit Order"
	quest.392E0A600200162C.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Readers can't get enough of the blossoms. Send us postcards!\"&r"
		"Visit a &bSakura Grove&r and bring 2 &6Photographs&r."
		"Load an Exposure &6Camera&r with film and take your shots. &6Black and White Film&r develops by crafting it with a &6Water Bottle&r; print it in a &bLightroom&r with &6Paper&r and &6Black Dye&r."
		"&eTip:&r Main Street's camera quests walk through every step."
	]
	quest.392E0A600200162C.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from The Gazette"
	quest.392E0A600200162C.title: "Postcards from Sakura Grove"
	quest.395C5864871A86E6.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Magic Map Focus&r from a &6Raven Feather&r, &6Torchberries&r and &6Glowstone Dust&r, then craft it with paper into a &6Blank Magic Map&r."
		"Use the map to draw the area around you. It shows the forest's biomes and marks the boss landmarks."
		"&eTip:&r ravens drop the feathers, and torchberries hang from cave ceilings."
	]
	quest.395C5864871A86E6.quest_subtitle: "A map that marks the bosses"
	quest.395C5864871A86E6.title: "I Can See Forever"
	quest.39B8C4970A4FAF0D.quest_desc: [
		"Encode recipes onto &6Blank Patterns&r in a &6Pattern Encoding Terminal&r and load them into an &6ME Pattern Provider&r."
		"A &6Molecular Assembler&r touching the provider runs its crafting patterns and returns the results."
		"Jobs need a &bCrafting CPU&r: a solid box of crafting blocks with at least one &6Crafting Storage&r. A lone 1k Crafting Storage works."
		"&6Processing patterns&r push their inputs into any machine beside the provider, like a furnace, a Mekanism machine or a Create &bBasin&r. Send the output back into the provider."
		"Middle-click a craftable item in the terminal to order it."
	]
	quest.39B8C4970A4FAF0D.quest_subtitle: "Autocrafting comes online"
	quest.39B8C4970A4FAF0D.title: "Crafting Maestro"
	quest.39E91131D114120C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Digital Miner&r digs out a big area by filter, taking only what you ask for. Its recipe needs a whole &6Robit&r."
		"Set its radius and height range, add filters, and give it plenty of FE and an inventory to fill."
		"It also works aboard airships through the Aeronautics compat."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r Mekanism chunkloading is switched off. Keep miners inside your team's force-load budget."
	]
	quest.39E91131D114120C.quest_subtitle: "The Digital Miner"
	quest.39E91131D114120C.title: "Trapped Inside"
	quest.3A1216C6DA812B19.quest_desc: [
		"The &bLabyrinth&r is sunk into the Swamp, and the &6Minoshroom&r waits at its heart."
		"It drops &6Meef Stroganoff&r. Eat it: its strength is what lets you cross the &bFire Swamp&r without burning."
		"&eTip:&r it is a maze down there, so mark your path as you go."
	]
	quest.3A1216C6DA812B19.quest_subtitle: "The Minoshroom's Labyrinth"
	quest.3A1216C6DA812B19.title: "Mighty Stroganoff"
	quest.3AF3A3138D8CDFF3.quest_desc: [
		"HerbalBrews brews in a &bTea Kettle&r (iron or copper and a stick) set on a stove: its own &bStove&r (a campfire, cobblestone and an iron nugget), Farm \\& Charm's or Farmer's Delight's."
		"Kettle recipes take leaves or beans, sometimes sugar, and a glass bottle: green, black and oolong tea, hibiscus, lavender, rooibos, yerba mate and coffee."
		"&6Tea Blossoms&r come from breaking flowers with shears. Pack tea leaves into blocks and let them dry in the sun."
		"Coffee and hibiscus grow wild in jungles, lavender and yerba mate in the mountains, and rooibos in savannas."
		"The &bBrewing Cauldron&r turns your brews into &6Flasks&r for the road."
	]
	quest.3AF3A3138D8CDFF3.quest_subtitle: "Teas, coffee and flasks"
	quest.3AF3A3138D8CDFF3.title: "Tea Time"
	quest.3B833B34F071CD8D.quest_desc: [
		"Wild &6grape&r bushes grow in forests, plains, swamps and along rivers, and jungles, savannas and taigas have their own kinds. Their seeds start a vineyard."
		"Drop grapes into a &bGrapevine Pot&r and jump on them to press juice, then collect it in empty &6Wine Bottles&r."
		"A &bFermentation Barrel&r turns juice into wine. Red Wine, for one, takes red grape juice, sugar and an empty Wine Bottle. Apples go through the &bApple Press&r for cider."
		"Wine ages with world time, so bottles keep improving while the server runs, even when you're offline. Older wine has stronger effects, so keep a cellar."
		"Place a Grapevine Pot and make any wine."
	]
	quest.3B833B34F071CD8D.quest_subtitle: "Vineyards and the wine cellar"
	quest.3B833B34F071CD8D.title: "Juice It Up!"
	quest.3C3A582538136380.quest_desc: [
		"The first rare stock: Totems of Undying, sniffer eggs and the Wayfarer armour trims, plus Reactor Crates."
		"&7Opens when your team holds the Expert rank.&r"
	]
	quest.3C3A582538136380.quest_subtitle: "Opens at Expert rank"
	quest.3C3A582538136380.title: "Expert Shelf"
	quest.3C4779C99795F2FA.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every ledger in the colony, backed up twice.\"&r"
		"64 &616k ME Storage Components&r and 16 &664k ME Storage Components&r."
		"Components are crafted from processors and certus; an &bInscriber&r line and a pattern-driven crafting CPU make short work of it."
	]
	quest.3C4779C99795F2FA.quest_subtitle: "Monthly Grand Contract from Lattice Data Exchange"
	quest.3C4779C99795F2FA.title: "The Data Vault"
	quest.3CA89C8F29BEC3EA.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Ships keep vanishing over the deep trench. You know what to do.\"&r"
		"Kill &bThe Leviathan&r: bring an &6Abyssal Sacrifice&r to the &bAltar of Abyss&r in a &bSunken City&r. An &6Eye of Abyss&r finds one in the deep ocean."
		"The sacrifice takes a nautilus shell, a heart of the sea, an &6Athame&r, &6Crystallized Coral&r and blocks of diamond, emerald, gold, iron and amethyst. Deepling Priests and Warlocks drop athames and Coral Golems the coral fragments; all of them roam deep oceans."
		"&cThe Leviathan can't be hurt out of the water.&r Bring water breathing and a way to see."
	]
	quest.3CA89C8F29BEC3EA.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.3CA89C8F29BEC3EA.title: "Bounty: The Leviathan"
	quest.3CAD5FEE8C2E015E.quest_desc: [
		"&7Two great beasts down. The climb gets steeper from here.&r"
		""
		"The Hydra and the Netherite Monstrosity have fallen. Tick the box and claim the reward to move your team to &bWorld Tier: Ascent&r."
		"Mobs hit harder again, and the loot keeps pace."
		"&eAscent opens:&r Ancient Cities and the Warden in Below and Beyond, and the Twilight Forest's later bosses."
	]
	quest.3CAD5FEE8C2E015E.quest_subtitle: "The climb steepens"
	quest.3CAD5FEE8C2E015E.title: "World Tier: Ascent"
	quest.3CC7D60810C89559.quest_desc: [
		"&7Your first trip was a quick dash for blazes and quartz. This one goes deeper.&r"
		""
		"The &bAmplified Nether&r stretches up to 256 blocks tall: towering cliffs, deep basins and very long falls."
		"Its big sites hold the best loot: deep &bYUNG's fortresses&r, &bMoog's Nether structures&r, and Dungeons and Taverns' &bNether Keeps&r and &bPiglin Donjons&r. Lootr gives every player their own chests."
		"&6My Nether's Delight&r turns hoglins and striders into dinner."
		"&eTip:&r pack fire resistance and plenty of blocks to bridge with."
		"Step inside a YUNG's Nether fortress."
	]
	quest.3CC7D60810C89559.quest_subtitle: "Deeper this time"
	quest.3CC7D60810C89559.title: "Return to the Nether"
	quest.3CD7A7AAF18DE64B.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Factory Gauge&r (stock link and precision mechanism) joins your network like a link: right-click a Stock Link with it before placing."
		"On a packager it watches that inventory: give it an item and an address, hold right-click to set a target amount, and it reorders from the network whenever stock runs low."
		"Placed anywhere else, it watches the whole network and sends ingredients off to be processed, so a board of gauges becomes a self-restocking factory."
		"&eTip:&r a 3x3 grid of wrench-connected &bMechanical Crafters&r can craft gauge orders directly, and a &6Re-Packager&r keeps split orders together."
	]
	quest.3CD7A7AAF18DE64B.quest_subtitle: "Factory Gauges keep the shelves full"
	quest.3CD7A7AAF18DE64B.title: "High Logistics"
	quest.3DACB27D87A0A6E5.quest_desc: [
		"The &bSupercritical Phase Shifter&r (SPS) turns polonium into antimatter, and a &bChemical Crystallizer&r turns that into &6Antimatter Pellets&r."
		"Its casing needs plutonium and polonium pellets with HDPE, and it drinks enormous power. Fusion helps."
		"Mekanism: Ponders shows the multiblock."
	]
	quest.3DACB27D87A0A6E5.quest_subtitle: "Antimatter from polonium"
	quest.3DACB27D87A0A6E5.title: "Impossible Material"
	quest.3DD305F3E14D2377.quest_desc: [
		"Land on &bMercury&r, closest to the sun, in the same space-rated suit. It needs all three unit quests, like Venus."
		"Mine its tungsten ore and smelt &6Tungsten Ingots&r. Mercury is the only place it's found."
		"&eTip:&r Crushing Wheels turn tungsten ore into Crushed Raw Tungsten, which smelts into ingots too."
	]
	quest.3DD305F3E14D2377.quest_subtitle: "Mercury and its tungsten"
	quest.3DD305F3E14D2377.title: "Swift Messenger"
	quest.3E3D3188ED1A2659.quest_desc: [
		"The collector's cabinet: far-realm armour trims, the rarest records and Enchanted Golden Apples."
		"&7Opens when your team holds the Grandmaster rank.&r"
	]
	quest.3E3D3188ED1A2659.quest_subtitle: "Opens at Grandmaster rank"
	quest.3E3D3188ED1A2659.title: "Grandmaster Shelf"
	quest.3EA22635E846D88E.quest_desc: [
		"Opens with &6Steel Backbone&r: steel, treated wood, wire, concrete and diesel, every day."
		"Bluewater Refinery also posts a weekly &bbulk order&r here, sized for a factory feeding a Task Screen. Bulk orders add a roll of the &6Foundry Crate&r."
	]
	quest.3EA22635E846D88E.quest_subtitle: "Steel, wire and fuel, reset daily"
	quest.3EA22635E846D88E.title: "Tier III Orders"
	quest.3EA6265E98899670.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Stock Link&r on a packager shares that inventory with a logistics network. To join an existing network, right-click its link with the new one before placing it."
		"Put a &6Stock Ticker&r on the network with a seated mob or a blaze burner in front of it: that's your &bStock Keeper&r. Right-click the keeper, pick items and an address, and the order is packed and sent."
		"&cKnown issue:&r keep a static item in hotbar slot 9 while the keeper's screen is open, or the server kicks you. The &6Portable Stock Ticker&r (this chapter's capstone) doesn't have the problem."
		"Keep links and keepers inside your claim, 6+ blocks from its edge, and never bind to another team's network."
	]
	quest.3EA6265E98899670.quest_subtitle: "A Stock Keeper fetches what you ask for"
	quest.3EA6265E98899670.title: "Order Up!"
	quest.3EE1A6E706C272CD.quest_desc: [
		"&bEnd ships&r float beside some End cities, with an &6Elytra&r in an item frame. Lootr makes that frame per-player, so every friend takes their own pair."
		"Dungeons and Taverns adds lone End ships too. Their vaults hold an elytra, and the key comes from its End Castle."
		"&eGetting there:&r End cities sit on the outer islands. Each dragon kill opens a new End gateway out to them."
		"&eTip:&r shulkers guard End cities. Milk clears their levitation."
	]
	quest.3EE1A6E706C272CD.quest_subtitle: "Raid an End ship"
	quest.3EE1A6E706C272CD.title: "Wings for Everyone"
	quest.3FC2CA4C5B55A027.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The orbital station needs hull plate and light, delivered in person.\"&r"
		"Visit &bEarth Orbit&r (set it as the Rocket Station's destination) and deliver 64 &6Titanium Sheetmetal&r and 16 &6Glowstone Lamps&r."
		"Four Titanium Sheets craft four sheetmetal, or a stonecutter makes one per sheet. A lamp is four sheets around a Glowstone block, two per craft."
		"&cNothing to stand on up there:&r bring blocks, a full suit and spare air."
	]
	quest.3FC2CA4C5B55A027.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Lunar Survey Corps"
	quest.3FC2CA4C5B55A027.title: "Station Supplies to Orbit"
	quest.3FCB6F872ECD12C2.quest_desc: [
		"Applied Create's pattern providers feed a &bMechanical Crafter&r array, placing every ingredient in the right crafter. They handle Create mechanical recipes and plain shaped ones."
		"Encode a &bprocessing&r pattern with the recipe's inputs and output, slot it in, and set the provider against any crafter in a connected array."
		"The &6Andesite Pattern Provider&r holds 9 patterns. The &6Brass Pattern Provider&r holds 36, and you build it on a 3x3 crafter array."
		"&7Stress Storage Cells can't be crafted in Starwright, so the ME Gearbox has no stored stress to export.&r"
	]
	quest.3FCB6F872ECD12C2.quest_subtitle: "Applied Create joins the works"
	quest.3FCB6F872ECD12C2.title: "Through Mechanical Crafters"
	quest.4026479B02A84582.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The far side of the void, on our front page. Readers will faint.\"&r"
		"Step into an &bEnd City&r and bring 4 &6Photographs&r."
		"End cities stand on the outer islands. Each dragon kill opens a new &bEnd Gateway&r out to them."
		"&eTip:&r an &bEnd Ship&r moored alongside makes the best shot. Milk clears a shulker's levitation."
	]
	quest.4026479B02A84582.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from The Gazette"
	quest.4026479B02A84582.title: "Cities at the Edge"
	quest.402B2804288D4E44.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Task Screen&r (a book and stone) shows one quest task on a wall and &baccepts deliveries directly&r: items from a funnel, chute or hopper, fluids from a pipe, and FE from a cable."
		"Place it, then use the &6Task Screen Configurator&r (a screen and a stick) on it to pick the contract task. Bigger screens (3x3 up to 7x7) are crafted from smaller ones."
		"&eTip:&r bulk orders, fluid orders and energy orders are sized for this. &cEnergy orders can only be filled through a screen.&r"
	]
	quest.402B2804288D4E44.quest_subtitle: "Let the factory fill the order"
	quest.402B2804288D4E44.title: "Task Screens"
	quest.404902FEDEEE9AD5.quest_desc: [
		"&bExposure: Space&r turns an Exposure &6Camera&r into a telescope. Camera basics are on Main Street."
		"Craft a &6Space Filter&r (iron nuggets, an amethyst shard and a glass pane) and a &6Normal Telescopic Lens&r (built around a &6Spyglass&r and a &6Copper Block&r; EMI shows the rest)."
		"Fit both to your camera and photograph stars, planets and nebulae at night."
	]
	quest.404902FEDEEE9AD5.quest_subtitle: "Your camera, now a telescope"
	quest.404902FEDEEE9AD5.title: "Space Filter"
	quest.405F306B6BDC7E62.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every lamp, every workshop, every winter. Send power.\"&r"
		"Deliver &6200 million FE&r."
		"&cOnly a Task Screen accepts energy:&r set one to this task and run a cable from your generators into it. It takes up to 250,000 FE per tick."
		"Spare capacity from a Mekanism reactor, IE generators or Create alternators all counts."
	]
	quest.405F306B6BDC7E62.quest_subtitle: "Monthly Grand Contract from the Voltaic Grid Authority"
	quest.405F306B6BDC7E62.title: "Light Up the Colony"
	quest.408A0F7E64D71534.quest_desc: [
		"Goods for builders and anglers, Foundry Crates, banner patterns and the backpack Feeding Upgrade."
		"&7Opens when your team holds the Specialist rank.&r"
	]
	quest.408A0F7E64D71534.quest_subtitle: "Opens at Specialist rank"
	quest.408A0F7E64D71534.title: "Specialist Shelf"
	quest.40CA9ECEACECD431.quest_desc: [
		"&7Envelope, burner, propellers and a deck to stand on. Time to cast off.&r"
		""
		"Build a small hull with a balloon, a &6Hot Air Burner&r and a &6Propeller Bearing&r. Assemble it with a &6Physics Assembler&r and fly."
		"This quest grants your team the &bAirwright&r stage, which unlocks every &6Icarus&r wing recipe."
		"&cClaims stop at the ship.&r Protect it with a Contraption Claim Block next."
		""
		"&eYou also receive a &6Wingwright's Licence&e. &bIcarus wings&e use it in place of an elytra, and it comes back after crafting."
	]
	quest.40CA9ECEACECD431.quest_subtitle: "Assemble it, fly it"
	quest.40CA9ECEACECD431.title: "Maiden Voyage"
	quest.40DE29389C5CC2D7.quest_desc: [
		"Throw them for a quick burst of experience."
		"Handy before a round at the &benchanting table&r or a costly anvil repair."
	]
	quest.40DE29389C5CC2D7.quest_subtitle: "4 seals"
	quest.40DE29389C5CC2D7.title: "Bottles o' Enchanting x16"
	quest.40EE6855E2F4FD25.quest_desc: [
		"Every player already has a personal bank account. A &bBlaze Banker&r opens a separate one in the banker's name, made for a team or a town fund."
		"Craft a &6Banking Guide&r (a cog coin, a sturdy sheet and paper) and use it on a placed &bBlaze Burner&r to turn it into a Blaze Banker."
		"Put a &6Bank Card&r in its card slot to bind the card to the banker's account. Players you trust in the banker get full access."
		"&eTip:&r breaking a Blaze Banker gives back the burner and the guide."
		"Craft a Banking Guide to finish."
	]
	quest.40EE6855E2F4FD25.quest_subtitle: "A shared purse for the team"
	quest.40EE6855E2F4FD25.title: "Open an Account"
	quest.41267FEC24FC3323.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Naga&r coils inside the walled &bNaga Courtyard&r. It is fast and hits hard when it charges, so keep moving."
		"Its &6Naga Scales&r make a sturdy chestplate and leggings. Beating it lifts the barrier around the &bLich Tower&r."
		"The Naga and the Lich together count toward &bWorld Tier Frontier&r for your team. See Bosses \\& Tiers."
	]
	quest.41267FEC24FC3323.quest_subtitle: "The serpent of the courtyard"
	quest.41267FEC24FC3323.title: "The Naga"
	quest.414E208959E8A428.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Hull plate for the ore freighters. Martian steel, and plenty of it.\"&r"
		"Compact a Titanium Ingot, &6Raw Martian Iron&r and &6Volcanic Ash&r in a heated &bBasin&r under a &bMechanical Press&r: two &6Martian Steel Ingots&r per press."
		"Martian iron ore and volcanic ash both come from Mars; the titanium can come from home or the Moon."
		"&eTip:&r a small press line at your Mars colony saves hauling raw ore home."
	]
	quest.414E208959E8A428.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Ares Mining Consortium"
	quest.414E208959E8A428.title: "Hull Steel from Mars"
	quest.4170375D86F0A024.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every bus, plane and assembler we build eats cores.\"&r"
		"16 &6Formation Cores&r and 16 &6Annihilation Cores&r. Each recipe makes two from a &6Logic Processor&r and &6Fluix Dust&r, with &6Certus Quartz&r for formation or &6Nether Quartz&r for annihilation."
		"&eTip:&r a Create &bMillstone&r grinds fluix crystals into dust."
	]
	quest.4170375D86F0A024.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Lattice Data Exchange"
	quest.4170375D86F0A024.title: "Cores for the Exchange"
	quest.41C3943A1F9B53C1.quest_desc: [
		"Some meals are too big for one plate. A &bfeast&r is placed as a block and served out portion by portion, so cook for the whole crew."
		"&6Roast Chicken&r is a good first one: cooked chicken, a baked potato, bread, a carrot, an onion and an egg, crafted with a bowl."
		"&6Honey Glazed Ham&r, &6Shepherd's Pie&r, &6Gleaming Salad&r and the &6Rice Roll Medley&r are crafted too, and the &6Stuffed Pumpkin&r cooks in a pot."
		"Most feasts serve into a &6Bowl&r: right-click the placed feast with one in hand."
		"Place any feast to finish."
	]
	quest.41C3943A1F9B53C1.quest_subtitle: "Cook for the whole crew"
	quest.41C3943A1F9B53C1.title: "A Glorious Feast"
	quest.421A5DDB52CF8411.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Set Levitite can't be picked back up, so the shipyard casts its own. Send the blend.\"&r"
		"16,000 mB of &6Levitite Blend&r. Crush End Stone into &6End Stone Powder&r; a heated &bMechanical Mixer&r turns four powder, two zinc nuggets and 500 mB of water into 500 mB of blend."
		"Hand it in by the bucket from the quest screen, or pipe it into a &bTask Screen&r."
		"&cHeat crystallizes poured blend:&r keep spills away from torches, fire and Blaze Burners."
	]
	quest.421A5DDB52CF8411.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Skyward Freight"
	quest.421A5DDB52CF8411.title: "Blend for the Shipyard"
	quest.424BDA7957FE98A4.quest_desc: [
		"Hostile Neural Networks simulates mobs instead of spawning them. Right-click a mob with a &6Model Framework&r to build its &6Data Model&r."
		"Put the model in a &6Deep Learner&r and hold it while you fight that mob. Each kill trains the model."
		"A &6Simulation Chamber&r runs a trained model on FE and &6Prediction Matrices&r and prints &6Predictions&r. The &6Loot Fabricator&r turns predictions into the mob's real drops."
		"&eNote:&r the Loot Fabricator needs a &6Netherite Ingot&r, so bring one back from the deep Nether."
	]
	quest.424BDA7957FE98A4.quest_subtitle: "A mob farm without mobs"
	quest.424BDA7957FE98A4.title: "Neural Networks"
	quest.42EA07B609E4D05B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Out here, the gear you find matters as much as the gear you make.&r"
		""
		"Apotheosis rolls &baffixes&r onto weapons and armor from mobs and chests. The name's color shows the rarity, from gray Common through green, blue and purple to orange Mythic, and Loot Beams light dropped gear in the same color."
		"Affix gear can also carry &bsockets&r for Apotheosis gems, which drop from monsters too."
		"Better Combat gives every weapon its own swings and combos, and Combat Roll adds a dodge roll on its own key."
		"&eNote:&r your team's World Tier, raised in the &bBosses \\& Tiers&r chapter, sets how dangerous and how rewarding the world gets."
		"Pick up any affixed item."
	]
	quest.42EA07B609E4D05B.quest_subtitle: "Loot with a story"
	quest.42EA07B609E4D05B.title: "Touched by Fate"
	quest.444DD73252255ACF.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every board in the colony knows the name.\"&r"
		"Pay &61,000 Contract Seals&r to become a Legend of the Guild, the highest rank there is."
		"Opens the &eLegend shelf&r, the Grand Contract &bThe Sunward Charter&r and the Exchange's &6Patron of the Guild&r."
	]
	quest.444DD73252255ACF.quest_subtitle: "1,000 Contract Seals"
	quest.444DD73252255ACF.title: "Rank VII: Legend of the Guild"
	quest.4474A9C47944BA89.quest_desc: [
		"The &bUndergarden&r is a dark, forgotten world deep below. Your ticket is the &6Catalyst&r: four copper ingots, four stone and an ender pearl."
		"Build a frame shaped like a Nether portal from &bstone bricks&r (mossy, cracked or chiseled bricks, deepslate bricks and deepslate tiles work too), then use the Catalyst on it."
		"&eTip:&r there's no sky down there, so bring plenty of light. Beds do work, so you can set a spawn point near the portal."
	]
	quest.4474A9C47944BA89.quest_subtitle: "A portal of stone bricks"
	quest.4474A9C47944BA89.title: "One Ticket Please"
	quest.447925ABBEF67B2A.quest_desc: [
		"Tier I orders need nothing more than a furnace, a crafting table and some legwork: bricks, charcoal, glass and lamps."
		"Each one comes back a day after you claim it."
	]
	quest.447925ABBEF67B2A.quest_subtitle: "Furnace work, reset daily"
	quest.447925ABBEF67B2A.title: "Tier I Orders"
	quest.44A4643E12825614.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Closer to the Sun than anyone has lived. We need the best you make.\"&r"
		"128 &6Durasteel&r and 256 &6Tungsten Ingots&r."
		"Tungsten comes from Mercury's ores; Durasteel comes out of the &bMetallurgic Infuser&r, as it did for the Inner Worlds."
	]
	quest.44A4643E12825614.quest_subtitle: "Monthly Grand Contract from the Sunward Expedition"
	quest.44A4643E12825614.title: "The Sunward Charter"
	quest.453514A41434FD4E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Budding Certus&r grows buds like amethyst. Only a full &6Certus Quartz Cluster&r drops crystals (four, more with Fortune); younger buds drop dust."
		"A &bGrowth Accelerator&r (it needs a Fluix Block) touching the budding block makes it grow far faster. Power it through its top or bottom with FE, AE or a Crank."
		"Flawed, Chipped and Damaged blocks wear down as they grow. Throw one, or a &6Certus Quartz Block&r, into water with &6Charged Certus&r to raise it a tier."
		"&eTip:&r more accelerators help, but every covered side of a budding block slows its buds, so don't box it in."
	]
	quest.453514A41434FD4E.quest_subtitle: "A certus garden at home"
	quest.453514A41434FD4E.title: "Accelerator Is an Understatement"
	quest.4572AA26D4750963.quest_desc: [
		"&bIgnis&r rules the &bBurning Arena&r in the Nether. An &6Eye of Flame&r (an Eye of Ender, blaze powder, netherite scrap and soul sand) leads there."
		"Clear the arena's guards, then use &6Burning Ashes&r on the &bAltar of Fire&r to summon it."
		"&eTip:&r bring fire resistance."
		"Its prize is the &6Ignitium Ingot&r."
	]
	quest.4572AA26D4750963.quest_subtitle: "Cataclysm's Ignis"
	quest.4572AA26D4750963.title: "The Extinguished Fire"
	quest.45A23B73D5F9D348.quest_desc: [
		"Infuse an &6Osmium Ingot&r with redstone to make a &6Basic Control Circuit&r."
		"Each tier builds on the last: a basic circuit with Infused Alloy makes an &6Advanced&r one, Reinforced Alloy makes &6Elite&r and Atomic Alloy makes &6Ultimate&r."
		"&eTip:&r machine tiers and factories eat circuits, so keep a stack."
	]
	quest.45A23B73D5F9D348.quest_subtitle: "Control circuits"
	quest.45A23B73D5F9D348.title: "Tricking a Rock Into Thinking"
	quest.45A43915474CAF5A.quest_desc: [
		"&7Ascent reached. The deeper forest is waiting.&r"
		""
		"The &bKnight Stronghold&r lies beneath the Dark Forest. Fight down through it and defeat the &6Knight Phantoms&r."
		"Beating them opens the &bDark Tower&r, home of carminite and the Ur-Ghast."
	]
	quest.45A43915474CAF5A.quest_subtitle: "The Knight Stronghold"
	quest.45A43915474CAF5A.title: "Carminite Acclimation"
	quest.4612D395724E7B7B.quest_desc: [
		"Climb the &bDark Tower&r and bring down the &6Ur-Ghast&r at its top."
		"Its &6Fiery Tears&r, like the Hydra's blood, turn an iron ingot into a &6Fiery Ingot&r for fiery tools and armour."
	]
	quest.4612D395724E7B7B.quest_subtitle: "The Ur-Ghast of the Dark Tower"
	quest.4612D395724E7B7B.title: "Tears of Fire"
	quest.463775D7B1A9B895.quest_desc: [
		"The Mekanism &6Jetpack&r burns hydrogen. Split water into hydrogen and oxygen in an &bElectrolytic Separator&r, then fill the jetpack in a &bChemical Tank&r."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r its recipe also needs a Create Aeronautics part, so it comes after your first ship. Check EMI."
		"It has normal and hover modes; switch with Mekanism's jetpack mode key."
	]
	quest.463775D7B1A9B895.quest_subtitle: "A jetpack that burns hydrogen"
	quest.463775D7B1A9B895.title: "Hydrogen Powered Flight"
	quest.46F873267A32958C.quest_desc: [
		"Six templates from Trail Ruins and Trial Chambers: &6Wayfinder&r, &6Raiser&r, &6Shaper&r, &6Host&r, &6Flow&r and &6Bolt&r."
		"Applying a trim at a &bSmithing Table&r uses the template up, so copy each one in a crafting grid first."
	]
	quest.46F873267A32958C.quest_subtitle: "15 seals"
	quest.46F873267A32958C.title: "Ruin and Trial Trim Set"
	quest.477E437640216DF5.quest_desc: [
		"Goods for skyfarers: Space Rations, Orbital Crates, more armour trims and a spare Elytra for teams who freed the End."
		"&7Opens when your team holds the Master rank.&r"
	]
	quest.477E437640216DF5.quest_subtitle: "Opens at Master rank"
	quest.477E437640216DF5.title: "Master Shelf"
	quest.47C733BE1C436199.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &6Wired Modem&r on the computer and on each machine, join them with &6Networking Cable&r, and right-click each modem until chat says its peripheral is connected."
		""
		"A Create &6Stressometer&r (craft a Speedometer, then convert it in the crafting grid) reports getStress() and getStressCapacity()."
		"Mekanism Energy Cubes and Crafts \\& Additions Accumulators report their stored energy too."
		"Draw it all on your monitor as bars and numbers, refreshed every second."
		"&7Hint: peripheral.find(\"Create_Stressometer\") finds the gauge for you."
	]
	quest.47C733BE1C436199.quest_subtitle: "Your whole grid on one screen"
	quest.47C733BE1C436199.title: "Stress Dashboard"
	quest.4846E08EDA173D1E.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our plastics line runs on resin, and we can't refine it fast enough.\"&r"
		"8,000 mB of &6Phenolic Resin&r from an IE &bRefinery&r. With a &6Silver Plate&r as catalyst it turns &6Ethanol&r into &6Acetaldehyde&r; with no catalyst, acetaldehyde and &6Creosote Oil&r refine into resin."
		"Diesel Generators ethanol works, so the fermenters from your fuel line can feed it."
		"&eTip:&r a catalyst is never used up, but it has to go in by hand."
	]
	quest.4846E08EDA173D1E.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Bluewater Refinery"
	quest.4846E08EDA173D1E.title: "Resin for the Plastics Line"
	quest.4863E5F2D5609288.quest_desc: [
		"&bCarry On&r: hold the Carry key (sneak by default) and right-click with empty hands to pick up a chest, a block or a small animal. Right-click again to set it down. Chests keep their contents."
		"&cRefused on purpose:&r loot chests, urns, Create, IE, Mekanism, AE2 and Northstar machines, contraptions and ships, bosses, vehicles and players. Those are dupe and corruption guards, not bugs."
	]
	quest.4863E5F2D5609288.quest_subtitle: "Carry On moves chests whole"
	quest.4863E5F2D5609288.title: "Lift With Your Legs"
	quest.49BDF026EE8B2904.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The Storm Empress has taken the sea lanes. Take them back.\"&r"
		"Kill &bScylla&r, the Storm Empress, in her &bAcropolis&r in warm oceans. An &6Eye of Storm&r leads there."
		"After each defeat she leaves a &bBoss Respawner&r; use another Eye of Storm on it to call her back."
		"Her prizes are &6Lacrima&r and &6Essence of the Storm&r."
	]
	quest.49BDF026EE8B2904.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.49BDF026EE8B2904.title: "Bounty: Scylla"
	quest.4A16E4A9D510E5A1.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Hydra&r lairs in the &bFire Swamp&r. Its heads bite and breathe fire, so bring Fire Resistance and plenty of food."
		"Beating it opens the &bKnight Stronghold&r in the Dark Forest."
		"It also counts toward &bWorld Tier Ascent&r, together with the Netherite Monstrosity."
	]
	quest.4A16E4A9D510E5A1.quest_subtitle: "Three heads in the Fire Swamp"
	quest.4A16E4A9D510E5A1.title: "The Hydra"
	quest.4A60764377A4A565.quest_desc: [
		"Sleep in a &6Bed&r to set your spawn point and skip the night."
		"Comforts &6Sleeping Bags&r and &6Hammocks&r are for expeditions: a sleeping bag gets you through the night and a hammock through the day, and neither moves your spawn."
	]
	quest.4A60764377A4A565.quest_subtitle: "Set your spawn"
	quest.4A60764377A4A565.title: "Sweet Dreams"
	quest.4B29180AA370C373.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Tournament Stand&r (a barrel, a book and planks) hosts a fishing tournament. Set the length in Minecraft days and the scoring rules, let everyone sign up, then press Start."
		"Scores come from your catches, with multipliers for rarer fish and perfect catches. Press Tab during the tournament to show the scoreboard."
		"Host one for the crew and crown a champion."
	]
	quest.4B29180AA370C373.quest_subtitle: "Fishing for glory"
	quest.4B29180AA370C373.title: "Tournament Day"
	quest.4B34FB8F0F645F42.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Fortress patrols keep the blazes off our walls. Today it's your patrol.\"&r"
		"Kill 20 &bBlazes&r and 15 &bWither Skeletons&r. Both keep spawning inside &bYUNG's Nether fortresses&r."
		"&cWither skeletons inflict Wither;&r a bucket of milk clears it."
		"&eTip:&r keep any &6Wither Skeleton Skulls&r. Three of them summon the Wither."
	]
	quest.4B34FB8F0F645F42.quest_subtitle: "Daily bounty from Bastion Watch"
	quest.4B34FB8F0F645F42.title: "Fortress Sweep"
	quest.4BA5A28E4D19BBD5.quest_desc: [
		"&7Megaproject.&r A market hall for the whole server, next to your town square."
		"Fill it with 16 &6Vendors&r, the player-run shops: shift-click one to set its item, price and mode, and right-click to trade."
		"Two &6Bank Terminals&r let visitors reach their own accounts, or any account they are trusted with."
		"&eTip:&r register the stalls with Create: Marketplace so they show on the market board, and give every team a stall."
	]
	quest.4BA5A28E4D19BBD5.quest_subtitle: "Megaproject: a market for everyone"
	quest.4BA5A28E4D19BBD5.title: "Exchange Hall"
	quest.4BCD6DC4BB6DD6A3.quest_desc: [
		"Scale it up: &6Crafting Co-Processing Units&r let a CPU send out batches faster, &616k Storage Components&r make bigger cells, and a &6Wireless Access Point&r lets wireless terminals reach the network."
		"Your ME network now autocrafts through Create, from Mechanical Crafters to the stock network."
		"&eNext:&r a &6Wireless Crafting Terminal&r. AE2WTLib can merge it with its wireless pattern terminals into one &6Wireless Universal Terminal&r."
		"ExtendedAE and MEGA Cells go further still; the Ascension trophy asks for both."
		"&7This also opens the weekly Processor Order contract.&r"
	]
	quest.4BCD6DC4BB6DD6A3.quest_subtitle: "Every machine, one network"
	quest.4BCD6DC4BB6DD6A3.title: "The Network"
	quest.4BDBAB56E245E196.quest_desc: [
		"&bEMI&r is the recipe viewer. Hover any item and press &bR&r for its recipes or &bU&r for its uses. Its recipe tree plans long crafting chains for you."
		"&7JEI is installed too, but it only runs underneath so every mod's recipes reach EMI.&r"
		"&bEMI Loot&r shows which chests, mobs and blocks drop an item, and &bEMI Ores&r shows the heights where each ore generates."
		"For anything from Create, hold &bW&r over the item to watch its &bPonder&r scene."
	]
	quest.4BDBAB56E245E196.quest_subtitle: "EMI knows every recipe"
	quest.4BDBAB56E245E196.title: "Look It Up"
	quest.4C51B2229BB8AFEC.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Gate Pearl&r opens a &bGateway&r: use it on open ground and waves of monsters pour out. Beat every wave to claim its rewards."
		"Clear the &6Gateway of the Apothic Pinnacle&r. Its pearl is crafted from &6Gem Dust&r, &6Godforged Pearl&r, &6Sigil of Malice&r, &6Warden Tendril&r and &6Infused Dragon's Breath&r; EMI shows the layout."
		"&eTip:&r the Frontier, Ascent and Summit gate pearls are cheaper warm-ups for the same kind of fight."
	]
	quest.4C51B2229BB8AFEC.quest_subtitle: "Gateways to Eternity"
	quest.4C51B2229BB8AFEC.title: "At the Pinnacle"
	quest.4C54932B26046DE9.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The whole colony eats at the festival. Bring everything.\"&r"
		"512 each of &6Cabbage&r, &6Tomatoes&r, &6Onions&r and &6Rice&r."
		"Big farms with &bMechanical Harvesters&r on a contraption, or Create deployers, keep this one easy."
		"&eTip:&r four Task Screens fed by one sorting line fill the order while you're away."
	]
	quest.4C54932B26046DE9.quest_subtitle: "Monthly Grand Contract from Greenhollow Co-op"
	quest.4C54932B26046DE9.title: "Harvest Festival"
	quest.4C8317867AD6AB9D.quest_desc: [
		"&bWhen Dungeons Arise&r sky ships and fortresses, and &bMoog's Soaring Structures&r islands, are rare and far apart. Distant Horizons draws them on the skyline."
		"Fly out and find a &6Heavenly Rider&r."
		"The Explorer's Compass won't find these landmarks, so scan the horizon from the deck."
		"&eTip:&r Icarus wings make boarding and leaving far safer."
	]
	quest.4C8317867AD6AB9D.quest_subtitle: "Fortresses on the skyline"
	quest.4C8317867AD6AB9D.title: "Castles in the Air"
	quest.4CEA6742D62CFAB2.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"There is a desk with your name on it in the Guild Hall.\"&r"
		"Pay &6120 Contract Seals&r to rise to Expert."
		"Opens the &eExpert shelf&r and two Grand Contracts: &bLight Up the Colony&r and &bThe Data Vault&r."
	]
	quest.4CEA6742D62CFAB2.quest_subtitle: "120 Contract Seals"
	quest.4CEA6742D62CFAB2.title: "Rank IV: Expert"
	quest.4D32643C5EB97EE6.quest_desc: [
		"No more culls from here on: Tier IV is &bmajor boss bounties&r, each reset weekly."
		"The &bWither&r and the &bWarden&r from World Tier Summit, plus two Cataclysm bosses whose lairs can call them back: the &bAncient Remnant&r and &bMaledictus&r."
		"&7Tier V opens with Lunar Program.&r"
	]
	quest.4D32643C5EB97EE6.quest_subtitle: "Major boss bounties"
	quest.4D32643C5EB97EE6.title: "Tier IV Bounties"
	quest.4D468B9BCB993205.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Mechanical Belt&r is made from dried kelp. Use it on one shaft, then on another in line with it, to connect them."
		"Belts carry items past your machines: presses, saws and fans all process whatever rides along them."
		"&eTip:&r a funnel puts items onto a belt or pulls them off into a chest."
	]
	quest.4D468B9BCB993205.quest_subtitle: "Belts move everything"
	quest.4D468B9BCB993205.title: "Kelp Drive"
	quest.4D73C39BDB52A930.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mechanical Arm&r is made from &6Brass Casing&r, a &6Precision Mechanism&r, &6Brass Sheets&r and &6Andesite Alloy&r."
		"Before placing it, hold the arm and right-click the blocks it should take from. Click a selected block again to make it a drop-off point. Then place the arm nearby and power it."
		"It works with belts, depots, funnels, basins, Blaze Burners and Mechanical Crafters."
		"&eTip:&r one arm can serve several inputs and outputs, which makes it ideal for loading crafters."
	]
	quest.4D73C39BDB52A930.quest_subtitle: "Pick up here, put down there"
	quest.4D73C39BDB52A930.title: "Busy Hands"
	quest.4DC9E95A37FC226B.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Industrial Turbine&r is a hollow box of &6Turbine Casing&r with a column of &6Turbine Rotors&r and &6Blades&r up the middle."
		"The top rotor carries a &6Rotational Complex&r, ringed by a layer of &6Pressure Dispersers&r. Above them, &6Electromagnetic Coils&r touching the complex make power, and &6Turbine Vents&r let the steam out."
		"Feed steam in through &6Turbine Valves&r. A &6Saturating Condenser&r turns spent steam back into water."
		"&eTip:&r Mekanism: Ponders shows the build step by step."
	]
	quest.4DC9E95A37FC226B.quest_subtitle: "Steam into power"
	quest.4DC9E95A37FC226B.title: "Spin the Turbine"
	quest.4E06356D3DCA8891.quest_desc: [
		"Mine Martian iron ore for &6Raw Martian Iron&r and dig up &6Volcanic Ash&r."
		"Both go into Martian steel, along with titanium from home or the Moon."
		"&eTip:&r Crushing Wheels also turn Martian iron ore into &6Raw Martian Iron&r."
	]
	quest.4E06356D3DCA8891.quest_subtitle: "Martian iron and ash"
	quest.4E06356D3DCA8891.title: "Red Dirt"
	quest.4EC6D83FA4A7A19C.quest_desc: [
		"Combine a &6Book&r and a &6Titanium Ingot&r into a &6Space Atlas&r."
		"Put it in the &bAstronomy Table&r and feed it readings. Enough of them unlock a planet."
		"Later the atlas rides in the &bRocket Station&r, where it chooses the destination from the planets you've unlocked."
	]
	quest.4EC6D83FA4A7A19C.quest_subtitle: "Every destination starts here"
	quest.4EC6D83FA4A7A19C.title: "Space Atlas"
	quest.4F2FA921E6455559.quest_desc: [
		"&6Globe&r, &6Snout&r, &6Flow&r and &6Guster&r patterns for town and airship banners."
		"A pattern sits in the &bLoom&r and is never used up."
	]
	quest.4F2FA921E6455559.quest_subtitle: "8 seals"
	quest.4F2FA921E6455559.title: "Banner Patterns x4"
	quest.4FB0AB6F00BC0ED8.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &6Titanium Ingot&r, &6Raw Martian Iron&r and &6Volcanic Ash&r in a &bBasin&r under a &bMechanical Press&r. Compacting makes &6Martian Steel&r."
		"A Press also flattens the ingots into &6Martian Steel Sheets&r. Suits and machines need both."
		"&eTip:&r automate it. A colony and a starship take a lot of steel."
	]
	quest.4FB0AB6F00BC0ED8.quest_subtitle: "Compacted in a basin"
	quest.4FB0AB6F00BC0ED8.title: "Martian Steel"
	quest.4FE9148CE9EE10B9.quest_desc: [
		"Dig sites also give &6Artifact Shards&r. Craft them into an &6Unidentified Artifact&r."
		"Build an &6Archeology Table&r from a brush, artifact shards and planks, and identify the artifact there."
		"Identified relics include enchanted books with Better Archeology's own enchantments, such as &bTunneling&r and &bPenetrating Strike&r."
	]
	quest.4FE9148CE9EE10B9.quest_subtitle: "Shards, artifacts and the table"
	quest.4FE9148CE9EE10B9.title: "It's All Coming Together"
	quest.5028411460B088F8.quest_desc: [
		"Mine the &6Mysterious Cube&r without Silk Touch and it drops all four &6Inscriber Presses&r: Silicon, Logic, Calculation and Engineering."
		"Bring home &6certus quartz&r, some &6Sky Stone&r and the Flawed, Chipped or Damaged &6Budding Certus&r. Without Silk Touch those drop a tier."
		"&cLeave Flawless Budding Certus where it is:&r it never wears out, but mining it knocks it down a tier, even with Silk Touch."
		"&eTip:&r once you have an Inscriber, a press plus an &6Iron Block&r makes a copy, so one set can equip every friend."
		"Most AE2 items name a guide key in their tooltip. Hold it to read AE2's built-in guide."
	]
	quest.5028411460B088F8.quest_subtitle: "Four presses in one cube"
	quest.5028411460B088F8.title: "Unknown Technology"
	quest.5112975F69D5C01E.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Not our kind of warden. Somebody has to keep the Deep Dark quiet.\"&r"
		"Kill a &bWarden&r. In an &bAncient City&r every shriek from a &bSculk Shrieker&r raises the warning level, and the fourth brings a Warden."
		"The city's shriekers keep working, so you can call one again whenever you're ready."
		"&cIts sonic boom ignores armour and shields.&r Fight as a team and keep your distance."
	]
	quest.5112975F69D5C01E.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.5112975F69D5C01E.title: "Bounty: The Warden"
	quest.519DE109F7A29F9F.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Market day again, and the stalls want fresh vegetables.\"&r"
		"32 &6Tomatoes&r and 32 &6Onions&r from Farmer's Delight."
		"Break &6Tomato Shrubs&r (hot, dry biomes) for tomato seeds, and &6Wild Onions&r for onions you plant as they are."
		"Farm \\& Charm grows its own tomatoes and onions, but this order wants the Farmer's Delight ones. The tooltip names the mod."
		"&eTip:&r later on, an Immersive Engineering &bGarden Cloche&r grows both indoors."
	]
	quest.519DE109F7A29F9F.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Greenhollow Co-op"
	quest.519DE109F7A29F9F.title: "Fresh Produce"
	quest.51B9317F83A6BE34.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrade to a &6Good Telescopic Lens&r: your Normal lens with a diamond, an amethyst block and a spyglass."
		"Better lenses analyse faster."
		"Watch for meteor showers and aurora nights. They reveal objects you can't catch any other time."
		"&eTip:&r the Excellent and Sculk lenses go further still. EMI has their recipes."
	]
	quest.51B9317F83A6BE34.quest_subtitle: "Better glass, rarer objects"
	quest.51B9317F83A6BE34.title: "Clearer Skies"
	quest.51BD29ACAC6D79FD.quest_desc: [
		"Put &6Iron Ingots&r and fuel in the Crude Blast Furnace. Each ingot slowly becomes a &6Steel Ingot&r and leaves &6Slag&r behind."
		"Empty the slag slot, or the furnace stops. The crude furnace can't be automated, so check on it."
		"Almost Unified keeps one steel for every mod. This is the steel Mekanism, airships and everything later will ask for."
		"&eTip:&r a row of furnaces side by side keeps up with demand."
	]
	quest.51BD29ACAC6D79FD.quest_subtitle: "Iron in, steel out"
	quest.51BD29ACAC6D79FD.title: "The Upgrade"
	quest.5208E4A2CDEA8B14.quest_desc: [
		"An Exposure &6Camera&r takes a lever, a button, a glass pane and iron. Sneak and use it to open its attachments and load a roll of &6Black and White Film&r. Color Film costs gold and lapis instead."
		"Raise the camera to look through the viewfinder and take the shot. Scroll to zoom; a lens changes the zoom range, and a flash helps in the dark."
		"Expose one frame of film."
	]
	quest.5208E4A2CDEA8B14.quest_subtitle: "Cameras and film"
	quest.5208E4A2CDEA8B14.title: "Say Cheese"
	quest.522CD5565413BA12.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The packs in the Snowy Forest are getting bold. Hunt them.\"&r"
		"Kill 10 &bWinter Wolves&r and 6 &bYetis&r in the Twilight Forest's &bSnowy Forest&r. The Lich's defeat lifts the frost curse that guards it."
		"Both drop &6Arctic Fur&r, which makes warm Arctic armour."
	]
	quest.522CD5565413BA12.quest_subtitle: "Daily bounty from the Twilight Rangers"
	quest.522CD5565413BA12.title: "Snowbound Patrol"
	quest.525506A113421DB1.quest_desc: [
		"The Airwright stage unlocks the &6Icarus&r wing recipes. &6Feathered Wings&r need feathers and honeycomb; EMI shows the rest."
		"Wings glide and flap. Flapping costs hunger, and heavy armour slows you down."
		"They share the two-slot &bCurios&r back slot with a backpack."
		"Dye them afterwards for a crew livery."
	]
	quest.525506A113421DB1.quest_subtitle: "Glide, flap and land softly"
	quest.525506A113421DB1.title: "Wings of Icarus"
	quest.5296445A84ED74F6.quest_desc: [
		"One random pick: tomatoes, cabbages, onions, rice, red grapes, barley or green tea leaves, or eggs, sugar, honey, cheese or a bucket of milk."
		"&eTip:&r onions and rice plant as they are, and grapes craft into seeds."
	]
	quest.5296445A84ED74F6.quest_subtitle: "5 seals"
	quest.5296445A84ED74F6.title: "Chef's Basket"
	quest.5306AC468F7200A8.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"We're commissioning a new substation. Push power at it and don't let up.\"&r"
		"Deliver 10,000,000 FE. &cOnly a Task Screen accepts energy:&r set one to this order with the &6Task Screen Configurator&r and cable your generators into it."
		"It takes up to 100,000 FE per tick. Turbines, IE generators, Create alternators and charged energy cubes all count."
	]
	quest.5306AC468F7200A8.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Voltaic Grid Authority"
	quest.5306AC468F7200A8.title: "Grid Load Test"
	quest.5308DEE5F8C34901.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Bring back proof of where you've been, and the colony will pay for it.\"&r"
		""
		"The &bFrontier Board&r posts repeatable exploration orders from four clients: the &6Cartographers' Society&r (maps), the &6Lantern Museum&r (relics, fossils and minerals), the &6Field Survey Office&r (specimens) and &6The Gazette&r (photographs)."
		"Most orders send you somewhere first. Step into the biome, structure or dimension the order names, then hand in what you brought home. The goods are used up."
		"Tier I to III orders reset daily. Tier IV and V orders reset weekly and add an &6Explorer's Cache&r. Each tier opens at its gate; open a locked order to see what it waits on."
		"&eTip:&r a &6Nature's Compass&r finds biomes, and an &6Explorer's Compass&r (from the Explorer's Licence) finds most structures."
	]
	quest.5308DEE5F8C34901.quest_subtitle: "Specimens, relics, maps and photos"
	quest.5308DEE5F8C34901.title: "The Frontier Board"
	quest.53218DED68CC37DC.quest_desc: [
		"&7Every station is running and the cellar is stocked. One last challenge.&r"
		""
		"Eat a course of every Farmer's Delight meal: 27 dishes in all, from Mixed Salad and Bone Broth to Squid Ink Pasta and the feast servings."
		"Plan ahead for the tricky ones: ink sacs for the pasta, fish for the stews and the Grilled Salmon, glow berries and a golden carrot for the Gleaming Salad."
		"Every new dish also counts toward your Spice of Life hearts, so this quest pays twice. The &6Food Book&r shows what you've eaten so far."
	]
	quest.53218DED68CC37DC.quest_subtitle: "A course of every meal"
	quest.53218DED68CC37DC.title: "Master Chef"
	quest.5335702BF40E9027.quest_desc: [
		"&7Megaproject.&r Park a ship in &bEarth Orbit&r and make it a station."
		"Reach orbit by rocket (a Rocket Station can set Earth Orbit as its destination), then bring your starship up or assemble a new ship there."
		"Claim it with a &6Contraption Claim Block&r: land claims don't cover ships, and an unclaimed station isn't protected."
		"&eTip:&r pack space suits and spare air for everyone who visits."
	]
	quest.5335702BF40E9027.quest_subtitle: "Megaproject: a home in orbit"
	quest.5335702BF40E9027.title: "Orbital Station"
	quest.53DF8594A1F86694.quest_desc: [
		"&bXaero's Minimap&r and &bWorld Map&r are your maps. Claim chunks right on the World Map (FTB Chunks gives &b500 claims&r per player, and a party adds its members’ allowances together)."
		"Your team and its allies can use the blocks inside your claims; other players can't."
		"Force-loading is one shared budget of about &b25 chunks&r per player, and it only runs while someone on the team has played recently. Power Loader chunk loaders and Ship Control Modules count against it."
		"The world border is invisible under shaders, so watch your coordinates near the edge (the Overworld's is 5,000 blocks from the centre)."
		"&cLand claims don't cover airships.&r A &6Contraption Claim Block&r (Airwrights chapter) protects a ship for your team."
	]
	quest.53DF8594A1F86694.quest_subtitle: "Maps, claims and chunk loading"
	quest.53DF8594A1F86694.title: "Stake Your Claim"
	quest.53F139E16ECF2BDA.quest_desc: [
		"Weekly orders from the far side of the void: chorus, End cities and the dragon skeletons of the Shadowlands, plus the Grand Survey."
		"Each pays &6500 XP&r, &62 cogs&r, &610 Contract Seals&r and an &6Explorer's Cache&r."
		"These orders also wait on &bFree the End&r: the outer islands open with a dragon kill."
	]
	quest.53F139E16ECF2BDA.quest_subtitle: "Opens with Lunar Program"
	quest.53F139E16ECF2BDA.title: "Tier V Orders"
	quest.546472033FBFF92F.quest_desc: [
		"Craft &6Nether Quartz&r with eight &6Redstone&r into &6Rose Quartz&r."
		"Polish it with &6Sand Paper&r (paper and sand): hold the sand paper, put the rose quartz in your off-hand and hold right-click."
		"&eTip:&r later, a &bDeployer&r holding sand paper polishes rose quartz on a belt or depot for you."
	]
	quest.546472033FBFF92F.quest_subtitle: "Quartz, charged and polished"
	quest.546472033FBFF92F.title: "Supercharged"
	quest.5489297940B89403.quest_desc: [
		"&7Roots are down. Time to see what's past the next hill.&r"
		""
		"Structures sit in rings around spawn. Close in: &bCTOV villages&r, &bCreate ruins&r and &bYUNG's&r overhauled dungeons. Mid-range: &bDungeons and Taverns&r and &bMoog's&r sites."
		"The &bWhen Dungeons Arise&r landmarks are rare and far apart. They are best reached by air."
		"&6Traveler's Titles&r names each new biome and dimension on screen as you arrive."
		"Craft a &6Compass&r and an &6Empty Map&r (paper around a compass), then head out."
	]
	quest.5489297940B89403.quest_subtitle: "Structures in rings around spawn"
	quest.5489297940B89403.title: "Trailhead"
	quest.549382FEBEDB10A6.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Copper Backtank&r, place it as a block and give it rotation from a shaft. It fills with air."
		"Wear it with a &6Copper Diving Helmet&r to breathe underwater, and add &6Copper Diving Boots&r to walk the sea floor."
		"A worn backtank also powers the &6Extendo Grip&r instead of wearing it down."
		"&eTip:&r the &6Jetpack&r upgrade needs an Elytra, so it waits in Airwrights."
	]
	quest.549382FEBEDB10A6.quest_subtitle: "Air on your back"
	quest.549382FEBEDB10A6.title: "Pressure to Go"
	quest.552A51C90822B8CA.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Four baskets for the morning market, with one of every loaf.\"&r"
		"4 &6Baskets of Bread&r."
		"Each basket is crafted from a loaf of bread, a &6Baguette&r, a &6Bun&r and &6Braided Bread&r on a &6Tray&r."
		"Bake the loaves in the Farm \\& Charm &bStove&r from &6Dough&r and &6Sweet Dough&r (both stirred in the &bCrafting Bowl&r) plus yeast, sugar, an egg or water, as each recipe asks."
		"&eTip:&r each stove batch gives three to five loaves, so one baking session covers all four baskets."
	]
	quest.552A51C90822B8CA.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Hearthstone Bakery"
	quest.552A51C90822B8CA.title: "Baskets of Bread"
	quest.55ACED1B136DDBDD.quest_desc: [
		"Keep looting until you have opened &625 Lootr containers&r in total."
		"Your copy of each chest is yours alone. Your friends' copies stay full until they open them, so there's no need to race."
		"Barrels, chest minecarts and shulker boxes in structures count too."
	]
	quest.55ACED1B136DDBDD.quest_subtitle: "Twenty-five containers"
	quest.55ACED1B136DDBDD.title: "Close Quarters"
	quest.560B18227152CBA2.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Big, ugly and getting bigger. Bring us one of each.\"&r"
		"Kill a &bMutant Zombie&r and a &bMutant Skeleton&r. Both turn up rarely wherever ordinary zombies and skeletons spawn."
		"Or make your own: brew a &6Thick Potion&r with a mutant trophy (a &6Hulk Hammer&r, &6Creeper Shard&r, &6Endersoul Hand&r or &6Mutant Skeleton Skull&r) into &6Chemical X&r, add gunpowder, and throw it at a plain zombie or skeleton."
		"&cA downed Mutant Zombie gets back up unless you set it on fire.&r"
	]
	quest.560B18227152CBA2.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.560B18227152CBA2.title: "Mutant Menace"
	quest.566F6602B7DBE2B3.quest_desc: [
		"Hatches in about 20 minutes, twice as fast on moss."
		"The &bSniffer&r digs up &6Torchflower Seeds&r and &6Pitcher Pods&r, two rare flowers for your gardens."
	]
	quest.566F6602B7DBE2B3.quest_subtitle: "15 seals"
	quest.566F6602B7DBE2B3.title: "Sniffer Egg"
	quest.56DBBBA399A21A84.quest_desc: [
		"&7Smoking coke ovens, a glowing furnace and an excavator turning on the frontier. The grid is real.&r"
		""
		"Bring a stack of &6Steel Ingots&r, plus &6Steel Mechanical Components&r and &6Heavy Engineering Blocks&r."
		"&eNext:&r Electro-Chemistry brings Mekanism, and Airwrights opens airship building. Both stand on IE steel."
		"&7This also opens the Tier III orders on the Guild’s contract boards.&r"
	]
	quest.56DBBBA399A21A84.quest_subtitle: "The rung everything stands on"
	quest.56DBBBA399A21A84.title: "Steel Backbone"
	quest.5721DCBFFA4087DD.quest_desc: [
		"&7The whole base holds its breath as the control rods rise.&r"
		""
		"Build a &6Fission Reactor&r: a casing box with columns of &6Fission Fuel Assemblies&r capped by &6Control Rod Assemblies&r, plus &6Fission Reactor Ports&r for fuel, coolant, steam and waste."
		"A &6Logic Adapter&r lets redstone watch it. Cool it with water or sodium and send the steam to your turbine."
		"Spin its &6Nuclear Waste&r into &6Plutonium&r in the Isotopic Centrifuge."
		"&cStart slow:&r keep coolant flowing and the burn rate low. A reactor that overheats takes damage and can melt down. The Automation chapter has a SCRAM script."
		"&eNext:&r The Network. This also opens the weekly Circuit Order contract."
	]
	quest.5721DCBFFA4087DD.quest_subtitle: "Fission, steam and plutonium"
	quest.5721DCBFFA4087DD.title: "Reactor Online"
	quest.578B54D68940504E.quest_desc: [
		"&bCatacombs&r are old depthrock-brick tombs buried in the Undergarden, and the Forgotten still walk their halls."
		"Their chests can hold &6Forgotten Nuggets&r, &6Regalium&r, froststeel and a &6Forgotten Upgrade&r smithing template. Lootr gives each player their own."
		"Find a catacomb and step inside."
	]
	quest.578B54D68940504E.quest_subtitle: "Enter the catacombs"
	quest.578B54D68940504E.title: "Forgotten Halls"
	quest.57CA3897619A2A54.quest_desc: [
		"&6Train Track&r only comes from &bsequenced assembly&r in this pack: send stone, smooth stone or andesite slabs down a belt past two &bDeployers&r holding iron or zinc nuggets, then under a &bMechanical Press&r. Each slab becomes one track."
		""
		"To lay a line, hold track, right-click an existing track, then right-click where the line should end. You get straights, turns and slopes paid for from your inventory, and blocks in your offhand are paved underneath."
		"&eTip:&r Steam 'n' Rails makes wooden, narrow, wide and monorail track the same way. EMI shows every recipe."
	]
	quest.57CA3897619A2A54.quest_subtitle: "Every railway starts on an assembly line"
	quest.57CA3897619A2A54.title: "A New Gauge"
	quest.57EAB4E5AF2E4761.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Saddle&r, which nothing can craft, plus a &6Name Tag&r and two &6Leads&r."
		"Everything you need to ride, name and lead home your first horse."
	]
	quest.57EAB4E5AF2E4761.quest_subtitle: "4 seals"
	quest.57EAB4E5AF2E4761.title: "Stable Kit"
	quest.57FC9D6C6B05586A.quest_desc: [
		"Select a track, place a &6Train Station&r beside it and switch the station to &bAssembly Mode&r."
		"Use &6Train Casing&r on the track to set down bogeys. Click again to cycle designs, or press &bAlt&r for the Steam 'n' Rails bogey menu. Build the carriage on top, mark it with &6Super Glue&r, add &6Train Controls&r and confirm assembly at the station."
		""
		"Then program a &6Train Schedule&r (sturdy sheet and paper) and hand it to any mob or blaze burner sitting in front of the controls by right-clicking them with it."
		"&eTip:&r chests or barrels of fuel on board make a train faster. Fuel stored in vaults is never burned."
	]
	quest.57FC9D6C6B05586A.quest_subtitle: "Bogeys, glue, controls and a driver"
	quest.57FC9D6C6B05586A.title: "All Aboard!"
	quest.589E3C6CB6217301.quest_desc: [
		"Gadgets \\& Gizmos lets airships carry cargo between colonies on their own."
		"&6Ship Docks&r (andesite alloy, a bell, a compass and smooth stone) mark the stops. A &6Shipping Schedule&r (a Create schedule and a compass) tells a ship where to go."
		"&cExperimental:&r test a short route near home before trusting it with real cargo."
		"&eTeam note:&r Ship Control Modules count against your team's chunk-loading budget."
	]
	quest.589E3C6CB6217301.quest_subtitle: "Ships that fly their own routes"
	quest.589E3C6CB6217301.title: "Freight by Air"
	quest.59171316E17FEA29.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Oxygen Tank Unit&r is built around a &6Netherite Backtank&r, with insulation, iron sheets and a Module Base."
		"It gives the MekaSuit air for long walks."
		"&eTip:&r one more sequenced assembly turns it into an &6Oxygen Tank Expansion Unit&r. Check EMI."
		"&7Its in-game name may show as a raw item key.&r"
	]
	quest.59171316E17FEA29.quest_subtitle: "Air for long walks"
	quest.59171316E17FEA29.title: "Oxygen Tank Unit"
	quest.5920289143059BD1.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The motor pool runs dry by Friday. Eight buckets' worth, please.\"&r"
		"8,000 mB of &6Diesel&r. Pump &6Crude Oil&r with a &bPumpjack&r over an oil chunk, then heat it in a distillation tower built on a &6Distillation Controller&r. Each batch splits into equal parts diesel and gasoline."
		"&eTip:&r hand it in from buckets or tanks in the quest screen, or pipe it straight into a &6Task Screen&r."
	]
	quest.5920289143059BD1.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Bluewater Refinery"
	quest.5920289143059BD1.title: "Fuel Delivery"
	quest.596EAC095F4EF676.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pigstep&r, &6Otherside&r, &6Relic&r, &6Precipice&r and &6Creator&r: five of the rarest records."
		"Play them in a jukebox, or anywhere with a backpack &6Jukebox Upgrade&r."
	]
	quest.596EAC095F4EF676.quest_subtitle: "20 seals"
	quest.596EAC095F4EF676.title: "Rare Music Discs x5"
	quest.59C9F3434E96F15B.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The desert tomb is rumbling again.\"&r"
		"Kill the &bAncient Remnant&r in a &bCursed Pyramid&r in the desert. An &6Eye of Desert&r leads to one."
		"The first time, wake it with the &6Necklace of the Desert&r, brushed from suspicious sand inside the pyramid."
		"After each defeat it leaves a &bBoss Respawner&r; use another Eye of Desert on it to fight again."
	]
	quest.59C9F3434E96F15B.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.59C9F3434E96F15B.title: "Bounty: Ancient Remnant"
	quest.5A54B33C9241EA5D.quest_desc: [
		"Infuse a &6Copper Ingot&r with redstone to make &6Infused Alloy&r, the first of Mekanism's machine alloys."
		"It goes into Advanced Control Circuits, the Electrolytic Separator, the Purification Chamber and more."
		"&eLater:&r &6Reinforced Alloy&r (Infused Alloy plus diamond) and &6Atomic Alloy&r (Reinforced Alloy plus refined obsidian) are made the same way."
	]
	quest.5A54B33C9241EA5D.quest_subtitle: "Copper meets redstone"
	quest.5A54B33C9241EA5D.title: "The Alloy That Started It All"
	quest.5AAF6A676CE94794.quest_desc: [
		"At the centre of every Ancient City stands a huge frame of &breinforced deepslate&r. Use the &6Heart of the Deep&r on it to open a portal to the &bOtherside&r."
		"The Otherside is a sculk-choked world below the bedrock, with echoing forests, blooming caverns, Ancient Temples and new sculk monsters."
		"&eSummit:&r the Otherside and the Wither together unlock World Tier Summit in Bosses \\& Tiers, and Summit opens the End."
	]
	quest.5AAF6A676CE94794.quest_subtitle: "Open the Otherside"
	quest.5AAF6A676CE94794.title: "Below the Bedrock"
	quest.5ACC483F4135F2C4.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Engineer's Workbench&r crafts from &6Engineer's Blueprints&r: put a blueprint in, add the materials and pick the part."
		"The &6Components&r blueprint (paper, blue dye, copper, lead and iron) makes Mechanical and Electronic Components and Vacuum Tubes. The &6Molds&r blueprint makes press molds for plates, rods, gears and wire."
		"&eTip:&r IE's own lead ore is turned off in Starwright. Mine Mekanism's lead ore instead."
	]
	quest.5ACC483F4135F2C4.quest_subtitle: "Blueprints and molds"
	quest.5ACC483F4135F2C4.title: "Time to Tinker"
	quest.5AE294653975C39E.quest_desc: [
		"Rice grows in &bshallow water&r: plant it in a puddle one block deep over dirt and it climbs out into tall &6Rice Panicles&r."
		"Your first grains come from &6Wild Rice&r in wet biomes such as swamps. Breaking it drops rice; shears keep the whole plant."
		"A panicle crafts into Rice. On a cutting board or through a Create &bMillstone&r it gives &6Straw&r as well."
		"Rice turns up in a dozen meals, from Cooked Rice to the rolls of the Rice Roll Medley."
		"Plant one rice."
	]
	quest.5AE294653975C39E.quest_subtitle: "Rice likes wet feet"
	quest.5AE294653975C39E.title: "Dipping Your Roots"
	quest.5AE4C90FB74FD9B1.quest_desc: [
		"FTB Chunks claims protect land, not ships. A &6Contraption Claim Block&r protects a ship for your FTB team."
		"Build it on a &bMechanical Crafter&r grid from a &6Sturdy Sheet&r, &6Brass Ingots&r, a &6Precision Mechanism&r and an &6Ender Pearl&r."
		"Put one aboard every ship you'd hate to lose."
	]
	quest.5AE4C90FB74FD9B1.quest_subtitle: "Land claims don't fly"
	quest.5AE4C90FB74FD9B1.title: "Claim Your Ship"
	quest.5B0FD64C71D68DEB.quest_desc: [
		"A computer beside a Create &6Train Station&r can rename it, assemble or disassemble the train, check isTrainPresent() and give the waiting train a new timetable with &bsetSchedule()&r."
		""
		"Give each station a computer with a &6Wireless Modem&r and let one dispatcher send orders over &brednet&r. Wireless modems reach 64 blocks, further at high altitude."
		"Create: Additional Logistics adds a &6Train Network Monitor&r peripheral (Train Casing, a Transmitter and an Ender Modem) that lists every train and station."
		"&7Hint: read a working timetable with getSchedule() and copy its table layout."
	]
	quest.5B0FD64C71D68DEB.quest_subtitle: "Timetables written in Lua"
	quest.5B0FD64C71D68DEB.title: "Train Dispatcher"
	quest.5B2F4D999AF63CC5.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Temperature Regulator&r keeps a configurable area of your base at a livable temperature."
		"Mechanical-craft it from a &6Blaze Rod&r, an &6Advanced Circuit&r, &6Blue Ice&r, a shaft and titanium."
		"&6Advanced Circuits&r are Circuits sent through one more sequenced assembly."
	]
	quest.5B2F4D999AF63CC5.quest_subtitle: "A livable base anywhere"
	quest.5B2F4D999AF63CC5.title: "Climate Control"
	quest.5B50A7915973A8C9.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Water Wheel&r (a shaft and planks) in moving water turns, and &6Shafts&r and &6Cogwheels&r carry that rotation to your machines."
		"A large cogwheel meshed with a small one changes speed: big driving small doubles it, small driving big halves it."
		"&eTip:&r Create: Connected adds the &6Parallel Gearbox&r and &66-way Gearbox&r for tidier shaft lines."
	]
	quest.5B50A7915973A8C9.quest_subtitle: "Your first rotation"
	quest.5B50A7915973A8C9.title: "Harnessed Hydraulics"
	quest.5BCCCE572C3DAA4C.quest_desc: [
		"Chart &bVenus&r in your atlas, bring the Navigator and land."
		"Acid rain and brutal heat: wear the MekaSuit with its Space Suit, Oxygen Tank, Insulation and Heat-Resistive units installed."
		"&eTip:&r a Temperature Regulator makes a Venus outpost bearable."
	]
	quest.5BCCCE572C3DAA4C.quest_subtitle: "Land on Venus"
	quest.5BCCCE572C3DAA4C.title: "Morning Star"
	quest.5BD624F6413EE9F3.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Precision Mechanism&r is built in steps. Run a &6Golden Sheet&r along a belt under three &bDeployers&r holding a &6Cogwheel&r, a &6Large Cogwheel&r and an &6Iron Nugget&r, in that order."
		"The part goes round &bfive times&r. Send unfinished parts back to the first deployer. Most finish as mechanisms, but some come out as scrap."
		"A &bMechanical Press&r turns gold ingots into golden sheets."
		"&eUnlocks:&r train controls, the Numismatics &6Bank Terminal&r and the Airwrights biplane."
	]
	quest.5BD624F6413EE9F3.quest_subtitle: "Your first sequenced assembly"
	quest.5BD624F6413EE9F3.title: "Complex Curiosities"
	quest.5BF3ED60DF1D75C7.quest_desc: [
		"Craft &6Martian Steel&r armor from ingots, then upgrade it with &6Martian Steel Sheets&r the same way as the iron suit: &6Tinted Glass&r for the helmet, a &6Copper Backtank&r and &6Durable Fabric&r for the chestplate."
		"The Martian steel suit is tougher than the iron one."
		"&eTip:&r make the leggings and boots too. A full suit is the safe way to walk Mars."
	]
	quest.5BF3ED60DF1D75C7.quest_subtitle: "Tougher than iron"
	quest.5BF3ED60DF1D75C7.title: "Martian Space Suit"
	quest.5C0439ED63F90BC6.quest_desc: [
		"One random pick: Northstar ice cream, beef stew, golden carrots, cooked salmon, glowstone torches, an oxygen tank or a Mekanism canteen."
		"Opens once your team completes the &6Lunar Program&r."
	]
	quest.5C0439ED63F90BC6.quest_subtitle: "6 seals"
	quest.5C0439ED63F90BC6.title: "Space Rations"
	quest.5C2ADBD2496759D2.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every windmill on the ridge needs gearing before it can feed the grid.\"&r"
		"64 &6Cogwheels&r, 32 &6Large Cogwheels&r and 128 &6Shafts&r. Two alloy craft into eight shafts, or a &bMechanical Saw&r cuts one alloy into six. A shaft and a plank make a cogwheel; a shaft and two planks make a large one."
		"&eTip:&r once you have &bDeployers&r, one holding planks fits cogwheels onto shafts riding a belt."
	]
	quest.5C2ADBD2496759D2.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Voltaic Grid Authority"
	quest.5C2ADBD2496759D2.title: "Gearing for the Wind Farm"
	quest.5C6FB5BC9874ABF6.quest_desc: [
		"&bApotheosis World Tiers&r set how dangerous your world is: Haven, Frontier, Ascent, Summit and Pinnacle. Each step makes mobs stronger and loot better, with rarer affixes and finer gems."
		"From Frontier on, &cApothic Invaders&r start to appear."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r each tier opens through this chapter. Everyone on the team claims the reward for themselves, then picks the tier in the World Tier screen (&bCtrl + T&r)."
		"Each tier asks for a set of boss kills. The &bWorld Tier&r screen (key in Controls) compares the tiers, and &bBoss Checklist&r (its key, or the pause menu button) lists every boss with its drops and how to find it."
		"Tick the box to begin."
	]
	quest.5C6FB5BC9874ABF6.quest_subtitle: "The boss ladder starts here"
	quest.5C6FB5BC9874ABF6.title: "World Tier: Haven"
	quest.5CBD66B0579BCBA0.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Something keeps climbing out of that portal. Go down and see.\"&r"
		"Kill 16 &bShattered&r and 6 &bSculk Centipedes&r in the &bOtherside&r."
		"Shattered prowl the &bEchoing Forest&r and the &bDeeplands&r; the centipedes live only in the Deeplands."
		"Shattered drop &6Sculk Bones&r."
	]
	quest.5CBD66B0579BCBA0.quest_subtitle: "Daily bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.5CBD66B0579BCBA0.title: "Echoes Below"
	quest.5CD116CBD9AEFE98.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The Union's fitters go through brass plate like paper.\"&r"
		"48 &6Brass Sheets&r. Mix &6Copper&r and &6Zinc Ingots&r in a &bBasin&r on a fuelled &bBlaze Burner&r under a &bMechanical Mixer&r; each pair makes two brass ingots. A &bMechanical Press&r flattens them into sheets."
		"&eTip:&r keep the burner fed. Without heat the mix never starts."
	]
	quest.5CD116CBD9AEFE98.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Brassworks Union"
	quest.5CD116CBD9AEFE98.title: "Sheet Brass"
	quest.5CD73D9234274484.quest_desc: [
		"Rechiseled's &6Chisel&r (iron and a stick) turns blocks into hundreds of decorative variants, many with connected textures. Use it to open its screen, drop blocks in and pick a look."
		"Rechiseled: Create's &bMechanical Chisel&r (a chisel on andesite casing) does the same on rotation for big builds."
		"The Universal Sawmill's &6Saw&r is a stonecutter for wood: logs and planks become stairs, slabs, fences, doors and more, for every wood in the pack."
		"Every Compat gives modded woods their own Macaw's and Handcrafted pieces. Supplementaries, Another Furniture, Macaw's and Create Deco fill in the rest of the street."
	]
	quest.5CD73D9234274484.quest_subtitle: "Hundreds of new looks"
	quest.5CD73D9234274484.title: "Chisel \\& Saw"
	quest.5CEE47354759D054.quest_desc: [
		"Slot it into a &6Sophisticated Backpack&r and it feeds you from the food inside whenever you get hungry."
		"&7One less thing to watch on a long dig.&r"
	]
	quest.5CEE47354759D054.quest_subtitle: "8 seals"
	quest.5CEE47354759D054.title: "Feeding Upgrade"
	quest.5D6062385FD595FF.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every workshop in the colony is hiring. Bring us what your machines make.\"&r"
		""
		"Eight clients post here: Andesite Mill \\& Co., the Brassworks Union, Ironvale Foundry, Northline Railways, the Voltaic Grid Authority, Meridian Chemworks, Lattice Data Exchange and Bluewater Refinery."
		"Tier I to III orders reset &bdaily&r. Tier IV and V orders, and every bulk order, reset &bweekly&r. Each tier opens with a tech milestone, and a few orders also wait on Brass, Rails \\& Parcels or The Network."
		"&eTip:&r fluid, energy and bulk orders are sized for a &6Task Screen&r. Energy can only go in through one."
	]
	quest.5D6062385FD595FF.quest_subtitle: "Parts, materials, fuel and power"
	quest.5D6062385FD595FF.title: "The Industry Board"
	quest.5D83C9D86361E4AB.quest_desc: [
		"&7From a water wheel to the inner planets. One last delivery to prove it.&r"
		""
		"Bring together the best of every world: four &6Antimatter Pellets&r from your SPS, 16 &6Polished Lunar Sapphire&r from the Moon, four blocks each of &6Martian Steel&r and Mercury &6Tungsten&r, a &616M MEGA Storage Component&r and an ExtendedAE &6ME Extended Pattern Provider&r."
		"This quest only checks your inventory, so nothing is used up."
		"&eTip:&r pellets come out of a &bChemical Crystallizer&r fed with antimatter."
		"&7Thank you for flying Starwright. The world is yours.&r"
	]
	quest.5D83C9D86361E4AB.quest_subtitle: "The trophy of the whole program"
	quest.5D83C9D86361E4AB.title: "Ascension"
	quest.5E1A6011386794EE.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Electrolysis Machine&r splits water into hydrogen and oxygen: rocket fuel and air from one tank."
		"Mechanical-craft it from an &6Amethyst Crystal&r (Polished Amethyst, an iron ingot and redstone), a Circuit, Martian steel, a Fluid Tank, a Fluid Pipe and a shaft."
		"&eTip:&r sandpaper turns an amethyst shard into Polished Amethyst."
	]
	quest.5E1A6011386794EE.quest_subtitle: "Fuel and oxygen from one tank"
	quest.5E1A6011386794EE.title: "Water to Air"
	quest.5E1FC22746B0C030.quest_desc: [
		"Link two friends' bases: a &6Train Station&r at each end, signals on any shared track and a schedule that shuttles between them."
		"Trains keep running through unloaded chunks and still stop at stations and red signals, so the line works while nobody is near."
		"A &6Postbox&r beside a station loads outgoing packages onto trains that stop there and unloads the ones addressed to it."
		"Fares are optional: a Numismatics &6Depositor&r takes coins and sends a redstone pulse, ready for a ticket gate. Bank accounts are on Main Street."
		""
		"Tick the box once your line runs both ways."
	]
	quest.5E1FC22746B0C030.quest_subtitle: "A railway from your door to theirs"
	quest.5E1FC22746B0C030.title: "Line Between Friends"
	quest.5EB5F6512B1BAFA0.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our freighters fly steadier when the props level themselves. Sixteen, please.\"&r"
		"A &6Smart Propeller&r is a Create Propeller over a &6Gyroscopic Mechanism&r over Brass Casing. Each craft makes two."
		"The mechanism is a &bsequenced assembly&r on an Iron Sheet: Deployers add a cogwheel, a shaft and a brass nugget, five loops in all."
		"&eTip:&r a looped belt makes the mechanisms unattended. Filter out the odd scrap piece."
	]
	quest.5EB5F6512B1BAFA0.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Skyward Freight"
	quest.5EB5F6512B1BAFA0.title: "Props That Level Themselves"
	quest.5ED4DC162002DB92.quest_desc: [
		"Three &bweekly&r orders: a cake order, a trophy fishing trip and a bulk order sized for a Create food line feeding a &6Task Screen&r."
		"Each also rolls a basket of goods: a Chef's Basket, or an Angler's Tackle Box for the fishing trip."
		"&eTip:&r the &6Founders' Feast&r opens here too, once your team has finished &6Master Chef&r."
	]
	quest.5ED4DC162002DB92.quest_subtitle: "Opens with Reactor Online"
	quest.5ED4DC162002DB92.title: "Tier IV Orders"
	quest.5EFC4314608477A0.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Inscriber&r stamps materials into circuits. The press goes in the top slot and the material in the middle; presses are never used up."
		"&cStarwright rule:&r its recipe is changed to need Create &6Precision Mechanisms&r and &6Steel&r. Check EMI for the exact layout."
		"It runs on FE or AE, like the Charger. With no press, it grinds &6Certus Quartz&r into dust (a Create &bMillstone&r can do that too)."
	]
	quest.5EFC4314608477A0.quest_subtitle: "Presses meet power"
	quest.5EFC4314608477A0.title: "The Inscriber"
	quest.5F296DAE79D754C2.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Millstone&r (a cogwheel, stone and andesite casing) grinds what you feed it: wheat into flour, cobblestone into gravel, gravel into flint, bones into bone meal and flowers into dye."
		"Right-click it to put items in or take the results out; funnels and chutes can do both for you."
		"&7Raw ores need Crushing Wheels instead, which arrive with the Brass Age.&r"
	]
	quest.5F296DAE79D754C2.quest_subtitle: "The Millstone"
	quest.5F296DAE79D754C2.title: "Embrace the Grind"
	quest.5FFDA1E8C4BB5E61.quest_desc: [
		"&7Tombs emptied, vaults cracked, relics identified. The rings around spawn feel like home now.&r"
		""
		"Open &6100 Lootr containers&r."
		"The landmarks on the skyline are next. The &bAirwrights&r chapter builds the ships that reach them."
		"&7Keep a compass handy: the world border grows every season.&r"
	]
	quest.5FFDA1E8C4BB5E61.quest_subtitle: "A hundred chests later"
	quest.5FFDA1E8C4BB5E61.title: "Seasoned Trailblazer"
	quest.606D5E76465F3975.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our route ships fly themselves now, and every controller needs a brain.\"&r"
		"Sixteen Gadgets \\& Gizmos &6Computation Mechanisms&r, the heart of its contraption controllers and data links."
		"Each is a &bsequenced assembly&r on a Blackstone Sheet: Deployers add two cogwheels, a copper nugget and an Electron Tube, five loops in all."
		"Blackstone Sheets are pressed &6Blackstone Alloy&r: blackstone, a copper nugget and lava in a Mixer over a &bsuperheated&r Blaze Burner."
		"&eTip:&r Blaze Cakes keep the burner superheated."
	]
	quest.606D5E76465F3975.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Skyward Freight"
	quest.606D5E76465F3975.title: "Autopilot Cores"
	quest.607AA86257F73399.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The forge-beast is awake again. Put it back to sleep.\"&r"
		"Kill the &bNetherite Monstrosity&r. When it falls it leaves a &bBoss Respawner&r in its Soul Forge lair."
		"Use an &6Eye of Monstrous&r (an eye of ender, netherite scrap, blackstone and a lava bucket) on the respawner to call it back."
		"&eTip:&r every kill drops its &6Infernal Forge&r, a &6Monstrous Horn&r and 16 to 24 &6Lava Power Cells&r."
	]
	quest.607AA86257F73399.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from Bastion Watch"
	quest.607AA86257F73399.title: "Bounty: Netherite Monstrosity"
	quest.61005E823624ED67.quest_desc: [
		"The heart of a &6Beacon&r for the town square, or for any late recipe that calls for one."
		"Opens at World Tier &bSummit&r, once the Wither has fallen. Restocks weekly."
	]
	quest.61005E823624ED67.quest_subtitle: "100 seals"
	quest.61005E823624ED67.title: "Nether Star"
	quest.61E6C44B41B5B9E1.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Nature's Compass&r is a compass ringed with saplings and logs. It points the way to any biome you choose."
		"Use it to open its biome list, pick one, and follow the needle."
		"Its search radius is capped. If a biome isn't found, travel a while and search again."
		"&eTip:&r Tectonic, Terralith and Regions Unexplored add plenty of new biomes, and the compass lists them all."
	]
	quest.61E6C44B41B5B9E1.quest_subtitle: "Nature's Compass finds biomes"
	quest.61E6C44B41B5B9E1.title: "Which Way to the Jungle?"
	quest.628142CEA5FCBDCE.quest_desc: [
		"Choose one: 64 bricks, stone bricks, glass, polished andesite, smooth stone, terracotta, white concrete or oak planks, or 16 lanterns, copycat blocks or iron catwalks."
		"&7For the build that is always one stack short.&r"
	]
	quest.628142CEA5FCBDCE.quest_subtitle: "5 seals"
	quest.628142CEA5FCBDCE.title: "Builder's Bundle"
	quest.62A61DE9F4750EBF.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The starlit land is beautiful. What lives in it is not.\"&r"
		"Kill 16 &bNightfall Spiders&r and 12 &bLonestar Skeletons&r in &bEternal Starlight&r. Both spawn across nearly every biome there."
		"Lonestar Skeletons drop &6Deepsilver Nuggets&r, and Nightfall Spiders their eyes."
		"&7The way in is the Gatekeeper's Orb of Prophecy, from Below and Beyond.&r"
	]
	quest.62A61DE9F4750EBF.quest_subtitle: "Daily bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.62A61DE9F4750EBF.title: "Starlit Hunt"
	quest.62B4DE545E4CC805.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our herbarium is short on mountain flowers. Press us a fresh set.\"&r"
		"Visit a &bMeadow&r, the flowery grassland on mountain slopes, and bring 16 each of &6Allium&r, &6Azure Bluet&r and &6Cornflower&r."
		"&6Bone Meal&r on meadow grass sprouts more of the local flowers."
		"&eTip:&r a &6Nature's Compass&r points the way to any biome."
	]
	quest.62B4DE545E4CC805.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Field Survey Office"
	quest.62B4DE545E4CC805.title: "Pressed Flowers"
	quest.62BD6E67CE4A7286.quest_desc: [
		"Among the best saturation of any food, so sixteen last a long trip."
		"They also breed horses and donkeys."
	]
	quest.62BD6E67CE4A7286.quest_subtitle: "2 seals"
	quest.62BD6E67CE4A7286.title: "Golden Carrots x16"
	quest.6312E631463F5813.quest_desc: [
		"Farm \\& Charm is the base of every Let's Do mod. Its &bCooking Pot&r and &bRoaster&r cook when set on heat: its own &bStove&r (bricks, a campfire and iron), a campfire, a magma block or a Farmer's Delight Stove."
		"The Stove also bakes breads and pies. The &bCrafting Bowl&r mixes doughs and butter, and the &bMincer&r grinds wheat into flour and meat into minced beef, bacon, lamb ham or chicken parts."
		"Around the farm: &bChicken Coops&r, &bFeeding Troughs&r and horse-drawn carts, the &6Plow&r, &6Seeder&r and &6Supply Cart&r."
		"&eTip:&r Farm \\& Charm and Farmer's Delight each have a Cooking Pot and a Stove, with separate recipes. EMI shows which one a dish needs."
		"Place a Farm \\& Charm Cooking Pot and a Roaster."
	]
	quest.6312E631463F5813.quest_subtitle: "The Let's Do kitchen"
	quest.6312E631463F5813.title: "Farm \\& Charm"
	quest.6313D66B9B4D1771.quest_desc: [
		"Armor works the same way: &6Plates&r for a helmet, chestplate, leggings or boots, plus an optional &6Lining&r."
		"Materials trade off protection, durability and traits, so try a few combinations."
		"Silent Gear items keep their data, so Apotheosis affixes still work on them."
		"&7Spot a white piece or \"unknown material\"? Tell the admins.&r"
		"Make any piece of Silent Gear armor."
	]
	quest.6313D66B9B4D1771.quest_subtitle: "Plates, linings and traits"
	quest.6313D66B9B4D1771.title: "Better Armor"
	quest.633753D4809D2C61.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"New berths need new couplings. Sixteen connectors for the docks.\"&r"
		"&6Docking Connectors&r are built on &bMechanical Crafters&r from iron sheets, chutes, pistons, brass sheets, brass casing and an Electron Tube. Each craft makes two."
		"They lock together in pairs to make a rigid connection, and extended connectors try to line up with each other."
		"&eTip:&r funnels can feed every crafter in the grid, so the line runs unattended."
	]
	quest.633753D4809D2C61.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from Skyward Freight"
	quest.633753D4809D2C61.title: "Docking Hardware"
	quest.635E63E9B6A3CCDE.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Chemical Dissolution Chamber&r dissolves ore in &6Sulfuric Acid&r into slurry, a &6Chemical Washer&r cleans it with water, and a &6Chemical Crystallizer&r grows five &6Crystals&r per ore."
		"Inject the crystals into shards and follow the chain back down to ingots."
		"Sulfuric acid takes a few steps: oxidize sulfur into sulfur dioxide, add oxygen for sulfur trioxide, then add water vapour. EMI shows each machine."
		"&eTip:&r all three machines need &6Ultimate Control Circuits&r and &6Refined Obsidian&r."
	]
	quest.635E63E9B6A3CCDE.quest_subtitle: "Five ingots per ore"
	quest.635E63E9B6A3CCDE.title: "Most Bang for Your Buck"
	quest.636C980435E2309B.quest_desc: [
		"&7Heated mixers, glowing tubes, crafters and arms. The workshop has grown up.&r"
		""
		"Stock the parts every brass build eats: &6Precision Mechanisms&r, &6Electron Tubes&r and &6Brass Casing&r."
		"&eNext:&r Steel \\& Sparks, where your Mechanical Crafters build the Crafts \\& Additions &6Alternator&r for Starwright's first FE. Below and Beyond opens too."
		"&7Next: Steel \\& Sparks, where the Guild’s Tier III orders open.&r"
	]
	quest.636C980435E2309B.quest_subtitle: "A workshop that builds itself"
	quest.636C980435E2309B.title: "Brass Works"
	quest.63A206447F968E11.quest_desc: [
		"Craft 27 &6Coke Bricks&r (clay, sandstone and bricks), stack them in a 3x3x3 cube and hit the centre of one side with the hammer to form a &bCoke Oven&r."
		"It slowly bakes up to 16 coal at a time into &6Coal Coke&r, plus &6Creosote Oil&r. It won't push the creosote out, so fill buckets in its GUI or pump it."
		"Creosote on planks makes &6Treated Wood&r, IE's basic building material. A Create &bSpout&r can treat planks too."
		"&eTip:&r build two or three ovens. Coking is slow."
	]
	quest.63A206447F968E11.quest_subtitle: "Coke, creosote and treated wood"
	quest.63A206447F968E11.title: "Concentrated Carbon"
	quest.63D24BB8455E407D.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Every village goes in the Society's atlas, and every atlas needs fresh sheets.\"&r"
		"Step inside any village (CTOV villages count) and bring 4 &6Filled Maps&r."
		"An &6Empty Map&r is a compass ringed with paper. Hold it and use it to draw the land around you."
		"&eTip:&r a &bCartography Table&r zooms a map out with more paper, so one sheet covers more ground."
	]
	quest.63D24BB8455E407D.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Cartographers' Society"
	quest.63D24BB8455E407D.title: "Village Census"
	quest.64468A0EB307CE27.quest_desc: [
		"Keep shooting the night sky with a &6Telescopic Lens&r and a &6Space Filter&r on your Exposure camera, and study each new object in the &bPhoto Analyzer&r."
		"Study half of all the cosmic objects Exposure: Space knows about."
		"&eTip:&r meteor showers and aurora nights reveal objects you can't see otherwise, and better lenses analyse faster."
	]
	quest.64468A0EB307CE27.quest_subtitle: "Half the sky catalogued"
	quest.64468A0EB307CE27.title: "Halfway to the Stars"
	quest.64A1D729B5DB5F26.quest_desc: [
		"&7Wheels turning, belts rolling, presses thumping.&r"
		""
		"Prove the workshop runs: casings, sheets and zinc in quantity. Smelt raw zinc in a furnace; crushing it for extra yield comes with the Brass Age."
		"This opens the &6Brass Age&r and the &bTwilight Forest&r. The Brass Age starts with a short Nether trip to catch a blaze, so pack for it."
		"&7Crushing Wheels, Deployers and Mechanical Crafters need brass or electron tubes, so they wait for the Brass Age.&r"
	]
	quest.64A1D729B5DB5F26.quest_subtitle: "A working andesite workshop"
	quest.64A1D729B5DB5F26.title: "Andesite Works"
	quest.655FBF8021E4963A.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The survey's done. Now we need rails under it.\"&r"
		"64 &6Train Track&r. Run stone, smooth stone or andesite slabs past two &bDeployers&r adding iron or zinc nuggets, then under a &bMechanical Press&r. Each slab becomes one track."
		"&eTip:&r the same line stocks your own railway."
	]
	quest.655FBF8021E4963A.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Northline Railways"
	quest.655FBF8021E4963A.title: "Track Crew"
	quest.6573EE324D51E048.quest_desc: [
		"The &6ME Controller&r (Sky Stone Blocks, Fluix Crystals and an Engineering Processor) gives each face &b32 channels&r. Without one, a network runs at most 8 devices."
		"Feed FE into an &6Energy Acceptor&r (2 FE make 1 AE) and add an &6Energy Cell&r as a buffer, so dumping a full inventory in can't make the network reboot."
		"Normal cables carry 8 channels and dense cables 32. A network can have only one controller, though it can be a multiblock."
		"&eTip:&r Applied Create's &6Kinetic Energy Acceptor&r runs ME on Create rotation, and Applied Flux stores FE in ME cells."
	]
	quest.6573EE324D51E048.quest_subtitle: "The heart of the network"
	quest.6573EE324D51E048.title: "Networking Switchboard"
	quest.6575B36D502BB123.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Some places are too big for a village map. Chart the landmarks.\"&r"
		"Survey a &bWoodland Mansion&r or one of the great &bWhen Dungeons Arise&r sites (Foundry, Bandit Towers, Keep Kayra, Infested Temple, Plague Asylum or Shiraz Palace). Bring 4 &6Filled Maps&r and 2 &6Photographs&r."
		"Cartographer villagers sell &6Woodland Explorer Maps&r that lead to one of these sites. When Dungeons Arise sites are off the Explorer's Compass list."
		"&eTip:&r they stand far from spawn, so take an airship."
	]
	quest.6575B36D502BB123.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Cartographers' Society"
	quest.6575B36D502BB123.title: "Landmark Survey"
	quest.657FCF657B8C20BE.quest_desc: [
		"The &bWooden Brewingstation&r (a furnace, a cauldron, iron and planks) sets up a small brewery with a kettle, oven, timer and whistle."
		"Beers take &6Hops&r, &6Yeast&r and a dried grain; whiskeys take dried grains and yeast. Wild hops grow in taigas, and yeast cooks in a Farm \\& Charm pot from sugar, wheat and a water bottle."
		"While it brews, the kettle, oven, timer and whistle act up. Sort each one out to raise the brew's quality."
		"&7Brewery's drinks come with real intoxication. Pace yourself.&r"
		"Place a Wooden Brewingstation."
	]
	quest.657FCF657B8C20BE.quest_subtitle: "Beer and whiskey from the silo"
	quest.657FCF657B8C20BE.title: "First Sip"
	quest.65A73EF3DD75AA23.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Kitchens, cellars and docks all post their orders here.\"&r"
		""
		"Seven clients buy food and drink for the colony: Greenhollow Co-op (produce and dairy), Hearthstone Bakery, The Copper Kettle (stews and ales), Old Vine Cellars (wine), Lantern Row Tea House, Harbor Kitchens (fish) and The Mess Hall (rations)."
		"Tier I to III orders reset &bdaily&r and Tier IV orders &bweekly&r. Each tier opens with your team's progress, and its gate shows what it waits on."
		"Every order uses up the goods it asks for. Every teammate claims their own XP and coins; the &6Contract Seals&r are paid once per team."
		"&eTip:&r the Kitchen \\& Cellar chapter teaches the cooking, baking and brewing used here."
	]
	quest.65A73EF3DD75AA23.quest_subtitle: "Seven clients, one hungry colony"
	quest.65A73EF3DD75AA23.title: "The Provisions Board"
	quest.661C8B021E138E76.quest_desc: [
		"An &6ME Terminal&r on a cable shows everything the network holds. Craft it with a crafting table and a &6Calculation Processor&r into a &6Crafting Terminal&r."
		"Its grid refills from storage, so shift-clicking the output can craft far more than you meant."
		"Mount terminals facing you with the cable behind them; a backwards terminal isn't connected."
		"&cTeam rule:&r ME terminals and wireless access points go inside your team's claim, at least 6 blocks from its edge."
	]
	quest.661C8B021E138E76.quest_subtitle: "Craft straight from storage"
	quest.661C8B021E138E76.title: "A (Much) Bigger Table"
	quest.6656E293E15E46C0.quest_desc: [
		"The top shelf: whiskey, a wine-paired dinner, tea and coffee, ocean fishing and rations for Nether patrols."
		"Ocean fishing also waits on Main Street's Town Charter, and the Nether rations on Return to the Nether. Orders still reset &bdaily&r."
	]
	quest.6656E293E15E46C0.quest_subtitle: "Opens with Steel Backbone"
	quest.6656E293E15E46C0.title: "Tier III Orders"
	quest.66C0759130C96C7F.quest_desc: [
		"&7Hell and sea, gems and sigils. Time to put it all together.&r"
		""
		"Enchant any item at &blevel 60&r on an enchanting table ringed with your own shelves."
		"It takes World Tier &bAscent&r, which lifts your Eterna cap to 60, and shelves that reach that high: plain Hellshelves and Seashelves stop at 45."
		"&6Infuse&r a Hellshelf or Seashelf by enchanting it in the table once the table's stats meet the infusion recipe (EMI shows the targets). Infused shelves reach 60."
	]
	quest.66C0759130C96C7F.quest_subtitle: "Level 60, on your own shelves"
	quest.66C0759130C96C7F.title: "Arms Master"
	quest.66F5264BC563FE64.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The work crews come in cold and hungry. Stew, and plenty of it.\"&r"
		"8 bowls of &6Beef Stew&r."
		"Cook &6Raw Beef&r, a &6Carrot&r and a &6Potato&r in a Farmer's Delight &bCooking Pot&r set over heat, such as a &bStove&r or a campfire, and serve it into &6Bowls&r."
		"&eTip:&r a cow pen and a carrot and potato patch keep this order going all week."
	]
	quest.66F5264BC563FE64.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from The Copper Kettle"
	quest.66F5264BC563FE64.title: "Hearty Meals"
	quest.670376D4CAF1D557.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Launch day drains the whole grid. Fill our reserve banks first.\"&r"
		"A bulk order: deliver 50,000,000 FE. &cOnly a Task Screen accepts energy:&r set one to this order and cable your power plant into it."
		"It takes up to 100,000 FE per tick. A reactor and turbine fill it quickly; a smaller grid gets there over an evening."
	]
	quest.670376D4CAF1D557.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Voltaic Grid Authority"
	quest.670376D4CAF1D557.title: "Charge the Reserve Banks"
	quest.6732D4A49F32F47B.quest_desc: [
		"Set the destination to &bEarth Orbit&r and fly up to start an orbital station."
		"Bring building blocks: there is nothing to stand on up there."
		"&7The view of home alone is worth the fuel.&r"
	]
	quest.6732D4A49F32F47B.quest_subtitle: "A station above the world"
	quest.6732D4A49F32F47B.title: "High Orbit"
	quest.6737712F566E2896.quest_desc: [
		"&7Smoke from the chimney, iron in your pack and a pot on the stove.&r"
		""
		"Shelter, iron, a kitchen and a food journal: you've made it through landfall."
		"This opens the &6Andesite Age&r, &bTrailblazers&r, &bBosses \\& Tiers&r, &aKitchen \\& Cellar&r, &aMain Street&r, &aArms \\& Armor&r and the &5Contracts&r board."
		"&eTip:&r the daily T1 contracts on that board turn spare produce and meals into coins."
	]
	quest.6737712F566E2896.quest_subtitle: "You have landed"
	quest.6737712F566E2896.title: "Roots Down"
	quest.6760E1F97E35B7C6.quest_desc: [
		"Regeneration, Absorption, Resistance and Fire Resistance in one bite. Save it for a boss."
		"Restocks weekly."
	]
	quest.6760E1F97E35B7C6.quest_subtitle: "35 seals"
	quest.6760E1F97E35B7C6.title: "Enchanted Golden Apple"
	quest.679D66E054F60E90.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Interplanetary Navigator&r is mechanical-crafted from a Targeting Computer, a Circuit, &6Polished Lunar Sapphire&r and titanium."
		"Longer trips such as Mars need one aboard the rocket."
		"&7This also opens the weekly lunar contracts.&r"
		"&eNext:&r Red Planet."
	]
	quest.679D66E054F60E90.quest_subtitle: "Next stop: Mars"
	quest.679D66E054F60E90.title: "Lunar Program"
	quest.67BDCA8A86D8F072.quest_desc: [
		"Develop the exposed roll by crafting it with a &6Water Bottle&r (black and white) or with Awkward, Thick and Mundane potions (color). A Create Spout line can develop film too."
		"Load the developed film, &6Paper&r and dyes into a &bLightroom&r (an iron trapdoor, planks and a redstone torch), pick a frame and press &bPrint&r. Black and white needs black dye; color needs cyan, magenta, yellow and black."
		"Hang prints in a &6Photograph Frame&r (1x1 up to 3x3) or collect them in a &6Photo Album&r."
		"Print a photograph."
	]
	quest.67BDCA8A86D8F072.quest_subtitle: "Develop, print, frame"
	quest.67BDCA8A86D8F072.title: "A Moment in Time"
	quest.67DDF3F9A8BC894D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Endless Gateway of Apothic Invaders&r never runs out of waves, and each one hits harder than the last."
		"Survive to wave 100 and it pays out a &6Sigil of Supremacy&r, which overcharges every affix on an affix item."
		"&eTip:&r bring the whole team, plenty of healing and your best Apotheosis gear."
	]
	quest.67DDF3F9A8BC894D.quest_subtitle: "Wave 100 and beyond"
	quest.67DDF3F9A8BC894D.title: "Supremacy!"
	quest.683E4FBCB449C94B.quest_desc: [
		"&bYUNG's Better Desert Temples&r turns desert pyramids into deep temples full of traps and restless dead."
		"The &6Pharaoh&r waits in the burial chamber. Slay him to clear the temple."
		"&cMind the traps.&r Bring food, armour and a way back up."
	]
	quest.683E4FBCB449C94B.quest_subtitle: "A Pharaoh's tomb in the sand"
	quest.683E4FBCB449C94B.title: "Eternal Slumber"
	quest.684B219DCFEF822D.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Rocket Combustion Chamber&r from a Hardened Precision Mechanism, a &6Propeller&r, an &6Oxygen Separator&r and &6Titanium Sheets&r."
		"The &6Oxygen Separator&r is an &6Electron Tube&r, Iron Sheets and a &6Fluid Pipe&r. Your air gear needs more of them later."
	]
	quest.684B219DCFEF822D.quest_subtitle: "Where fuel becomes thrust"
	quest.684B219DCFEF822D.title: "Combustion Chamber"
	quest.685BEADD01251991.quest_desc: [
		"Build a sealed Martian habitat: two &6Oxygen Sealers&r for the rooms and Northstar &6Solar Panels&r to power it."
		"Each panel is mechanical-crafted from a Circuit, &6Tinted Glass&r, a shaft and titanium."
		"&eTip:&r the Electrolysis Machine's oxygen keeps the sealers running, and Large Fans stretch each one's reach."
	]
	quest.685BEADD01251991.quest_subtitle: "A sealed home on Mars"
	quest.685BEADD01251991.title: "Found a Colony"
	quest.686698F3D5642A2A.quest_desc: [
		"The &bFerrous Wroughtnaut&r waits in a &bWrought Chamber&r somewhere underground."
		"Its armour turns aside blows from the front. Dodge its big axe swing, then strike its back while it recovers."
		"&eTip:&r it heals when left alone and resets if someone respawns nearby, so finish the fight in one go."
		"Beating it unlocks Frontier on its own, no Twilight trip needed."
		"Its prizes are the &6Axe of a Thousand Metals&r and the &6Wrought Helm&r."
	]
	quest.686698F3D5642A2A.quest_subtitle: "Mowzie's Ferrous Wroughtnaut"
	quest.686698F3D5642A2A.title: "Just a Flesh Wound"
	quest.6867EBFBC94C2660.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The taproom's dry and the regulars are getting loud. Refill us.\"&r"
		"8 &6Beer&r and 8 &6Mead&r, poured into Tankards."
		"Both ferment in a Brewin' and Chewin' &bKeg&r: Beer from a bucket of water, wheat, wheat seeds and a brown mushroom; Mead from four Honey Bottles, wheat, wheat seeds and sweet berries."
		"A batch takes about eight minutes and pours four tankards."
		"&eTip:&r run two kegs side by side, one for each drink."
	]
	quest.6867EBFBC94C2660.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from The Copper Kettle"
	quest.6867EBFBC94C2660.title: "Ale and Mead"
	quest.6894CCC61B85B936.quest_desc: [
		"Candlelight is Let's Do at its fanciest: copper &bCooking Pans&r and &bPots&r for the stove, plus plates, wine glasses, napkins and cloches to set a proper table."
		"The &6Beef Wellington&r bakes in the Farm \\& Charm &bStove&r from &6Lamb Ham&r (mutton through the Mincer), &6Dough&r and Candlelight's &6Mushroom Soup&r."
		"The soup cooks in a pot from mushrooms, butter, milk and a bottle of red wine. Any potion bottle works in place of the wine."
		"Cook a Beef Wellington and set it down on the table."
	]
	quest.6894CCC61B85B936.quest_subtitle: "Candlelight fine dining"
	quest.6894CCC61B85B936.title: "Dish Fit for a Duke"
	quest.68A91D4E5193B315.quest_desc: [
		"Create: Let The Adventure Begin scatters old Create builds across the land: crumbling ruins, big windmills, quarries and oil rigs."
		"Their chests hold &6Andesite Alloy&r and &6Zinc&r, and now and then something rarer. A good head start on the Andesite Age."
		"Find one of the ruins and step inside."
	]
	quest.68A91D4E5193B315.quest_subtitle: "Someone built with Create before you"
	quest.68A91D4E5193B315.title: "Old Engineers' Ruins"
	quest.68D80BD4A9C9AA73.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Mechanical Press&r (andesite casing, an iron block and a shaft) flattens ingots into sheets on a &6Depot&r or a passing belt."
		"&6Iron Sheets&r go into nearly everything from here on. Gold, copper and later brass press into sheets the same way."
	]
	quest.68D80BD4A9C9AA73.quest_subtitle: "Sheets by the stack"
	quest.68D80BD4A9C9AA73.title: "Bonk!"
	quest.6900B76E5DA9E492.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Atmospheric Concentrator&r collects oxygen from the air. Mekanism oxygen works too."
		"Pump that oxygen into an &6Oxygen Filler&r and it fills your suit."
		"The Concentrator is mechanical-crafted from an Oxygen Separator, a Circuit, a Fluid Tank, a Propeller, a shaft, titanium and wool. The Filler is a plain craft: a Circuit, an Oxygen Separator, and iron and titanium sheets."
	]
	quest.6900B76E5DA9E492.quest_subtitle: "Oxygen on tap"
	quest.6900B76E5DA9E492.title: "Fill 'er Up"
	quest.69383BD15E290C32.quest_desc: [
		"Set a &bBasin&r on a fuelled &bBlaze Burner&r and put a powered &bMechanical Mixer&r above the basin."
		"Add &6Copper Ingots&r and &6Zinc Ingots&r: each pair mixes into two &6Brass Ingots&r. Without heat, the mix won't start."
		"&eTip:&r keep the burner fed. When its fuel runs out, the mixing stops."
	]
	quest.69383BD15E290C32.quest_subtitle: "Copper, zinc and heat"
	quest.69383BD15E290C32.title: "Real Alloys"
	quest.6960DF48DE0C7CEF.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Portable Stock Ticker&r (clipboard, redstone link, stock ticker, andesite casing) and sneak-click your Stock Link or Stock Ticker to bind it."
		"Use it anywhere to open a Stock Keeper menu for your network. Address the order to your own name, and a &bRobo Bee Port&r with bees beside your packagers flies it to you. It also avoids the slot-9 kick, which makes it the pack's recommended way to order."
		""
		"&7Trains now run between your bases, and packages between your factories.&r"
		"This unlocks the Track Crew contract on the Contract Board, and later the Automation chapter's Train Dispatcher."
	]
	quest.6960DF48DE0C7CEF.quest_subtitle: "Trains between bases, packages between factories"
	quest.6960DF48DE0C7CEF.title: "Rails \\& Parcels"
	quest.69A39718E2425AFB.quest_desc: [
		"&6Levitite&r keeps a ship afloat without balloons."
		"Crush &6End Stone&r into &6End Stone Powder&r, then mix it with &6Zinc Nuggets&r and water in a heated &bMechanical Mixer&r to make &6Levitite Blend&r."
		"Heat the blend to crystallize it into Levitite. EMI shows the details."
		"&7End Stone means the End, which opens at Summit.&r"
	]
	quest.69A39718E2425AFB.quest_subtitle: "Levitite, from the End"
	quest.69A39718E2425AFB.title: "Unidentified Floating Object"
	quest.6A01311E65CA22E7.quest_desc: [
		"&7Every contract pays in seals. This is where the Guild takes them back.&r"
		""
		"Each offer here is a &brequisition&r, a purchase you can repeat. Open it and click its seal task to pay: the seals are used up and the goods are ready to claim. Seals you hand in stay counted, so you can pay for a big item over several visits."
		"Shelves open with your &bContractor Rank&r, bought with seals in the Guild Hall. The Registered shelf is open to everyone."
		"Some goods also wait on your team's progress, such as Foundry Crates after Steel Backbone. A locked offer shows the quest it needs."
		"Most offers restock at once; the rarest restock weekly. Each purchase is claimed once per team, so agree who collects."
		"&7The Exchange never sells machines, coins or anything that would skip a chapter.&r"
	]
	quest.6A01311E65CA22E7.quest_subtitle: "Where Contract Seals are spent"
	quest.6A01311E65CA22E7.title: "The Guild Exchange"
	quest.6A15EC62D533901F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Astronomy Table&r adds your readings to a &6Space Atlas&r."
		"Build it from &6Paper&r, an &6Iron Ingot&r, &6Stripped Logs&r and &6Wooden Slabs&r."
		"&eTip:&r keep a chest of readings beside it. You'll need plenty."
	]
	quest.6A15EC62D533901F.quest_subtitle: "A desk for your star maps"
	quest.6A15EC62D533901F.title: "Charting the Heavens"
	quest.6A25081BBA7048D9.quest_desc: [
		"Your backpack becomes indestructible, and a dropped one can't despawn or fall into the void."
		"Opens at World Tier &bSummit&r. Restocks weekly."
	]
	quest.6A25081BBA7048D9.quest_subtitle: "60 seals"
	quest.6A25081BBA7048D9.title: "Everlasting Upgrade"
	quest.6A7376D9F74AA7DD.quest_desc: [
		"Workshop and homestead stock: Bottles o' Enchanting, Warp Scrolls, the Chef's Basket and Workshop Crates."
		"&7Opens when your team holds the Journeyman rank.&r"
	]
	quest.6A7376D9F74AA7DD.quest_subtitle: "Opens at Journeyman rank"
	quest.6A7376D9F74AA7DD.title: "Journeyman Shelf"
	quest.6ACCAFB23C03D6E3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Nether Quartz Ore&r is common all through the Nether's netherrack. Mine a good stack and bring it home."
		"Charged with redstone, quartz becomes &6Rose Quartz&r, and rose quartz becomes the &6Electron Tubes&r every brass machine needs."
		"&eTip:&r a Fortune pickaxe makes this trip much shorter."
	]
	quest.6ACCAFB23C03D6E3.quest_subtitle: "White crystals in red rock"
	quest.6ACCAFB23C03D6E3.title: "Quartz Run"
	quest.6AED0D0ABE33B68E.quest_desc: [
		"Airship work starts once your Steel \\& Sparks backbone is built."
		"Create Aeronautics ships fly on propellers. An &6Andesite Propeller&r (a Create propeller, a shaft and wooden slabs) pushes air when it is placed and powered with rotation."
		"A &6Propeller Bearing&r spins attached sails as one big propeller and pushes harder."
	]
	quest.6AED0D0ABE33B68E.quest_subtitle: "Propellers push the air"
	quest.6AED0D0ABE33B68E.title: "For Every Action..."
	quest.6BF4CB462B10595C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Dimensional Drive&r has a Starwright recipe that needs Martian steel. Look it up in EMI."
		"Place it on an Aeronautics ship, right-click it to pick a planet, arm it, then climb to the trigger altitude (around Y 1750) to jump."
		"&cProtect the ship first:&r Sable ships need the Contraption Claim Block."
		"&eTip:&r stock the ship with air, fuel and a spare suit before you climb."
	]
	quest.6BF4CB462B10595C.quest_subtitle: "An airship that leaves the planet"
	quest.6BF4CB462B10595C.title: "Dimensional Drive"
	quest.6C4D0D804D2A5915.quest_desc: [
		"A Brewin' and Chewin' &bKeg&r (planks, iron and honeycomb) ferments a base liquid with up to four ingredients. Bases are water, milk, honey or a drink you made earlier."
		"Start with &6Beer&r: water, wheat, wheat seeds and a brown mushroom. Each batch pours out into four &6Tankards&r."
		"Some recipes need a set temperature, from Cold to Hot. Heat such as a campfire or a &bHeating Cask&r warms the keg; ice or an &bIce Crate&r cools it."
		"Cheese wheels ferment from milk and ripen once placed."
		"Ferment any drink and pour a serving."
	]
	quest.6C4D0D804D2A5915.quest_subtitle: "Kegs, drinks and cheese"
	quest.6C4D0D804D2A5915.title: "Acquired Taste"
	quest.6C55FE14AD94C256.quest_desc: [
		"Combine &6Engineer's Goggles&r with &6Leather&r to make &6Aviator's Goggles&r."
		"Engineer's Goggles are glass, a golden sheet and string."
		"&7Every crew needs a pair, whether or not the plane has a roof.&r"
	]
	quest.6C55FE14AD94C256.quest_subtitle: "Every crew needs goggles"
	quest.6C55FE14AD94C256.title: "High Fashion"
	quest.6C929F1AF3424A94.quest_desc: [
		"Each piece is the matching iron armor plus &6Iron Sheets&r: &6Tinted Glass&r for the helmet and &6Durable Fabric&r (string and wool) for the rest."
		"The chestplate is built around a &6Copper Backtank&r and holds your air."
		"&cSpace has no air.&r Wear all four pieces and keep the tank full."
	]
	quest.6C929F1AF3424A94.quest_subtitle: "Iron, glass and a backtank"
	quest.6C929F1AF3424A94.title: "Suit Up"
	quest.6CA5D2DEAC499E96.quest_desc: [
		"The Undergarden has its own ores. &6Cloggrum&r is common in depthrock, &6Froststeel&r sits in icy &bshiverstone&r, and rare &6Regalium&r crystals are worth a detour."
		"&6Utherium&r ore gives &6Utheric Clusters&r. Purify them into &6Utherium Crystals&r in an &bInfuser&r (dreadrock, rogdorium and a cluster), fuelled with &6Rogdorium&r mined from dreadrock."
		"&cUtheric Infection:&r the Undergarden can infect you. Eating &6Rogdorium&r or the &bPurity&r effect holds it back."
		"&eTip:&r utherium weapons deal 1.5x damage to Rotspawn."
	]
	quest.6CA5D2DEAC499E96.quest_subtitle: "Metals of the Undergarden"
	quest.6CA5D2DEAC499E96.title: "Deep Extraction"
	quest.6D148B08207774CC.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The Moon base runs on what you fly up. Fly up a lot.\"&r"
		"256 &6Titanium Ingots&r, 64 &6Polished Lunar Sapphire&r and 64,000 mB of rocket-grade &6Biofuel&r."
		"Titanium is smelted from the Moon's &6Raw Titanium&r. Biofuel is pressed from dried kelp and bone meal in a heated &bMechanical Press&r and basin; hand it in from tanks, or pipe it into a Task Screen."
	]
	quest.6D148B08207774CC.quest_subtitle: "Monthly Grand Contract from the Lunar Survey Corps"
	quest.6D148B08207774CC.title: "Lunar Supply Run"
	quest.6DA8470A7DD99A43.quest_desc: [
		"With the workshop turning, the colony wants finer goods: butter and cheese, baskets of bread, ale and mead, house wine and tea."
		"These lean on the Let's Do mods and Brewin' and Chewin'. Orders still reset &bdaily&r."
	]
	quest.6DA8470A7DD99A43.quest_subtitle: "Opens with Andesite Works"
	quest.6DA8470A7DD99A43.title: "Tier II Orders"
	quest.6E2A2AAA35DC2527.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"For once, all four of us agree: one expedition, every world, and an album to show for it.\"&r"
		""
		"The Cartographers' Society, the Lantern Museum, the Field Survey Office and The Gazette pool their funds for one great survey."
		"Visit every place on the list: five far corners of the Overworld, and one landmark biome each in the Nether, the Twilight Forest, the Undergarden, Eternal Starlight, the Otherside and the outer End."
		"Bring home a &6Photo Album&r of the journey (a Book and Quill with a Phantom Membrane)."
		"&eTip:&r Traveler's Titles names each biome as you arrive, so you'll know when you're there."
	]
	quest.6E2A2AAA35DC2527.quest_subtitle: "Signature order from all four clients"
	quest.6E2A2AAA35DC2527.title: "The Grand Survey"
	quest.6EAC93958186E880.quest_desc: [
		"The &bLeviathan&r lurks in the &bSunken City&r under the ocean. An &6Eye of Abyss&r (an Eye of Ender, obsidian and crying obsidian) shows the way."
		"It sleeps until you bring an &6Abyssal Sacrifice&r, a costly offering (check EMI). Boss Checklist explains the rest."
		"&eTip:&r bring water breathing and a way to see underwater."
		"Its prizes include the &6Tidal Claws&r."
	]
	quest.6EAC93958186E880.quest_subtitle: "Cataclysm's Leviathan"
	quest.6EAC93958186E880.title: "Terror of the Deep"
	quest.6EBEA8AD067B2EBE.quest_desc: [
		"&bSimple Voice Chat&r is proximity voice. Press &bAlt + V&r for its menu, and make a group for your crew."
		"&bPing Wheel&r drops a marker your friends can see (set its key in Controls), and &bEmotecraft&r handles the waving."
		"&bTraveler's Titles&r shows a title card for every new biome and dimension, and &bLoot Beams&r colour dropped loot by rarity."
	]
	quest.6EBEA8AD067B2EBE.quest_subtitle: "Talk, ping and wave"
	quest.6EBEA8AD067B2EBE.title: "Voices on the Wind"
	quest.6F26193D1FD50CB1.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Seeking Eye&r (a Starlight Flower and an ender pearl) opens a star map. Pick a target and it floats beside you, pointing the way. Use it to find a &bGolem Forge&r."
		"The &bStarlight Golem&r never moves, and its shield can't be broken. Throw the forge's &6Frozen Tubes&r at it so it overheats sooner."
		"While it pauses to recharge, switch off the nearby &bEnergy Blocks&r. Its shield fails, and that's your opening."
		"It drops &6Oxidized Golem Steel Ingots&r, an &6Oxidized Alloy Furnace&r and often an &6Energy Sword&r."
	]
	quest.6F26193D1FD50CB1.quest_subtitle: "Shut down the Starlight Golem"
	quest.6F26193D1FD50CB1.title: "Ancient Wisdom"
	quest.6F4111E0A7AC1E98.quest_desc: [
		"One random pick: reinforced or atomic alloy, advanced control circuits, AE2 processors, glowstone torches, refined obsidian ingots, netherite scrap or diamonds."
		"Opens once your team completes the &6Lunar Program&r."
	]
	quest.6F4111E0A7AC1E98.quest_subtitle: "12 seals"
	quest.6F4111E0A7AC1E98.title: "Orbital Crate"
	quest.6F4FB65BF8398036.quest_desc: [
		"&7A bank, a shop, a studio and a pier. Main Street is open.&r"
		""
		"Build a proper street: shaped and chiseled fronts, a shop with stock, a photo on the wall, music playing and somewhere to fish. Then invite the crew over."
		"&eNext:&r the &bGuild’s&r contract boards turn goods into coins and seals, and your vendors turn coins back into goods."
	]
	quest.6F4FB65BF8398036.quest_subtitle: "A street worth visiting"
	quest.6F4FB65BF8398036.title: "Town Square"
	quest.6F6FEDE0C6166586.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our labs want lunar glowstone, engraved and ready to study.\"&r"
		"Mine &6Moon Glowstone Ore&r, found all over the Moon, for Raw Glowstone Ore. Fortune helps."
		"Process the raw ore in a &bCircuit Engraver&r, the machine your circuit line already uses, to make &6Enriched Glowstone Ore&r."
		"&eTip:&r with Silk Touch, Crushing Wheels get about 1.75 raw ore from each ore block."
	]
	quest.6F6FEDE0C6166586.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Lunar Survey Corps"
	quest.6F6FEDE0C6166586.title: "Lunar Glowstone Samples"
	quest.6F71C96EF6E39FF8.quest_desc: [
		"Known issues, and how to dodge them:"
		"- Keep a plain item, like a block, in hotbar slot 9 while a &6Stock Keeper&r screen is open (Create #9695)."
		"- Leave &6Sophisticated Storage&r barrel displays at their default rotation; rotated ones can crash a client."
		"- The Diesel Generators &6Bulk Fermenter&r is ground-only, and the &6Huge Diesel Engine&r is disabled."
		"- No &6Copycat Byte Panels&r in train floors that run over copycat blocks on the ground."
		"- Airships need a &6Contraption Claim Block&r; land claims don't cover them."
		"If the game crashes anyway, &bCrash Assistant&r uploads the log in one click. Send the link to whoever runs the server."
	]
	quest.6F71C96EF6E39FF8.quest_subtitle: "Five seconds that save a crash"
	quest.6F71C96EF6E39FF8.title: "Field Notes"
	quest.6FA40B0AC5C8DA23.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Alpha Yeti&r rules a cave in the &bSnowy Forest&r. Watch out for the ice bombs it throws."
		"Collect its &6Alpha Yeti Fur&r. It keeps you warm on the &bGlacier&r and makes a set of Yeti armour."
	]
	quest.6FA40B0AC5C8DA23.quest_subtitle: "The Yeti's cave"
	quest.6FA40B0AC5C8DA23.title: "Alpha Fur"
	quest.6FC4E037B82480B1.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The fishing boats won't go out until the shallows are safe.\"&r"
		"Kill 16 &bDrowned&r. They rise in rivers at night and lurk in the dark of oceans and ocean ruins."
		"Some carry a trident or a nautilus shell, and may drop it."
		"&eTip:&r keep spare &6Nautilus Shells&r. Much later, the Leviathan's sacrifice needs one."
	]
	quest.6FC4E037B82480B1.quest_subtitle: "Daily bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.6FC4E037B82480B1.title: "Tide Watch"
	quest.7006F996EC5D545B.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"A harbour in the clouds, and a fleet to use it.\"&r"
		"64,000 mB of &6Levitite Blend&r, 32 &6Andesite Propellers&r and 32 &6Hot Air Burners&r."
		"The blend is &6End Stone Powder&r, zinc nuggets and water in a heated &bMechanical Mixer&r. Hand it in from tanks in the quest screen, or pipe it into a Task Screen."
		"Propellers and burners are the Create Aeronautics crafts you already know from your flagship."
	]
	quest.7006F996EC5D545B.quest_subtitle: "Monthly Grand Contract from Skyward Freight"
	quest.7006F996EC5D545B.title: "Skyport Construction"
	quest.700E97FF6C7C076D.quest_desc: [
		"&7The brass works hum. Now teach them to make electricity.&r"
		""
		"The Crafts \\& Additions &6Alternator&r turns Create rotation into &bFE&r. It needs at least 32 RPM, and faster shafts make more power. It is Starwright's only bridge from rotation to FE; the &6Electric Motor&r goes the other way."
		"Build it on your &bMechanical Crafters&r. It needs &6Iron Rods&r and a &6Copper Spool&r, so first make a &bRolling Mill&r: drop ingots or plates on top and it rolls them into rods and wire."
		"&eTip:&r a Copper Spool links two &6Connectors&r when you right-click each one. Those wires carry FE to your machines."
	]
	quest.700E97FF6C7C076D.quest_subtitle: "Rotation becomes FE"
	quest.700E97FF6C7C076D.title: "First Spark"
	quest.70140716807F1C63.quest_desc: [
		"Bakery builds on Farm \\& Charm: &6Flour&r from the Mincer, doughs from the Crafting Bowl and the &bStove&r for breads, croissants, pies and tarts. Jams cook in a pot from fruit and sugar."
		"The &bCaking Station&r (bricks, wooden slabs and sugar) shapes sweets. Right-click it with &6Cake Dough&r (flour, sugar, an egg and milk), then top the cake with jam."
		"Before the jam goes on, a knife cuts the cake into cupcakes, and a &6Rolling Pin&r flattens cupcakes into cookies."
		"Placed cakes are for sharing: right-click with a knife to cut a slice, or sneak and right-click to eat."
		"Place a Caking Station."
	]
	quest.70140716807F1C63.quest_subtitle: "Breads, cakes and jams"
	quest.70140716807F1C63.title: "Bake It Happen"
	quest.707D13F65486E543.quest_desc: [
		"&7The first rung. The world starts fighting back.&r"
		""
		"The Wroughtnaut or the Twilight duo is down. Tick the box, then each of you claims the reward to unlock &bWorld Tier: Frontier&r, and switches to it in the World Tier screen (&bCtrl + T&r) when ready."
		"Mobs grow tougher, Apothic Invaders begin to roam, and affix loot improves."
		"&eFrontier opens:&r Eternal Starlight's Gatekeeper in Below and Beyond, and the next rung of this ladder."
	]
	quest.707D13F65486E543.quest_subtitle: "The wilds push back"
	quest.707D13F65486E543.title: "World Tier: Frontier"
	quest.70A3AF57B13715BF.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Lantern&r is a torch wrapped in iron nuggets."
		"Hold one and press &bAlt + L&r to hang it on your belt. It keeps lighting the way while your hands stay busy."
		"&7Later, a TorchMaster &6Mega Torch&r (a diamond, a gold block, logs and a torch) stops monsters spawning across a whole base.&r"
	]
	quest.70A3AF57B13715BF.quest_subtitle: "Hands-free light"
	quest.70A3AF57B13715BF.title: "Light the Way"
	quest.716BA67E547A7054.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Metallurgic Infuser&r (a furnace, iron, osmium and redstone) infuses metals with a second ingredient."
		"Load an infusion source, such as &6Coal&r for carbon or &6Redstone&r for redstone, plus the item to infuse, and give it FE."
		"It makes Mekanism's alloys and control circuits, and with two rounds of carbon it turns iron into steel dust."
		"&eTip:&r an &bEnrichment Chamber&r turns coal and redstone into enriched forms that hold far more infusion."
	]
	quest.716BA67E547A7054.quest_subtitle: "Infusing metals"
	quest.716BA67E547A7054.title: "A Metallur-what?"
	quest.719BA90BFC814701.quest_desc: [
		"The &bExcavator&r digs ore out of a mineral vein for a very long time. Build it over the best vein your samples found."
		"It has two parts, an engine and a bucket wheel, built from steel and Light and Heavy Engineering Blocks. The manual shows the layout; hit the engine's rear centre Heavy Engineering Block with the hammer."
		"It eats a lot of FE through the three plugs on its side, so bring an HV line or build generators on site."
		"&eTip:&r an outpost like this is perfect for a train line. Let a station carry the ore home."
	]
	quest.719BA90BFC814701.quest_subtitle: "An Excavator on a rich vein"
	quest.719BA90BFC814701.title: "Diggy Diggy Hole"
	quest.71D8917A7F476120.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Mushrooms that grow in fire! The botanists can hardly wait.\"&r"
		"Visit a &bCrimson Forest&r in the Nether and bring 8 &6Crimson Fungus&r, 8 &6Warped Fungus&r and 4 &6Shroomlight&r."
		"Warped fungus grows in the blue &bWarped Forests&r. Shroomlight glows among the caps of the huge fungus trees in both."
		"&eTip:&r Bone Meal on nylium sprouts fungi, and on a fungus planted on its own nylium it grows a huge one."
	]
	quest.71D8917A7F476120.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Field Survey Office"
	quest.71D8917A7F476120.title: "Fungi of the Nether"
	quest.71EC7611C4E6788F.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The colony has customers now, and customers have orders.\" - the Guild&r"
		""
		"The Guild posts &brepeatable contracts&r on five boards: &aProvisions&r, &6Industry&r, &bFrontier&r, &cBounties&r and the &dStar Charter&r. Hand in what an order asks for and your team is paid in XP, coins and &6Contract Seals&r."
		"Contracts come back after a &bcooldown&r: daily, weekly, or monthly for the Grand Contracts here. New tiers open as the team climbs the book."
		"Seals pay for &bContractor Ranks&r below and buy goods at the &eGuild Exchange&r. Each rank opens a new Exchange shelf and new Grand Contracts."
		"Coins are wages: every teammate claims their own, whoever did the work. Seals and loot crates are paid once per team, so keep the seals together for ranks."
	]
	quest.71EC7611C4E6788F.quest_subtitle: "Steady work for the whole colony"
	quest.71EC7611C4E6788F.title: "The Contractors' Guild"
	quest.71FC5E73B1127971.quest_desc: [
		"The &bObsidilith&r waits atop a giant obsidian structure floating in the End."
		"Place an &6Eye of Ender&r in its &bObsidian Altar&r to wake it."
		"It drops an &6Obsidian Heart&r."
	]
	quest.71FC5E73B1127971.quest_subtitle: "BoMD's Obsidilith"
	quest.71FC5E73B1127971.title: "Obsidian Obliterator"
	quest.71FDCEB066640900.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a &6stripped log&r or stripped wood with &6Andesite Alloy&r to turn it into &6Andesite Casing&r, the shell of most early machines."
		"Strip logs with an axe for now. A Mechanical Saw does it in bulk later in this chapter."
	]
	quest.71FDCEB066640900.quest_subtitle: "A shell for your machines"
	quest.71FDCEB066640900.title: "The Andesite Age"
	quest.7221460CA63FFCA9.quest_desc: [
		"Hold it in either hand and it saves you from one death."
		"Restocks weekly."
	]
	quest.7221460CA63FFCA9.quest_subtitle: "40 seals"
	quest.7221460CA63FFCA9.title: "Totem of Undying"
	quest.722892B2A5CC37E7.quest_desc: [
		"&bForgotten Guardians&r stand watch in some catacomb tunnels. Kill one yourself and it drops 4 to 16 &6Forgotten Nuggets&r."
		"Nine nuggets make a &6Forgotten Ingot&r. With a &6Forgotten Upgrade&r template, a smithing table turns cloggrum tools and weapons into Forgotten ones."
		"&eTip:&r the template comes from catacomb chests, so search the halls before you head home."
	]
	quest.722892B2A5CC37E7.quest_subtitle: "Slay a Forgotten Guardian"
	quest.722892B2A5CC37E7.title: "Decommissioned"
	quest.72D2F04617CFA7F0.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Our foundry turns tetrachloride into titanium and alloys. Venus has the rock for it.\"&r"
		"16,000 mB of &6Titanium Tetrachloride&r from a &bsuperheated&r Mixer: Rutile Concentrate, a zinc ingot and carbon gas, plus either chlorine gas or a Sodium Catalyst. EMI shows both recipes."
		"Crushing &6Venus Gravel&r gives the most &6Rutile Concentrate&r; limestone and sand give less."
		"Compact three coal over heat for carbon gas. An &bElectrolysis Machine&r splits brine into chlorine and sodium."
		"&eTip:&r pipe the mixer's output straight into a Task Screen."
	]
	quest.72D2F04617CFA7F0.quest_subtitle: "Weekly order from the Sunward Expedition"
	quest.72D2F04617CFA7F0.title: "Foundry Feed from Venus"
	quest.72FB1BD747DE0544.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Mechanical Bearing&r or &6Mechanical Piston&r moves every block glued to it. Hold a contraption together with &6Super Glue&r or &6Chassis&r."
		"Put drills, saws or harvesters on board and they work as they move: tree farms, quarries and crop harvesters."
		"Each part's Ponder scene shows a working setup."
	]
	quest.72FB1BD747DE0544.quest_subtitle: "Optional: machines that move"
	quest.72FB1BD747DE0544.title: "Moving with Purpose"
	quest.7301F0D1220EAEDE.quest_desc: [
		"&7Every engine starts with a handful of rock and metal.&r"
		""
		"&6Andesite Alloy&r is andesite plus iron or zinc nuggets in a crafting grid. Shafts, cogwheels, casings and almost every early machine start from it."
		"Hold &bW&r over any Create item to watch its &bPonder&r scene; it shows each machine better than words can."
		"&eTip:&r make a &6Wrench&r and &6Engineer's Goggles&r early. The next quests show how, even before you have a press."
	]
	quest.7301F0D1220EAEDE.quest_subtitle: "Create's most important resource"
	quest.7301F0D1220EAEDE.title: "Sturdier Rocks"
	quest.73984793B48600B5.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Something keeps getting into the henhouse. Eight legs, we think.\"&r"
		"Kill 24 &bSpiders&r. They spawn in the dark like other monsters and climb walls to reach you. Cave spiders don't count."
		"&eTip:&r the string makes bows, wool and fishing rods, and spider eyes go into fermented spider eyes for potions."
	]
	quest.73984793B48600B5.quest_subtitle: "Daily bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.73984793B48600B5.title: "Webs and Fangs"
	quest.740470BF79988FA0.quest_desc: [
		"&7Every guild keeps a wall of patrons. Yours has an empty space.&r"
		""
		"Hand in 300 &6Contract Seals&r. Seals you hand in stay counted, so take as many visits as you need."
		"The Guild names your team its patron. Each of you takes a &6Dragon Egg&r for the trophy room and a great deal of experience, and the team picks one keepsake from the &6Trophy Case&r."
		"&7Nothing here unlocks anything. It is simply the proudest thing a contractor can buy.&r"
	]
	quest.740470BF79988FA0.quest_subtitle: "Your name above the Exchange door"
	quest.740470BF79988FA0.title: "Patron of the Guild"
	quest.74173888E3122775.quest_desc: [
		"&7Venus burns and Mercury bakes. The MekaSuit is your way through.&r"
		""
		"&bMekanism x Create: Northstar&r adds &6Durasteel&r, an alloy made in the &bMetallurgic Infuser&r. EMI shows the base metal and the infusion type."
		"&eTip:&r an Infusing Factory makes quick work of a stack."
	]
	quest.74173888E3122775.quest_subtitle: "An alloy for hostile worlds"
	quest.74173888E3122775.title: "Durasteel"
	quest.741B1A8FE417B261.quest_desc: [
		"The &bEnder Guardian&r holds the &bRuined Citadel&r in the End. Follow an &6Eye of Void&r (an Eye of Ender, purpur, end stone bricks and a shulker shell) to find it."
		"It's one of the three keys to Pinnacle, with the Ender Dragon and a Mars landing."
		"Its prize is the &6Gauntlet of Guard&r."
	]
	quest.741B1A8FE417B261.quest_subtitle: "Cataclysm's Ender Guardian"
	quest.741B1A8FE417B261.title: "Wasn't That a Shulker?"
	quest.741C272E9A1C1EB8.quest_desc: [
		"Opens with &6Reactor Online&r. From here every order resets &bweekly&r and adds a roll of the &6Reactor Crate&r."
		"Lattice Data Exchange's orders also need &6The Network&r. The Voltaic Grid Authority's power order can only be filled through a &6Task Screen&r."
	]
	quest.741C272E9A1C1EB8.quest_subtitle: "Chemistry and computation, reset weekly"
	quest.741C272E9A1C1EB8.title: "Tier IV Orders"
	quest.7441777147AAED8D.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Dockhands eat with one hand and haul with the other. Rolls, please.\"&r"
		"12 &6Cod Rolls&r and 12 &6Salmon Rolls&r."
		"Catch &6Cod&r at sea and &6Salmon&r in rivers, then cut each fish into two slices on a &bCutting Board&r with a knife."
		"Two slices and a &6Cooked Rice&r (rice cooked in a Cooking Pot) craft two rolls."
		"&eTip:&r rice grows in shallow water, so a paddy by the pier keeps the whole order close to hand."
	]
	quest.7441777147AAED8D.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Harbor Kitchens"
	quest.7441777147AAED8D.title: "Rolls for the Pier"
	quest.74620465D076CCCC.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The sunken halls are all green stone and blue light. We'd like some of both.\"&r"
		"Step into an &bOcean Monument&r and bring 24 &6Prismarine Shards&r and 8 &6Prismarine Crystals&r."
		"&bGuardians&r drop both. YUNG's monuments are larger, with better rewards, and &bElder Guardians&r curse intruders with Mining Fatigue."
		"&eTip:&r Cartographer villagers sell &6Ocean Explorer Maps&r that lead to a monument. Pack water breathing."
	]
	quest.74620465D076CCCC.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Lantern Museum"
	quest.74620465D076CCCC.title: "Monument Salvage"
	quest.74ACB4A4862E08E6.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"A shipyard down the coast wants girders, and we want your steel.\"&r"
		"32 &6Steel Ingots&r. Iron in an IE &bBlast Furnace&r fired with coal coke turns into steel and leaves slag. Mekanism's steel counts too: Almost Unified makes every steel this one ingot."
		"&eTip:&r an &bImproved Blast Furnace&r with preheaters runs by itself and keeps up easily."
	]
	quest.74ACB4A4862E08E6.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Ironvale Foundry"
	quest.74ACB4A4862E08E6.title: "Steel Order"
	quest.74BF27BFDD3B55E7.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Shafts, casings, cogs: it all starts with alloy, and the yard is empty.\"&r"
		"128 &6Andesite Alloy&r. A &bMechanical Mixer&r over a &bBasin&r makes one from a block of andesite and an iron or zinc nugget, half what the crafting grid costs."
		"&eTip:&r an &bEncased Fan&r washing gravel through water turns up iron nuggets."
	]
	quest.74BF27BFDD3B55E7.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Andesite Mill \\& Co."
	quest.74BF27BFDD3B55E7.title: "Alloy by the Crate"
	quest.74EFCA365B4EA5A0.quest_desc: [
		"The full Exposure: Space catalogue: every cosmic object, studied."
		"The last few only turn up on rare nights, so keep a camera handy and check the sky often."
		"&eTip:&r the &6Sculk Telescopic Lens&r is the top lens: an Excellent lens upgraded with echo shard, sculk catalyst and netherite scrap."
	]
	quest.74EFCA365B4EA5A0.quest_subtitle: "Every object studied"
	quest.74EFCA365B4EA5A0.title: "Cartographer of the Void"
	quest.74F811DA624CA054.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The dairy's overflowing, and the market wants butter and cheese.\"&r"
		"16 &6Butter&r and 8 &6Flaxen Cheese Wedges&r."
		"Stir a Milk Bucket in Farm \\& Charm's &bCrafting Bowl&r for four Butter."
		"Cheese ferments in a &bKeg&r kept &bWarm&r by a heat source nearby: a bucket of milk, a brown mushroom, pumpkin seeds and sugar. Serve it from the keg with a &6Honeycomb&r for an unripe wheel, place it until it ripens, then cut four wedges from it with a knife."
		"&eTip:&r keep a few wheels ripening so the next order is half done."
	]
	quest.74F811DA624CA054.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from Greenhollow Co-op"
	quest.74F811DA624CA054.title: "Butter and Cheese"
	quest.7562F49C22905BF3.quest_desc: [
		"Crush obsidian into &6Powdered Obsidian&r with &bCrushing Wheels&r, then sequence it into a &6Sturdy Sheet&r: a &bSpout&r pours in 500 mB of lava and a &bPress&r flattens it twice."
		"Right-click a placed &6Brass Casing&r with a Sturdy Sheet to turn it into &6Train Casing&r, the shell of stations, controls, signals and train doors."
		""
		"&eTip:&r stockpile Sturdy Sheets. Train Schedules, the Banking Guide, the Contraption Claim Block and, much later, Northstar titanium all use them."
	]
	quest.7562F49C22905BF3.quest_subtitle: "Sturdy sheets and train casing"
	quest.7562F49C22905BF3.title: "The Locomotive Age"
	quest.75A844EC9DEECA0D.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Not every order needs a whole crew.\" - the Guild&r"
		""
		"Some &6Notice Boards&r around the colony are &bGuild Job Boards&r (an op marks them). Right-click one, or type &e/jobs&r anywhere, to see jobs picked for &byou alone&r: 3 dailies (new at 05:00), a bigger weekly job (new on Monday) and, once you prestige, a weekly &dPrestige Contract&r."
		"Jobs are &eDeliver&r (hand items in), &cBounty&r (kill mobs, sometimes in a set dimension or biome), &bScout&r (reach a dimension or biome) and &aBreed&r. Bounties, scouting and breeding count up as you play; then &b[Claim]&r at a board. Hand everything in within 8 blocks of a board. The pay is yours, not the team's."
		"&b[Tier up]&r buys bigger, better-paid jobs with coins, from tier I to V. At V, &d[Prestige]&r starts you over at I with higher pay for good. &7[Reroll]&r swaps a job you can't do for a quarter of its pay. Finish all 3 dailies on days in a row for a streak worth up to +50% pay."
		"&e/jobs top&r shows the leaderboard, and your tier shows next to your name in chat."
	]
	quest.75A844EC9DEECA0D.quest_subtitle: "Work picked for you alone"
	quest.75A844EC9DEECA0D.title: "Guild Job Boards"
	quest.7612DF8723C9B6A8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Storage Cells&r keep items inside an item. An &6ME Drive&r holds ten, and the whole network shares what's in them."
		"A cell is a &6Cell Housing&r plus a &6Storage Component&r. Each tier holds four times as much and costs three of the tier below."
		"An item cell holds up to 63 different items. AE2 also makes fluid cells, and Applied Mekanistics adds chemical cells for Mekanism gases."
		"&eTip:&r 4k cells are a good balance of space and item types to start with."
	]
	quest.7612DF8723C9B6A8.quest_subtitle: "Storage that searches itself"
	quest.7612DF8723C9B6A8.title: "Better Than Chests"
	quest.7645608427E8E53A.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Brush&r (a copper ingot, a stick and a feather) and sweep &6Suspicious Sand&r and &6Suspicious Gravel&r for buried finds."
		"Better Archeology adds dig sites with &6Suspicious Dirt&r and &6Fossiliferous Dirt&r, plus faster iron, diamond and netherite brushes."
		"&7The full dig, fossils and all, is in the Trailblazers chapter.&r"
	]
	quest.7645608427E8E53A.quest_subtitle: "Optional: dig sites and fossils"
	quest.7645608427E8E53A.title: "Brush Up"
	quest.775405C51A168941.quest_desc: [
		"&6Organic Compost&r is crafted from dirt, straw, bone meal and either rotten flesh or tree bark (logs on a cutting board). Place it and it slowly decays into &6Rich Soil&r."
		"It composts faster in sunlight, near water and next to mushrooms, mycelium, podzol or more compost."
		"Till Rich Soil with a hoe into &6Rich Soil Farmland&r for a crop growth boost. Mushrooms planted on Rich Soil grow into &6Mushroom Colonies&r."
		"&cStarwright quirk:&r keep a real water block near Rich Soil Farmland. Farm \\& Charm's Water Sprinkler doesn't count as water for it."
		"Pick up a block of Rich Soil to finish."
	]
	quest.775405C51A168941.quest_subtitle: "Compost becomes Rich Soil"
	quest.775405C51A168941.title: "Plant Food"
	quest.77599DE8D96496F2.quest_desc: [
		"Daily culls in the &bUndergarden&r, &bEternal Starlight&r, the &bOtherside&r and the Twilight Forest's &bSnowy Forest&r, each opening with its own way in."
		"Bastion Watch adds two weekly jobs: a &bGateway&r bounty, and the &bNetherite Monstrosity&r from World Tier Ascent."
		"&7Tier IV opens with Reactor Online.&r"
	]
	quest.77599DE8D96496F2.quest_subtitle: "Deeper dimensions, bigger game"
	quest.77599DE8D96496F2.title: "Tier III Bounties"
	quest.77625926F50DD190.quest_desc: [
		"Use a bucket while fishing to land a fish alive, then give it a home in an &6Aquarium&r (glass panes). Aquariums take decorations too."
		"A &6Display&r (planks and slabs) shows off a starcaught fish or your Starcatcher's Guide. Sign the guide first, so visitors see your collection and not their own."
		"&eTip:&r trophy fish bite as soon as all their conditions are met."
	]
	quest.77625926F50DD190.quest_subtitle: "Aquariums and displays"
	quest.77625926F50DD190.title: "Show It Off"
	quest.777C535C0DCBC1BD.quest_desc: [
		"The &bapex bounties&r: the &bEnder Dragon&r, the &bLeviathan&r, the &bHarbinger&r and &bScylla&r, with the &bEnder Guardian&r as a major."
		"Each one is a full team fight, and apex bounties pay a roll from the &6Trophy Case&r."
		"&7When you're ready, the Legend of the Lodge waits at the end of the row.&r"
	]
	quest.777C535C0DCBC1BD.quest_subtitle: "Apex game"
	quest.777C535C0DCBC1BD.title: "Tier V Bounties"
	quest.78258D7B343316B5.quest_desc: [
		"One random pick of &bStarcatcher&r gear: worms, lush, cherry or dripstone bait, a copper or shiny hook, or a clear or golden bobber."
		"Sometimes it is only string or a few cod."
	]
	quest.78258D7B343316B5.quest_subtitle: "5 seals"
	quest.78258D7B343316B5.title: "Angler's Tackle Box"
	quest.784A6F03E6EDAAB2.quest_desc: [
		"A part is a template plus materials: a pickaxe template and three iron ingots make a Pickaxe Head. Put a head and a &6Tool Rod&r together in a crafting grid to finish the tool."
		"Mix materials freely. Each one adds its own stats and traits, and the tooltip shows the result. Bindings, grips and coatings add more."
		"&eTip:&r a vanilla tool or armor piece converts into its Silent Gear version in a crafting grid."
		"Make a Silent Gear pickaxe, shovel and axe."
	]
	quest.784A6F03E6EDAAB2.quest_subtitle: "Head, rod, done"
	quest.784A6F03E6EDAAB2.title: "Standard Tools"
	quest.78816A21C44989C1.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"Settlers are signing up. Build them something to land in.\"&r"
		"256 &6Martian Steel Ingots&r, 128 &6Martian Strawberries&r and 16 &6Solar Panels&r."
		"Martian steel comes from Mars's own iron, as you learned on the Red Planet; the strawberries grow there too."
	]
	quest.78816A21C44989C1.quest_subtitle: "Monthly Grand Contract from the Ares Mining Consortium"
	quest.78816A21C44989C1.title: "The Colony Ship"
	quest.78F78146255CF119.quest_desc: [
		"Five &bdaily&r orders that need little more than a farm, a &bCooking Pot&r and a &bCutting Board&r: produce, stew, pies, fish rolls and packed lunches."
		"A locked order shows the quest it still waits on."
	]
	quest.78F78146255CF119.quest_subtitle: "Daily orders, open from the start"
	quest.78F78146255CF119.title: "Tier I Orders"
	quest.78F7D96803013A98.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Stove&r (bricks, a campfire and iron) heats whatever sits on top of it: a &6Cooking Pot&r or a &6Skillet&r."
		"The &6Cooking Pot&r (iron, a brick, a wooden shovel and a water bucket) cooks soups, stews and meals from several ingredients at once."
		"Set an ingredient on a &6Cutting Board&r (planks and sticks), then use it with a knife or the right tool in hand to break it down."
		"&eSeveral food mods add a stove and a cooking pot. This quest wants the Farmer's Delight ones; EMI tooltips show which mod an item is from.&r"
	]
	quest.78F7D96803013A98.quest_subtitle: "A Farmer's Delight kitchen"
	quest.78F7D96803013A98.title: "Fire Up the Stove"
	quest.797F928DB6BA2199.quest_desc: [
		"Spare wings for when a pair wears thin, or for a friend who missed the End ships. &6Phantom Membranes&r repair them at an anvil."
		"Opens once your team has freed the End. Restocks weekly."
	]
	quest.797F928DB6BA2199.quest_subtitle: "60 seals"
	quest.797F928DB6BA2199.title: "Elytra"
	quest.79E1CF64468A68EE.quest_desc: [
		"Now wake it. The &bWarden&r is blind but hunts by sound and smell, and it has a huge health pool."
		"&cIts sonic boom ignores armour and shields.&r Bring ranged weapons, healing and an escape route, or fight it as a team."
		"It drops the &6Heart of the Deep&r. Keep it safe: the heart opens the Otherside."
		"&eTip:&r the heart also crafts a &6Sonorous Staff&r, so light your portal first."
	]
	quest.79E1CF64468A68EE.quest_subtitle: "Slay the Warden"
	quest.79E1CF64468A68EE.title: "Phantom Thief"
	quest.7A81C7B752F16373.quest_desc: [
		"A &bWooden Silo&r (planks) slowly dries whatever you load into it. Right-click one with &6Bone Meal&r to start."
		"Barley, oats, wheat and corn dry into the grains the Brewery brews with."
		"Bone meal and rotten flesh dry into &6Fertilizer&r, which feeds several nearby crops in one use. Podzol dries into &6Fertilized Soil&r; feed it compost with a &6Pitchfork&r to boost growth around it."
		"Spare wild crops and produce dry into bone meal, so nothing goes to waste."
	]
	quest.7A81C7B752F16373.quest_subtitle: "Silos for grain and fertilizer"
	quest.7A81C7B752F16373.title: "The Art of Drying"
	quest.7AC55F2C9554A3B6.quest_desc: [
		"Build a Mekanism &6Teleporter&r (basic circuits, a Teleportation Core and a steel casing) and two more &6Teleportation Cores&r (ender pearls, atomic alloy, diamonds and gold) for the teleporters you'll set up off-world."
		"Finishing this quest unlocks planet travel for your team's Mekanism teleporters: they can now jump to and from the planets. It's a reward for the program, not a way around it."
		"&7Waystones and FTB teleports still refuse planets.&r"
		"&eNext:&r Inner Worlds."
	]
	quest.7AC55F2C9554A3B6.quest_subtitle: "Teleporters reach the planets"
	quest.7AC55F2C9554A3B6.title: "Interplanetary Network"
	quest.7B0B8AE1512EE746.quest_desc: [
		"&6Better Archeology&r adds dig sites: archeologist camps, buried ruins, tumuli and old temples."
		"Brush &6Fossiliferous Dirt&r to uncover fossil pieces. Join a fossil's skull and body into a full fossil; placed, some have effects, like the Wolf-Fossil that skeletons fear."
		"Better brushes dig faster. An &6Iron Brush&r is a feather, an iron ingot and a stick; diamond and netherite brushes follow."
	]
	quest.7B0B8AE1512EE746.quest_subtitle: "Brush the dirt, find the bones"
	quest.7B0B8AE1512EE746.title: "Ancient Treasure"
	quest.7B0DE722C00AC9B3.quest_desc: [
		"&7The top of the world, and a door that has stayed shut until now.&r"
		""
		"The Wither is dead and the Otherside is open. Tick the box and claim the reward to move your team to &bWorld Tier: Summit&r."
		"&eThe End opens:&r from now on, End portal frames accept your team's Eyes of Ender."
		"&7Summit also opens the weekly Wither and Warden bounties.&r"
	]
	quest.7B0DE722C00AC9B3.quest_subtitle: "The top, and a door to the End"
	quest.7B0DE722C00AC9B3.title: "World Tier: Summit"
	quest.7B22085A53A166BE.quest_desc: [
		"Mekanism multiblocks talk to computers through their ports. Wire a &6Fission Reactor Port&r to an Advanced Computer and the whole reactor becomes one peripheral."
		""
		"Loop every second: read the temperature, damage, coolant and waste levels (getTemperature(), getDamagePercent() and friends) and call &bscram()&r the moment one looks wrong."
		"Put the readings on a monitor so the whole crew can keep an eye on the reactor."
		"&cMeltdowns are on in this pack: once damage passes 100%, the reactor can explode and leave radiation behind."
		"&eSave the script as startup.lua so the watchdog restarts with the computer."
	]
	quest.7B22085A53A166BE.quest_subtitle: "A watchdog for the fission reactor"
	quest.7B22085A53A166BE.title: "SCRAM"
	quest.7BC41FBE69F09519.quest_desc: [
		"Simply Swords adds whole weapon families, from longswords and katanas to scythes, glaives, chakrams and greathammers. The iron versions are just iron and sticks."
		"Each type has its own Better Combat moveset, with different reach, speed and combos, so try a few."
		"Rare &6unique weapons&r with special powers turn up in loot. Read each one's tooltip."
		"Craft an Iron Longsword and an Iron Katana."
	]
	quest.7BC41FBE69F09519.quest_subtitle: "A weapon for every style"
	quest.7BC41FBE69F09519.title: "Blade Collector"
	quest.7C47CAACF2A592DB.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Starcatcher's Rod&r from a bobber, an iron hook, a stick and string, or upgrade a plain fishing rod with a hook, a bobber and string."
		"When something bites, a minigame starts: hit its key at the right moment to reel the fish in."
		"Fish depend on the biome, and some only bite in certain weather or at certain times of day. Hooks, bobbers and baits change the odds; worms come from bone-mealing farmland."
		"The &6Starcatcher's Guide&r (a rod and a book) tracks every catch."
	]
	quest.7C47CAACF2A592DB.quest_subtitle: "Starcatcher's fishing minigame"
	quest.7C47CAACF2A592DB.title: "Gone Fishing"
	quest.7D1A3320046D453A.quest_desc: [
		"&7The last rung, for teams that have been everywhere.&r"
		""
		"The Ender Dragon, the Ender Guardian and a Mars landing: you've conquered the End and stood on another planet."
		"Tick the box and claim the reward to move your team to &bWorld Tier: Pinnacle&r, the hardest tier with the best loot in the pack."
		"&eNext:&r Ascension's endless Gateways wait for Pinnacle teams."
	]
	quest.7D1A3320046D453A.quest_subtitle: "The hardest tier, the best loot"
	quest.7D1A3320046D453A.title: "World Tier: Pinnacle"
	quest.7DA36ABDE1A6CCE7.quest_desc: [
		"Create: Enchantment Industry keeps XP as &bliquid experience&r in tanks and pipes."
		"Craft a &6Fluid Hatch&r (Copper Ingot and Item Drain) and place it on a &bFluid Tank&r. Right-click it with a &6Block of Experience&r to turn it into an &6Experience Hatch&r."
		"Right-click the hatch to store your XP. Sneak and right-click to take it back."
		"Nine &6Nuggets of Experience&r make a block. Crushing Wheels drop them as a bonus when they crush ores."
		"&eNext:&r a &bMechanical Grindstone&r grinds experience items into liquid XP and polishes like sand paper. A &bBlaze Enchanter&r spends liquid XP to enchant."
	]
	quest.7DA36ABDE1A6CCE7.quest_subtitle: "Experience as a liquid"
	quest.7DA36ABDE1A6CCE7.title: "Spirit-Taking"
	quest.7DE28BDF04DE0529.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The mineral hall has two empty cases, one red and one blue.\"&r"
		"Visit the &bCrystallized Desert&r in Eternal Starlight and bring 16 &6Red Starlight Crystal Shards&r and 16 &6Blue Starlight Crystal Shards&r."
		"Crystal clusters stud the desert and its caves, and a pickaxe breaks each into 4 shards. &bCrystallized Moths&r there drop shards of both colours."
		"&eTip:&r the Starlight Portal opens with the Gatekeeper's Orb of Prophecy (Below and Beyond)."
	]
	quest.7DE28BDF04DE0529.quest_subtitle: "Daily order from the Lantern Museum"
	quest.7DE28BDF04DE0529.title: "Starlight Crystals"
	quest.7EDECCD0E26C2744.quest_desc: [
		"&cEnd portal frames refuse Eyes of Ender until your team reaches World Tier Summit.&r"
		"Throw Eyes of Ender to find a stronghold. &bYUNG's Better Strongholds&r turns the hunt for its portal room into a proper dungeon crawl."
		"Beyond lies &bNullscape&r's End: 384 blocks tall and truly alien, with &bMoog's End structures&r out on the far islands."
		"&6Ender's Delight&r cooks with chorus fruit and shulkers once you're there."
	]
	quest.7EDECCD0E26C2744.quest_subtitle: "The End opens at Summit"
	quest.7EDECCD0E26C2744.title: "Into the Void"
	quest.7F246124AB833EA3.quest_desc: [
		"Set the destination to &bMars Orbit&r: a spot for a second station."
		"Bring building blocks: there is nothing to stand on up there."
	]
	quest.7F246124AB833EA3.quest_subtitle: "A second station"
	quest.7F246124AB833EA3.title: "Red Orbit"
	quest.7F375E064ED54976.quest_desc: [
		"&7\"The old machine under the hills is humming again.\"&r"
		"Kill &bThe Harbinger&r in its &bAncient Factory&r deep underground. An &6Eye of Mech&r (an eye of ender, iron and a block of redstone) leads there."
		"The first time it sleeps until you use a &6Nether Star&r on it. After each defeat it leaves a &bBoss Respawner&r: use another Eye of Mech on it."
		"Its prize is a &6Block of Witherite&r."
	]
	quest.7F375E064ED54976.quest_subtitle: "Weekly bounty from The Wardens' Lodge"
	quest.7F375E064ED54976.title: "Bounty: The Harbinger"
	quest.7F8BEB56018E8A66.quest_desc: [
		"Copycats+ shapes take on the look of whatever block you right-click into them: slopes, stairs, beams, panels, slices, bytes, catwalks and more."
		"Most are cut from &6Zinc&r in a stonecutter, and two copycat slabs make a &6Copycat Block&r."
		"Use them for roof edges, window frames, ship hulls and anything else a full block is too blunt for."
		"&cKnown crash:&r don't put copycat byte panels on a train floor over ground copycats."
		"Make 8 Copycat Blocks."
	]
	quest.7F8BEB56018E8A66.quest_subtitle: "Any block, any shape"
	quest.7F8BEB56018E8A66.title: "Copycat Shapes"
	quest.7F9C3A90D09AFC75.quest_desc: [
		"&7Old ruins in the Overworld still guard a door to the stars.&r"
		""
		"&bPortal Ruins&r stand in the Overworld in common, forest, desert, jungle and cold versions, and a &bGatekeeper&r keeps watch at each one."
		"Talk to the Gatekeeper and choose &bChallenge&r. Win the duel and you get the &6Orb of Prophecy&r, usually with a &6Seeking Eye&r."
		"&eTip:&r once you've proven yourself, the Gatekeeper will also trade with you."
		"&7Opens at World Tier Frontier.&r"
	]
	quest.7F9C3A90D09AFC75.quest_subtitle: "The Gatekeeper's trial"
	quest.7F9C3A90D09AFC75.title: "Duke It Out"
	quest.7FD3467511665A5D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Engineer's Goggles&r (glass, a golden sheet and string) show a network's stress capacity and each machine's stress impact."
		"The &6Wrench&r (a golden sheet, a cogwheel and a stick) rotates kinetic blocks, and picks them up when you sneak."
		"No press yet? The Diesel Generators &6Hammer&r (a stick, andesite alloy and an iron ingot) flattens an ingot held in your offhand into a sheet."
		"&cIf machines need more stress than your sources supply, the whole network stops.&r Add sources or slow things down."
	]
	quest.7FD3467511665A5D.quest_subtitle: "Goggles on, wrench in hand"
	quest.7FD3467511665A5D.title: "Kitted Out"
